{"generated_at":"2026-09-23T15:06:36.316568Z","waves":[{"wave":{"id":"5081a624-c095-4218-9a54-6d1a6711f282","name":"product","status":"ready","goal":"Loopflow is the product for conducting goal-authored work across humans, agents, devices, and machines. The product is not one interface; it is the shared API and surfaces that make waves understandable and steerable wherever they run: CLI, Mac, iOS, agent turns, local workers, and remote compute.","repo":"/Users/jack/src/loopflow","active_tasks":1,"active_projects":2,"live":false,"paused":false,"enabled":false,"endpoint":null,"created_at":"2026-07-14T19:04:43Z","parent_wave_id":null,"retired_at":null,"superseded_by_wave_id":null,"retirement_reason":null,"home":{"id":"home_39860354aaca640c2ccb50bf6ca609d8","route":"local","created_at":"2026-07-19T14:56:05Z","observed_at":"2026-07-19T14:56:05Z"}},"metric_portfolio":{"metrics":[{"identity":{"wave_id":"5081a624-c095-4218-9a54-6d1a6711f282","metric_id":"task-loop-trust"},"contract_revision":"59a0f1df8f31e8c5c539c4ea7cd74c013a14ff053bee000c0942622cb8cdcddb","name":"Task loops earn trust","description":"Fraction of Tasks settled during the trailing seven days that either\ncompleted with every PR landed through Loopflow auto-merge or stopped with a\nnon-resumable failure receipt. Open Tasks are excluded. A user-landed PR or\nmanual Git repair inside the Task fails the metric.","project_id":"d19956b2-9955-437d-aea6-d91766231c77","stage":"installed","instrumented":false,"instrument":"lifecycle-scorecard","unit":"ratio","target":{"kind":"at_least","value":1.0},"window":"7d","freshness_policy":"30h","freshness":{"kind":"never"},"evidence":{"kind":"unknown","cause":{"kind":"never"}}}],"contract_issues":[]},"projects":{"state":"ok","items":[{"project":{"id":"57fee17f-7231-46f3-afd8-031d866a1779","slug":"desktop","name":"Desktop","summary":"Make the Mac desktop a dependable workspace for understanding human-selected Project/KR/Task intent and organizing the open Sessions that advance it. Build on provider-native continuation, retained panes, and explicit client transfer. Shared Loopflow APIs","definition":"Make the Mac desktop a dependable workspace for understanding human-selected Project/KR/Task intent and organizing the open Sessions that advance it. Build on provider-native continuation, retained panes, and explicit client transfer. Shared Loopflow APIs own planning, Work identity, legal actions, and human resolution; Desktop presents their evidence and preserves useful view state. Prove the promoted Ask handoff and truthful, responsive opening on the configured app, then join planning to Sessions for selected external work. Missing or stale evidence stays visible. Desktop owns user presentation, not a second transcript, evidence authority, runtime, or priority engine.","flows":{"first":null,"loop":null,"finally":null},"krs":[{"text":"Across ten recorded trials on human-selected work from Cube, Etude, Kata, or Hootro, one native workspace exposes current Project definitions, KR proof, and Task directives; round-trips at least one authorized Task-directive edit through the existing PM API; navigates between a Task and its exact open Sessions or an explicit no-Session state; and preserves useful panes and Work context. Shared Rust/Swift fixtures and twenty live Project, Task, and Session comparisons agree on identity, planning evidence, descriptive conditions, legal actions, and reasons. One real promoted Ask completes provider-native continuation, Ready, Complete, pane reconciliation, and blocked-caller release through the permissioned UI path. Desktop creates no second planning or Session authority.","holds":false},{"text":"Across fourteen consecutive days of real use, at least twenty repository opens show the correctly scoped Sessions list and true count within a published p95 budget, without an empty-then-populate flash or manual repair, and at least twenty Session selections reach verified interactive embedded terminals within a published p95 budget, with serial-open position retained. Twenty cold-launch and planning-navigation trials on the long-lived registry meet published paint and interaction budgets. Missing or stale evidence never appears as healthy emptiness; delayed or failed selections stay explicit, and terminated clients never remain displayed as live.","holds":false}]},"runtime":{"work_id":"proj_86f8af8b1e71ee288b167663c5f9e41b","status":"ready","reason":"ready","updated_at":"2026-07-23T04:04:24Z","iteration":4,"pending_observations":0,"provider":"codex","last_failure":{"message":"project runner failed: Project plan refresh blocked before the next phase: could not refresh wave/product from Linear: Stored linear token expired and automatic refresh failed: linear OAuth refresh failed: the token endpoint rejected or could not complete the request. Run `lf auth linear` once to reconnect.. Reconnect or run `lf pm sync --wave product`.. Project Work proj_86f8af8b1e71ee288b167663c5f9e41b did not continue on its stale plan; repair Linear planning, then restart it with `lf project run 57fee17f-7231-46f3-afd8-031d866a1779`","occurred_at":"2026-08-28T22:01:06Z"}},"next_move":{"owner":"project","reason":"ready"},"section":"now","tasks":[{"task":{"id":"ee671927-255f-41e6-8429-b830d59cc1de","identifier":"LOO-291","name":"Join current Project/KR/Task planning to native Sessions","description":"In the existing desktop workspace, show the selected repository's current Project definition and KR proof plus Task directive and condition from shared planning reads. Navigate between a Task and its existing open Sessions using stable shared identity; show an explicit no-Session state when none exists. Preserve retained panes, selection, and explicit Move here. Let the human edit the selected Task directive through the existing PM API and show the refreshed authoritative result. Identify planning freshness, unavailable reads, and rejected writes. Use the shared Session actions and display path from LOO-284; do not recreate a Session legality matrix or a labels-only roadmap query. Prove ten configured planning-to-Session trials on human-selected external work, including one authorized edit round trip, and publish scoped paint/interaction budgets with twenty long-lived-registry trials. Do not restore general fleet controls or infer priorities, execution success, or portfolio momentum.\n\n## Accepted chapter allocation — 2026-09-23\n\nChapter 20260923T000959Z-502f011b; review 2026-10-21T00:09:59.226362+00:00. Queued after LOO-251 and LOO-284 in the same serial Desktop slot. Activation also requires a named human-selected external proving workflow; do not infer one. LOO-280 is conditional only on the real configured LOO-251 proof being blocked by Xcode/Ghostty. No execution launch or publication occurs as part of creating this planning record.","rank":0,"completed":false,"assignee":null},"reference":{"issue_url":"https://linear.app/loopflow/issue/LOO-291/join-current-projectkrtask-planning-to-native-sessions","workspace":null},"runtime":null,"next_move":{"owner":"project","reason":"Task is ready to start"},"condition":{"state":"waiting","reason":"Task is ready to start","observed_at":"2026-09-23T15:06:37.210247Z","evidence_age_secs":null,"local_progress":{"state":"not_applicable","unsettled":false,"dirty":null,"authored_commits":null,"recovery_required":null,"reason":null}},"actions":{"recommended":null,"reason":"Task is ready to start"},"active_pr":null,"section":"available"},{"task":{"id":"9ed54c17-2b89-4bf9-b20d-0a95a1a65d44","identifier":"LOO-283","name":"Evaluate shared Warp and Loopflow viewing without terminal regressions","description":"Bounded investigation, not authorization to restore tmux presentation by default. Native provider launch plus explicit Move here is the current contract. Human direction on 2026-09-22: simultaneous viewing is desirable; the second attachment starts view-only and Take control explicitly transfers input. Previous tmux presentation distorted colors and caused terminal-specific bugs. History: 4d5e96383 shared raw resume argv, not one live PTY; 90c871805 removed tmux presentation; 7889d65bc consolidated native resume.\n\nCompare an opt-in tmux configuration and a transparent PTY relay using disposable Sessions in Warp and embedded Ghostty. Prove one provider PID and unsent draft survive late attachment, takeover, detach, and viewer close/crash; test truecolor, keyboard, image paste/drop with visible provider attachments, independently sized windows, scrollback and viewport behavior. Read-only must be enforced by the PTY owner. Record what app relaunch can recover separately from client-local selection/scroll position. Concurrent provider resumes are not a shared-PTY solution.\n\nTmux control mode would need a protocol/rendering client and does not provide Warp-native presentation automatically. Research reports Claude clipboard-image failures inside tmux (anthropics/claude-code#25672); retest on the exact stack rather than assume text file paths prove image attachment. A custom relay needs replay, flow control, resize, failure recovery, and durable PTY ownership. Remote Home attachment remains a separate scope decision. The existing Task tmux kill-on-close/quit policy must not be copied for durable human Sessions.\n\nDone when a dated comparison records reproducible passes/failures and an explicit recommendation or no-go. Keep the native default unless all fidelity proofs justify a separately reviewed change. No production client interruption or app restart is required by this investigation.\n\n## Accepted chapter allocation — 2026-09-23\n\nChapter 20260923T000959Z-502f011b; review 2026-10-21T00:09:59.226362+00:00. Disposition: carry. Allocation: parked. Explicit human reprioritization of simultaneous viewing activates this bounded investigation; retain disposable proof and allowed no-go, native default intact.\n\nOne serial implementation slot per Project; allocation does not launch a controller or interrupt existing work. Preserve stable identity and all prior implementation/PR/Run evidence.","rank":1,"completed":false,"assignee":null},"reference":{"issue_url":"https://linear.app/loopflow/issue/LOO-283/evaluate-shared-warp-and-loopflow-viewing-without-terminal-regressions","workspace":null},"runtime":null,"next_move":{"owner":"project","reason":"Task is ready to start"},"condition":{"state":"waiting","reason":"Task is ready to start","observed_at":"2026-09-23T15:06:37.21025Z","evidence_age_secs":null,"local_progress":{"state":"not_applicable","unsettled":false,"dirty":null,"authored_commits":null,"recovery_required":null,"reason":null}},"actions":{"recommended":null,"reason":"Task is ready to start"},"active_pr":null,"section":"available"},{"task":{"id":"f7d1f6d9-0ed9-4ace-8d49-ed967dc875c9","identifier":"LOO-282","name":"Show the recorded location of an active Session client","description":"The ELSEWHERE pane is intentionally generic because ProviderClientRef records PID/start evidence but no terminal provenance. Record available client/terminal and Home context at provider launch and expose it through the shared Session projection so Mac/CLI can explain where the client is active (Warp, another Loopflow window, or SSH when known). Do not infer ownership from labels or add a Swift liveness registry. Missing provenance must stay explicit and readable; mirror any DTO additions in Rust/Swift fixtures without defaults.\n\nDone when an active client with known provenance has the same location in CLI and Mac, unknown/legacy provenance stays generic, and PID reuse cannot inherit another client's label. Selecting it leaves it alive. Move here remains explicit and warns about unsent input loss; no automatic takeover is introduced. Preserve the separate moved/completed stop intent consumed by the displaced launcher.\n\n## Accepted chapter allocation — 2026-09-23\n\nChapter 20260923T000959Z-502f011b; review 2026-10-21T00:09:59.226362+00:00. Disposition: carry. Allocation: parked. Select when generic ELSEWHERE provenance obstructs a selected Session workflow; shared recorded provenance only, no inferred ownership.\n\nOne serial implementation slot per Project; allocation does not launch a controller or interrupt existing work. Preserve stable identity and all prior implementation/PR/Run evidence.","rank":2,"completed":false,"assignee":null},"reference":{"issue_url":"https://linear.app/loopflow/issue/LOO-282/show-the-recorded-location-of-an-active-session-client","workspace":null},"runtime":null,"next_move":{"owner":"project","reason":"Task is ready to start"},"condition":{"state":"waiting","reason":"Task is ready to start","observed_at":"2026-09-23T15:06:37.210251Z","evidence_age_secs":null,"local_progress":{"state":"not_applicable","unsettled":false,"dirty":null,"authored_commits":null,"recovery_required":null,"reason":null}},"actions":{"recommended":null,"reason":"Task is ready to start"},"active_pr":null,"section":"available"},{"task":{"id":"656ca5c8-fe92-41c1-848a-b69b8b10f633","identifier":"LOO-284","name":"Project Session actions and Work labels from the shared API","description":"Follow-up already called for in Product memory after native Sessions PR #1250; preserve it as a Linear Task rather than a scratch-only item. Rust owns Session legality and exact Work identity, but Swift reconstructs legal actions from kind/state and joins roadmap data for display labels.\n\nProject legal actions and the display Work path in SessionRecord, update Rust/Swift shared fixtures with required or explicitly optional fields, and delete the corresponding Swift action matrix, replacement-policy inference, Sessions-only roadmap join, and unused narrower scopes in the same coherent change. Keep view-local opening/error state and terminal presence separate: they cannot be derived from the durable record alone. Preserve explicit Move here and non-destructive preparation.\n\nDone when CLI and Mac render identical legal actions and Work labels from the same projection across interactive Sessions, Asks, and human FlowSteps; no parallel Swift legality model or extra roadmap lookup remains. Exercise pending/ready/resolved and active-elsewhere cases and prove illegal resolution remains rejected at the shared API boundary.\n\n## Accepted chapter allocation — 2026-09-23\n\nChapter 20260923T000959Z-502f011b; review 2026-10-21T00:09:59.226362+00:00. Disposition: carry. Allocation: queued. After LOO-251, before planning integration: shared Session actions/Work labels and coherent Swift deletion.\n\nOne serial implementation slot per Project; allocation does not launch a controller or interrupt existing work. Preserve stable identity and all prior implementation/PR/Run evidence.","rank":3,"completed":false,"assignee":null},"reference":{"issue_url":"https://linear.app/loopflow/issue/LOO-284/project-session-actions-and-work-labels-from-the-shared-api","workspace":null},"runtime":null,"next_move":{"owner":"project","reason":"Task is ready to start"},"condition":{"state":"waiting","reason":"Task is ready to start","observed_at":"2026-09-23T15:06:37.210252Z","evidence_age_secs":null,"local_progress":{"state":"not_applicable","unsettled":false,"dirty":null,"authored_commits":null,"recovery_required":null,"reason":null}},"actions":{"recommended":null,"reason":"Task is ready to start"},"active_pr":null,"section":"available"},{"task":{"id":"40872684-3ee0-4507-b038-f1d379f49df6","identifier":"LOO-280","name":"Build one Ghostty-enabled Mac terminal product","description":"Observed 2026-09-22 at d31f2ffdf: SwiftPM links GhosttyKit and defines GHOSTTY_ENABLED; project.yml copies GhosttyResources but links neither GhosttyKit nor that flag, compiling terminal stubs. Earlier fresh Xcode build-for-testing failed on Ghostty-only test symbols. Resource validation also fails every terminal if optional shell payload is absent or mismatched; GHOSTTY_RESOURCES_DIR remains mutated process-wide.\n\nReplace these parallel definitions with one Mac terminal dependency consumed by both builds. Keep Loopflow's cross-platform library independent. One authoritative input must determine upstream revision, patch artifact version/checksum, and generated shell/terminfo provenance; ghostty-build currently rebuilds the library but not checked-in resources. Remove redundant Mac stubs/feature flags once consumers share the required target. Missing shell resources should disable blocks with a diagnostic while ordinary provider terminals still work; genuine library initialization failure remains an error. Contain initialization environment changes.\n\nDone when both SwiftPM and Xcode build-for-testing link the command-block exports, contain resources generated from the same source, and execute a real embedded PTY copy test through supported test paths. An app bundle missing shell resources still accepts terminal input. Resource copying, matching two manually edited revision strings, or compiling stubs does not count. Retain xterm-256color for provider fidelity unless separately proven. Respect hosted UI permission limits. Publish any changed binary only with authorization; no local .build path may remain in Package.swift.\n\n## Accepted chapter allocation — 2026-09-23\n\nChapter 20260923T000959Z-502f011b; review 2026-10-21T00:09:59.226362+00:00. Disposition: carry. Allocation: conditional_same_slot. Select only if real configured LOO-251 proof is blocked by the Xcode/Ghostty build gap; same serial Desktop slot, then return to LOO-251. Publication still requires separate authority.\n\nOne serial implementation slot per Project; allocation does not launch a controller or interrupt existing work. Preserve stable identity and all prior implementation/PR/Run evidence.","rank":4,"completed":false,"assignee":null},"reference":{"issue_url":"https://linear.app/loopflow/issue/LOO-280/build-one-ghostty-enabled-mac-terminal-product","workspace":null},"runtime":null,"next_move":{"owner":"project","reason":"Task is ready to start"},"condition":{"state":"waiting","reason":"Task is ready to start","observed_at":"2026-09-23T15:06:37.210252Z","evidence_age_secs":null,"local_progress":{"state":"not_applicable","unsettled":false,"dirty":null,"authored_commits":null,"recovery_required":null,"reason":null}},"actions":{"recommended":null,"reason":"Task is ready to start"},"active_pr":null,"section":"available"},{"task":{"id":"01a33274-2895-4b44-b599-7e298f9b7656","identifier":"LOO-281","name":"Prove shell blocks through the real shell, geometry, and long-output paths","description":"The branch at d31f2ffdf implements persistent completed command/output blocks, ordinary click selection, and Copy via a separate read-block C API. A real marked-output PTY test copies two blocks without native character selection. Human confirmation of final block appearance is still pending; invisible OSC metadata or triple-click selection does not meet the contract. Warp is the visual benchmark: whole-width grouping and separation, restrained tint/accent, hover/selection over the entire unit, and a distinct live prompt.\n\nClose the remaining evidence gaps and fix reproduced defects: shellIntegrationEmitsSemanticMarks manually calls zsh hooks, so it proves a fixture, not Ghostty login-shell detection/injection. Exercise the real no-command shell surface and one customized prompt (starship/powerlevel10k); document upstream system /bin/bash exclusion and avoid claiming all bundled shells are proven. Preserve provider Session behavior outside block semantics.\n\nGeometry helpers and their test both assume vertically centered grid padding; compare overlays and clicks to actual rendered cells at fractional cell heights, custom padding, resizing, scrolling, and wrapped output. Investigate renderer-mutex cost: ghostty_surface_command_blocks scans each viewport row with selectCommandBlock/prompt iteration every 100ms. Measure long output with the prompt thousands of rows above, then eliminate repeated scans if needed; record before/after latency. Treat geometry/performance as hypotheses until reproduced. Run the patch's two filtered Zig Screen tests or record the exact blocker.\n\nDone when visible blocks exist before interaction, ordinary clicks on command or output select and copy exactly both, switching blocks moves one highlight, live prompt remains editable, alternate-screen apps remain usable, and measured long-output/resize checks pass. Wait for parsed blocks in synthetic fixtures; inspect the real pasteboard. Page/pin IDs are not durable across reflow/recycling. Preserve one selected (id,text) snapshot and independent hover geometry. Do not restore native highlighting on block selection. Packaging parity is a separate Task; binary changes require a newly versioned artifact and authorized publication.\n\n## Accepted chapter allocation — 2026-09-23\n\nChapter 20260923T000959Z-502f011b; review 2026-10-21T00:09:59.226362+00:00. Disposition: carry. Allocation: parked. Select when reproduced shell-block behavior blocks human-selected work or the human prioritizes it. Preserve real-shell, geometry, copy, performance and Zig proof obligations.\n\nOne serial implementation slot per Project; allocation does not launch a controller or interrupt existing work. Preserve stable identity and all prior implementation/PR/Run evidence.","rank":5,"completed":false,"assignee":null},"reference":{"issue_url":"https://linear.app/loopflow/issue/LOO-281/prove-shell-blocks-through-the-real-shell-geometry-and-long-output","workspace":null},"runtime":null,"next_move":{"owner":"project","reason":"Task is ready to start"},"condition":{"state":"waiting","reason":"Task is ready to start","observed_at":"2026-09-23T15:06:37.210253Z","evidence_age_secs":null,"local_progress":{"state":"not_applicable","unsettled":false,"dirty":null,"authored_commits":null,"recovery_required":null,"reason":null}},"actions":{"recommended":null,"reason":"Task is ready to start"},"active_pr":null,"section":"available"},{"task":{"id":"3aef0d2f-630c-49ba-9535-01a7591b7d18","identifier":"LOO-251","name":"Finish the native Sessions multiplexer and promoted Ask handoff","description":"Reconciled 2026-09-22 against branch d31f2ffdf and Product memory. The original Ask-only directive is obsolete: use lf session list/open and provider-native resume. The split tree, per-window/per-repository layout and view retention, explicit Move here, typed TerminalIdentity, and clipboard/drop plumbing already exist. Do not rebuild them or restore a global surface registry/tmux presentation layer.\n\nRemaining outcome: prove the native Sessions workspace completes a promoted human Ask end to end and retains truthful readiness. One real promoted Ask must survive open, provider-native continuation, Ready, Complete, pane clearing, and release of the blocked caller. Exercise the permissioned UI path for focus, legal actions, and reconciliation; LocalAuthentication previously prevented runner initialization, which is no behavioral result. Preserve the existing Sessions readiness instrumentation and serial-open position evidence; measured Project budgets remain authoritative.\n\nKeep row selection non-destructive; Close view hides a Session while Complete resolves it. Move here alone replaces the exact owned client, warning that unsent input in the other terminal is lost. JSON preparation must not stop a provider. Window close/app quit still end embedded clients; provider history remains resumable.\n\nEvidence already recorded on 2026-09-22: human confirmed retained Session switching, copy/image paste/drop, and explicit Warp handoff. Subsequent real-PTY tests prove window-local release, typed close-event classification, and split paste routing. Human confirmation of corrected split paste remains pending: focus each side and confirm only that composer receives Command-V. Do not infer all-provider coverage from the Codex demo or mark this Task done from compilation alone.\n\nGhostty build parity, shell-block reliability, client provenance, and shared-view experiments are separate follow-ups. No fresh runtime proof or Task closure is claimed by this reconciliation.\n\n## Chapter proof obligations\n\nPublish defensible named Sessions readiness budgets and sampling methods before scoring. Retain every attempted repository open and Session selection, including errors, interruptions, truthful count, serial-open position, and verified interactive readiness. Preserve the fourteen-day/twenty-open proof populations in D2; evidence collection need not occupy an implementation slot. A source-only Xcode/Ghostty gap does not displace this opening Task: first attempt the real configured proof.\n\n## Accepted chapter allocation — 2026-09-23\n\nChapter 20260923T000959Z-502f011b; review 2026-10-21T00:09:59.226362+00:00. Disposition: carry. Allocation: opening. Open Desktop with the real configured LOO-251 proof; preserve caller release, permissioned UI, split-paste, readiness and published-budget obligations.\n\nOne serial implementation slot per Project; allocation does not launch a controller or interrupt existing work. Preserve stable identity and all prior implementation/PR/Run evidence.","rank":7,"completed":false,"assignee":null},"reference":{"issue_url":"https://linear.app/loopflow/issue/LOO-251/finish-the-native-sessions-multiplexer-and-promoted-ask-handoff","workspace":null},"runtime":null,"next_move":{"owner":"project","reason":"Task is ready to start"},"condition":{"state":"waiting","reason":"Task is ready to start","observed_at":"2026-09-23T15:06:37.210254Z","evidence_age_secs":null,"local_progress":{"state":"not_applicable","unsettled":false,"dirty":null,"authored_commits":null,"recovery_required":null,"reason":null}},"actions":{"recommended":null,"reason":"Task is ready to start"},"active_pr":null,"section":"available"},{"task":{"id":"daeb8f50-8a6a-4168-9c65-adbee99e2d96","identifier":"LOO-148","name":"Explain blocked Task recovery through the shared API in Desktop","description":"For a reproduced blocked or abandoned Task on a selected external workflow, Desktop presents the shared condition, reason, and any supported operation without inventing recovery legality. Infrastructure establishes the supported recovery/adoption semantics at the shared API boundary; Desktop consumes that result and proves the configured path or an honest unsupported outcome. Keep human resolution in Sessions. Do not add an action enum to descriptive NextMove/condition fields, assume abandoned implies recoverable, restore iOS scope, or create a second lifecycle model. Remain parked until the named workflow is blocked by this gap.\n\n## Accepted chapter allocation — 2026-09-23\n\nChapter 20260923T000959Z-502f011b; review 2026-10-21T00:09:59.226362+00:00. Disposition: rewrite. Allocation: parked. Desktop owns presentation; Infrastructure Reliability owns shared recovery legality. Select only for reproduced blocked/abandoned recovery gap on selected external work; reconcile stale enum proposal first.\n\nOne serial implementation slot per Project; allocation does not launch a controller or interrupt existing work. Preserve stable identity and all prior implementation/PR/Run evidence.","rank":9,"completed":false,"assignee":null},"reference":{"issue_url":"https://linear.app/loopflow/issue/LOO-148/explain-blocked-task-recovery-through-the-shared-api-in-desktop","workspace":null},"runtime":null,"next_move":{"owner":"project","reason":"Task is ready to start"},"condition":{"state":"waiting","reason":"Task is ready to start","observed_at":"2026-09-23T15:06:37.210995Z","evidence_age_secs":null,"local_progress":{"state":"not_applicable","unsettled":false,"dirty":null,"authored_commits":null,"recovery_required":null,"reason":null}},"actions":{"recommended":null,"reason":"Task is ready to start"},"active_pr":null,"section":"available"},{"task":{"id":"56cfdb24-cc73-4153-9ea8-1f2dab2af71a","identifier":"LOO-274","name":"Restore Wave fleet and roadmap loading in the Mac app","description":"Restore Wave fleet and roadmap loading in the Mac app\n\n<!-- loopflow-task-start:b298456644b27e19cead7f4344385592d4ac6affbb9e13ee84b9f38f0d5feb2e -->\n\n## Accepted chapter allocation — 2026-09-23\n\nChapter 20260923T000959Z-502f011b; review 2026-10-21T00:09:59.226362+00:00. Disposition: retire. Allocation: retire. Rejected general fleet restoration. Preserve code and history; do not reintroduce it under the scoped planning integration Task.\n\nOne serial implementation slot per Project; allocation does not launch a controller or interrupt existing work. Preserve stable identity and all prior implementation/PR/Run evidence.\n\nClosed as retired by accepted direction, not as shipped or achieved. The supported PM close operation marks the issue complete; this explicit retirement reason is its meaning. No product code, branch, PR, Run, or evidence is deleted.","rank":6,"completed":true,"assignee":null},"reference":{"issue_url":"https://linear.app/loopflow/issue/LOO-274/restore-wave-fleet-and-roadmap-loading-in-the-mac-app","workspace":null},"runtime":null,"next_move":{"owner":"project","reason":"Linear Task is complete"},"condition":{"state":"waiting","reason":"Linear Task is complete","observed_at":"2026-09-23T15:06:37.210254Z","evidence_age_secs":null,"local_progress":{"state":"not_applicable","unsettled":false,"dirty":null,"authored_commits":null,"recovery_required":null,"reason":null}},"actions":{"recommended":null,"reason":"Task is ready to start"},"active_pr":null,"section":"later"},{"task":{"id":"a80fc7e3-4da0-4b4e-9423-a81c2bddbd07","identifier":"LOO-221","name":"Fix Mac app Agent activity banner: activity --json decode misses `aggregate` key","description":"Fix Mac app Agent activity banner: activity --json decode misses `aggregate` key\n\nThe Mac app ([Loopflow.app](<http://Loopflow.app>) 0.12.8) shows a persistent warning banner in the Wave Fleet header:\n\n> Agent activity unavailable\n> lf query JSON did not decode: keyNotFound(CodingKeys(stringValue: \"aggregate\", intValue: nil), Swift.DecodingError.Context(codingPath: [], debugDescription: \"No value associated with key CodingKeys(stringValue: \"aggregate\", intValue: nil)\")\n\nWhere it happens:\n\n* swift/Loopflow/Services/RegistryQuery.swift:349 throws RegistryQueryError(\"lf query JSON did not decode: ...\").\n* The failing call is the activity query: `workActivity(...)` runs `lf activity --since ... --limit ... --json` and decodes `WorkActivitySnapshot` (RegistryQuery.swift:120-133). The Swift DTO requires a top-level `aggregate` key that the CLI's `lf activity --json` payload does not emit (or emits under a different shape).\n\nThis is wire-DTO drift between the Swift mirror and the Rust emitter. Per STYLE.md's DTO rules: no defaults, every field required or explicitly Optional, and round-trip fixtures under tests/fixtures/dto/ must cover the shape.\n\nDone when:\n\n* `lf activity --json` output and the Swift `WorkActivitySnapshot` DTO agree on the wire shape (decide whether `aggregate` is required from the CLI or removed/Optional in Swift — align with what the Rust side actually emits and the fixture).\n* The DTO fixture under tests/fixtures/dto/ covers the reconciled shape and both language fixture tests pass.\n* The Mac app renders agent activity with no \"Agent activity unavailable\" banner against the live `lf` 0.12.8+ CLI.\n\n<!-- loopflow-task-start:6830b0b58237613dc4b6515389de4a88bd48dd1bb2fee7f00954a9a08c98871b -->","rank":8,"completed":true,"assignee":null},"reference":{"issue_url":"https://linear.app/loopflow/issue/LOO-221/fix-mac-app-agent-activity-banner-activity-json-decode-misses","workspace":{"slug":"fix-mac-app-agent-activity","branch":"jack-heart/fix-mac-app-agent-activity","worktree":"/Users/jack/src/loopflow.fix-mac-app-agent-activity"}},"runtime":{"work_id":"task_95d4aa9a0e8d4166b3032215cf52ebb7","project_id":"proj_86f8af8b1e71ee288b167663c5f9e41b","routing_project_id":"proj_86f8af8b1e71ee288b167663c5f9e41b","status":"abandoned","reason":"abandoned","updated_at":"2026-08-20T03:50:34Z","provider":"codex"},"next_move":{"owner":"project","reason":"refresh reviewer-facing PR copy for the current head before settlement"},"condition":{"state":"blocked","reason":"Task LOO-221 worktree /Users/jack/src/loopflow.fix-mac-app-agent-activity is missing; restore that exact path on branch \"jack-heart/fix-mac-app-agent-activity\" before `lf task resume LOO-221`; Task identity and PR history are unchanged","observed_at":"2026-09-23T15:06:37.210472Z","evidence_age_secs":2978163,"local_progress":{"state":"missing","unsettled":true,"dirty":null,"authored_commits":null,"recovery_required":true,"reason":"Task LOO-221 worktree /Users/jack/src/loopflow.fix-mac-app-agent-activity is missing; restore that exact path on branch \"jack-heart/fix-mac-app-agent-activity\" before `lf task resume LOO-221`; Task identity and PR history are unchanged"}},"actions":{"recommended":"no_action","reason":"Task is terminal"},"active_pr":{"id":"pr_9632d6c5270a4c1a849586f9bc25f1c5","sequence":1,"slug":"fix-mac-app-agent-activity","branch":"jack-heart/fix-mac-app-agent-activity","base_commit":"bcea828c8bd29fe40c1365720c0938a7e2459acd","phase":"open","empty":null,"publication":{"requested_at":"2026-08-20T01:04:06Z","presentation":null,"github":{"number":1205,"url":"https://github.com/loopflowstudio/loopflow/pull/1205"},"merge":{"mode":"auto","requested_at":"2026-08-20T08:51:47Z","head_sha":"877eaa8d09d8f7878f0aa83bee7c2a4c43636afb","after_merge":"continue_task","next_slug":null}},"merge_commit":null,"abandoned_at":null},"section":"later"},{"task":{"id":"73f0dbcf-9bd1-48ee-947d-5ec370f0312d","identifier":"LOO-149","name":"Make Wave purpose, Projects, and Chat the stable Mac surface","description":"Superseded by Loopflow Live. The company Discord is now the canonical conversation, and the Mac app becomes the fast fleet/control surface. Preserve the useful objective, Project/KR hierarchy, stable Wave list, status reasons, accessibility, and progressive disclosure in the new control-room Task; do not keep in-app Chat as the default third pane.","rank":10,"completed":true,"assignee":null},"reference":{"issue_url":"https://linear.app/loopflow/issue/LOO-149/make-wave-purpose-projects-and-chat-the-stable-mac-surface","workspace":{"slug":"stable-wave-surface","branch":"jack-heart/stable-wave-surface-product-wave-real-data-proof","worktree":"/Users/jack/src/loopflow.stable-wave-surface"}},"runtime":{"work_id":"task_7ad56f01347e91c74dd3273747af17b8","project_id":"proj_86f8af8b1e71ee288b167663c5f9e41b","routing_project_id":"proj_86f8af8b1e71ee288b167663c5f9e41b","status":"abandoned","reason":"abandoned","updated_at":"2026-07-21T17:28:19Z","provider":"opencode"},"next_move":{"owner":"project","reason":"abandoned"},"condition":{"state":"blocked","reason":"Task LOO-149 worktree /Users/jack/src/loopflow.stable-wave-surface is missing; restore that exact path on branch \"jack-heart/stable-wave-surface-product-wave-real-data-proof\" before `lf task resume LOO-149`; Task identity and PR history are unchanged","observed_at":"2026-09-23T15:06:37.211043Z","evidence_age_secs":5521098,"local_progress":{"state":"missing","unsettled":true,"dirty":null,"authored_commits":null,"recovery_required":true,"reason":"Task LOO-149 worktree /Users/jack/src/loopflow.stable-wave-surface is missing; restore that exact path on branch \"jack-heart/stable-wave-surface-product-wave-real-data-proof\" before `lf task resume LOO-149`; Task identity and PR history are unchanged"}},"actions":{"recommended":"no_action","reason":"Task is terminal"},"active_pr":{"id":"pr_9304b71663e342babe9c2f1516d4f55e","sequence":5,"slug":"product-wave-real-data-proof","branch":"jack-heart/stable-wave-surface-product-wave-real-data-proof","base_commit":"9e3cccddb132da3060c51b8f9d8c155c1559af13","phase":"working","empty":null,"publication":null,"merge_commit":null,"abandoned_at":null},"section":"later"},{"task":{"id":"4baaafc6-4905-4477-ae22-36f974b50f00","identifier":"LOO-150","name":"[retired] Open interactive handoffs in the last successful surface","description":"## User-visible outcome\n\nOpen attaches an interactive human handoff in the surface that worked last time. Open in offers embedded Ghostty, Warp, and supported provider IDE targets only when each can honestly reach the same Session. A missing app or unsupported provider falls back visibly without changing or duplicating the durable handoff.\n\n## Dependencies\n\nBegin after W2-175 pins the shared attach descriptor. Integrate with the Active Sessions surface rather than adding a second launcher menu.\n\n## Contract\n\n* Embedded Ghostty is the required local fallback and runs the exact shared attach command. Swift presents the Session but does not create or name it.\n* Warp may attach through a command-bearing launch configuration. Opening only the worktree is a weaker action and must be labeled as such.\n* Offer Claude in VS Code or Cursor only with a known provider session id and proven workspace. Other IDEs open the worktree without claiming to attach.\n* Resolve Open in order: last successful surface for the provider on the current Home, last successful surface overall, then embedded Ghostty.\n* Update preference only after launch succeeds. Installed-app or capability loss causes a visible fallback and leaves the Session untouched.\n* Keep one Session, provider history, worktree, and completion path across all presentation targets.\n\n## Proof\n\nTests cover provider-specific preference, overall fallback, unavailable remembered app, unsupported provider, remote Home, launch failure, and preference update only after success. Manual trials attach one Session through embedded Ghostty and every supported external target without starting a duplicate process. Reuse the launcher and preference techniques in commits 710bcd60c, 6d0c98d67, b39ad201f, and current TaskWorkspaceView.","rank":11,"completed":true,"assignee":null},"reference":{"issue_url":"https://linear.app/loopflow/issue/LOO-150/retired-open-interactive-handoffs-in-the-last-successful-surface","workspace":{"slug":"open-interactive-handoffs-in-the","branch":"jack-heart/open-interactive-handoffs-in-the-5","worktree":"/Users/jack/src/loopflow.open-interactive-handoffs-in-the"}},"runtime":{"work_id":"task_fea3a9b60d2012bc558592d65dcab4a0","project_id":"proj_86f8af8b1e71ee288b167663c5f9e41b","routing_project_id":"proj_86f8af8b1e71ee288b167663c5f9e41b","status":"abandoned","reason":"abandoned","updated_at":"2026-07-21T17:28:19Z","provider":"opencode"},"next_move":{"owner":"project","reason":"abandoned"},"condition":{"state":"blocked","reason":"Task LOO-150 worktree /Users/jack/src/loopflow.open-interactive-handoffs-in-the is missing; restore that exact path on branch \"jack-heart/open-interactive-handoffs-in-the-5\" before `lf task resume LOO-150`; Task identity and PR history are unchanged","observed_at":"2026-09-23T15:06:37.211334Z","evidence_age_secs":5521098,"local_progress":{"state":"missing","unsettled":true,"dirty":null,"authored_commits":null,"recovery_required":true,"reason":"Task LOO-150 worktree /Users/jack/src/loopflow.open-interactive-handoffs-in-the is missing; restore that exact path on branch \"jack-heart/open-interactive-handoffs-in-the-5\" before `lf task resume LOO-150`; Task identity and PR history are unchanged"}},"actions":{"recommended":"no_action","reason":"Task is terminal"},"active_pr":{"id":"pr_d8eb09fcb36444fea8886a6464555232","sequence":5,"slug":"5","branch":"jack-heart/open-interactive-handoffs-in-the-5","base_commit":"2e6bcdb0aefb899b891c5d6597e99a063490f9e6","phase":"working","empty":null,"publication":null,"merge_commit":null,"abandoned_at":null},"section":"later"},{"task":{"id":"b5690fb1-3ee4-4d44-998e-08faa46d57d3","identifier":"LOO-151","name":"Show Active Sessions without turning every process into a control","description":"## User-visible outcome\n\nA user can progressively open Control and see every active Wave, Project, Task, direct execution body, and interactive human handoff. Deliberate handoffs are attachable; ordinary non-interactive bodies are visible and understandable but remain view-only.\n\n## Dependencies\n\nBegin after W2-123 defines the shared attention projection and W2-175 exposes durable interactive child Sessions and attach descriptors. Consume those contracts without Swift-side joins or filesystem inference.\n\n## Contract\n\n* Keep Chat as the default Wave experience. Control takes additional interaction to reach.\n* Active Sessions is the first Control view. Run History is named but deferred.\n* Account for all live Wave, Project, Task, and direct execution bodies using stable identity, parentage, provider/model, Home, worktree, current step, age, progress freshness, reason, and next owner when available.\n* Show Open or Attach only for deliberate interactive handoffs. Do not expose attach, steer, stop, or interrupt for ordinary non-interactive bodies in the first slice.\n* A human-waiting interactive handoff makes its Task, Project, and Wave red even while its body is alive.\n* Distinguish missing, stale, unreachable, stopped, and unavailable evidence; never turn missing rows into a healthy empty state.\n\n## Proof\n\nA shared fixture renders mixed Wave, Project, Task, direct execution, handoff, remote Home, dead body, and stale evidence rows. The real Product Wave census agrees with CLI identity and counts. Interactive Open attaches the exact Session; non-interactive rows expose no mutation controls. VoiceOver conveys ownership, reason, freshness, and available action.","rank":12,"completed":true,"assignee":null},"reference":{"issue_url":"https://linear.app/loopflow/issue/LOO-151/show-active-sessions-without-turning-every-process-into-a-control","workspace":{"slug":"show-active-sessions-without-turning","branch":"jack-heart/show-active-sessions-without-turning","worktree":"/Users/jack/src/loopflow.show-active-sessions-without-turning"}},"runtime":{"work_id":"task_0aabdbaea6fb475cdf0b64e5e7e7bd89","project_id":"proj_86f8af8b1e71ee288b167663c5f9e41b","routing_project_id":"proj_86f8af8b1e71ee288b167663c5f9e41b","status":"abandoned","reason":"abandoned","updated_at":"2026-07-21T17:28:19Z","provider":"claude"},"next_move":{"owner":"project","reason":"abandoned"},"condition":{"state":"blocked","reason":"Task LOO-151 worktree /Users/jack/src/loopflow.show-active-sessions-without-turning is missing; restore that exact path before `lf task resume LOO-151`; Task identity and PR history are unchanged","observed_at":"2026-09-23T15:06:37.212166Z","evidence_age_secs":5521098,"local_progress":{"state":"missing","unsettled":true,"dirty":null,"authored_commits":null,"recovery_required":true,"reason":"Task LOO-151 worktree /Users/jack/src/loopflow.show-active-sessions-without-turning is missing; restore that exact path before `lf task resume LOO-151`; Task identity and PR history are unchanged"}},"actions":{"recommended":"no_action","reason":"Task is terminal"},"active_pr":null,"section":"later"},{"task":{"id":"c957123f-7cd9-4e7b-acc4-4921b8a02af6","identifier":"LOO-152","name":"Make Wave Chat fast, durable, and legible across failures","description":"Superseded by Loopflow Live. Discord now owns shared company chat history across humans, Homes, and Waves. Reuse the durable Wave inbox, delivery, restart, and failure-legibility work in the Discord provider Tasks; do not deepen a separate Mac-owned Wave transcript.","rank":13,"completed":true,"assignee":null},"reference":{"issue_url":"https://linear.app/loopflow/issue/LOO-152/make-wave-chat-fast-durable-and-legible-across-failures","workspace":{"slug":"make-wave-chat-fast-durable","branch":"jack-heart/make-wave-chat-fast-durable-5","worktree":"/Users/jack/src/loopflow.make-wave-chat-fast-durable"}},"runtime":{"work_id":"task_50418b03bae612866b92c0101346fc3d","project_id":"proj_86f8af8b1e71ee288b167663c5f9e41b","routing_project_id":"proj_86f8af8b1e71ee288b167663c5f9e41b","status":"abandoned","reason":"abandoned","updated_at":"2026-07-21T17:28:19Z","provider":"opencode"},"next_move":{"owner":"project","reason":"abandoned"},"condition":{"state":"blocked","reason":"Task LOO-152 worktree /Users/jack/src/loopflow.make-wave-chat-fast-durable is missing; restore that exact path on branch \"jack-heart/make-wave-chat-fast-durable-5\" before `lf task resume LOO-152`; Task identity and PR history are unchanged","observed_at":"2026-09-23T15:06:37.212515Z","evidence_age_secs":5521098,"local_progress":{"state":"missing","unsettled":true,"dirty":null,"authored_commits":null,"recovery_required":true,"reason":"Task LOO-152 worktree /Users/jack/src/loopflow.make-wave-chat-fast-durable is missing; restore that exact path on branch \"jack-heart/make-wave-chat-fast-durable-5\" before `lf task resume LOO-152`; Task identity and PR history are unchanged"}},"actions":{"recommended":"no_action","reason":"Task is terminal"},"active_pr":{"id":"pr_5aca6b6190fc4af18423b2f9f8425b4c","sequence":5,"slug":"5","branch":"jack-heart/make-wave-chat-fast-durable-5","base_commit":"2e6bcdb0aefb899b891c5d6597e99a063490f9e6","phase":"working","empty":null,"publication":null,"merge_commit":null,"abandoned_at":null},"section":"later"},{"task":{"id":"b429bab9-9313-44c0-a4fd-4ccb889be96c","identifier":"LOO-153","name":"Make Wave purpose, Projects, and Chat the stable Mac surface","description":"## User-visible outcome\n\nSelecting a repository and Wave opens one calm, legible workspace: a stable Wave list on the left, the Wave objective and measured Projects in the center, and Chat on the right. The interface spends space on meaning rather than repository chrome, truncated prose, timestamps, or internal registry concepts.\n\n## Contract\n\n* Replace the permanent repository column with a repository dropdown above the stable Wave list.\n* Keep every Wave in one stable list. Give each row a small restrained green, red, or black glass lens; do not regroup rows by state and do not restore status pills.\n* Preserve room for future Wave ancestry without inventing hierarchy or recursive Projects now.\n* Lead the detail pane with a one-sentence objective. Keep Projects persistently visible and make open-Task count plus KR list their strongest qualities.\n* Keep Chat as the default third pane. Operational detail is progressive disclosure, not a competing default tab.\n* Remove raw sync timestamps, registered-wave vocabulary, giant empty states, clipped objective prose, and implementation errors from the primary hierarchy.\n* Consume shared status fields where they exist. Do not infer final lens semantics in Swift; W2-123 owns that projection.\n\n## Existing material\n\nBuild from WavesView, WaveDetailPane, current Project cards, and the existing Ghostty visual system. The attached direction is recorded in scratch/ux.md. Keep the basic three-pane structure while correcting its hierarchy.\n\n## Proof\n\nAt narrow and wide desktop sizes, every Wave in the real Product registry remains selectable without horizontal clipping. Opening Product immediately exposes its one-sentence objective, every Project, each open-Task count and KR list, and usable Chat. A screenshot fixture covers empty, loading, error, selected, and future-child indentation states. VoiceOver names the lens reason rather than only its color.\n\n## Exclusions\n\nDo not build Active Sessions, external launch adapters, Run History, a kanban board, or a Swift-owned Session model in this Task.\n\n## Superseded\n\nClosed before implementation. Its first Task Session pinned a development-provenance lf and could not open the production store. W2-178 owns the unchanged product work with a production-provenance execution context.","rank":14,"completed":true,"assignee":null},"reference":{"issue_url":"https://linear.app/loopflow/issue/LOO-153/make-wave-purpose-projects-and-chat-the-stable-mac-surface","workspace":{"slug":"make-wave-purpose-projects-and","branch":"jack-heart/make-wave-purpose-projects-and","worktree":"/Users/jack/src/loopflow.make-wave-purpose-projects-and"}},"runtime":{"work_id":"task_b88e0b61e1645fcc7185ddaa0402fa91","project_id":"proj_86f8af8b1e71ee288b167663c5f9e41b","routing_project_id":"proj_86f8af8b1e71ee288b167663c5f9e41b","status":"abandoned","reason":"abandoned","updated_at":"2026-07-21T17:28:19Z","provider":"claude"},"next_move":{"owner":"project","reason":"abandoned"},"condition":{"state":"blocked","reason":"Task LOO-153 worktree /Users/jack/src/loopflow.make-wave-purpose-projects-and is missing; restore that exact path on branch \"jack-heart/make-wave-purpose-projects-and\" before `lf task resume LOO-153`; Task identity and PR history are unchanged","observed_at":"2026-09-23T15:06:37.212744Z","evidence_age_secs":5521098,"local_progress":{"state":"missing","unsettled":true,"dirty":null,"authored_commits":null,"recovery_required":true,"reason":"Task LOO-153 worktree /Users/jack/src/loopflow.make-wave-purpose-projects-and is missing; restore that exact path on branch \"jack-heart/make-wave-purpose-projects-and\" before `lf task resume LOO-153`; Task identity and PR history are unchanged"}},"actions":{"recommended":"no_action","reason":"Task is terminal"},"active_pr":{"id":"pr_074332fd74164956b607b93422191091","sequence":1,"slug":"make-wave-purpose-projects-and","branch":"jack-heart/make-wave-purpose-projects-and","base_commit":"3551f5217f0dc4dce00d4a734c532853368265b8","phase":"working","empty":null,"publication":null,"merge_commit":null,"abandoned_at":null},"section":"later"},{"task":{"id":"f63ca30f-0311-4145-a517-dfea9e28debf","identifier":"LOO-154","name":"See and control all current and available work from the Mac","description":"Design: scratch/w2-141.md (W2-141). Depends on the lf work read command.\n\nOne query, two shapes — a lens may change the SHAPE, not merely filter one outline:\n\nNOW — flat, cross-wave, grouped by attention (Ready for review, Needs input, Working, Stopped, Failed), ordered by age within each group. Rows carry wave/project as context, not as structure. This is what Claude Codes agent view arrived at, and what Conductor (the healthiest worktree manager) uses: a status-grouped list, not lanes.\n\nROADMAP — the Wave > Project > Task tree from the PM snapshot. Complete, and renderable with zero processes running. Projects collapse to KR proof plus a session census; waves collapse to residency plus an attention count. synced_at always on screen.\n\nEvery row carries three orthogonal facts on independent channels, never collapsed into one status word: PM completion, Session status, and process liveness. A dead process is not a dead task — a Stopped row stays attachable and resumable and says why it stopped.\n\nSwift work:\n\n* [RegistryQuery.work](<http://RegistryQuery.work>)() -> lf work --json -> WorkSnapshot. Replaces the per-wave lf pm show fan-out in WavesView.buildWavePlanCache (one spawn, not N).\n* WaveProjectWork / WaveTaskWork already mirror the per-wave shape and runtime is already Optional, so the Available predicate decodes today.\n* Delete RegistryQuery.backlog() and BacklogItem. backlog() computes availability as !completed over lf pm show, which carries no Session data; its docstring tells callers to \"subtract running task ids/titles\" — a title-matched join. It has no production callers. Availability is the ABSENCE of a Session, not a PM property.\n\nNo kanban board. The board metaphor is losing empirically (Vibe Kanban sunsetting, Crystal deprecated, Terragon shut down), and a board whose drag does nothing is a lie.\n\nIneligible rows are greyed WITH THE REASON attached, never hidden — OmniFocus stacks a computed availability model and a per-view filter with different semantics, and produced years of \"where did my task go\" threads. One hiding mechanism, never two.\n\nHOME CONTROL — depends on W2-88 as well as lf work\n\nEach Loopflow Wave has one inherited Home. Show that address on its Wave or product row and consume shared Home runtime evidence without implementing SSH in Swift. The surface distinguishes unreachable, unknown, reachable but stopped, and running. Selecting the Home navigates or opens the correct execution context. The primary contextual action is Open or Attach when running, Start on <home> when reachable but stopped, and an actionable reason when it cannot be reached. Start is idempotent, runs on the configured Home rather than the UI machine, and returns the resident identity needed to attach. The same Home, state, reason, and controls must appear in CLI status and the shared DTO; no Mac-only lifecycle model.","rank":15,"completed":true,"assignee":null},"reference":{"issue_url":"https://linear.app/loopflow/issue/LOO-154/see-and-control-all-current-and-available-work-from-the-mac","workspace":{"slug":"see-and-control-all-current","branch":"jack-heart/see-and-control-all-current-wave-home-control","worktree":"/Users/jack/src/loopflow.see-and-control-all-current"}},"runtime":{"work_id":"task_9d7fe58867b15b69e9123cad881d65ef","project_id":"proj_86f8af8b1e71ee288b167663c5f9e41b","routing_project_id":"proj_86f8af8b1e71ee288b167663c5f9e41b","status":"abandoned","reason":"abandoned","updated_at":"2026-07-21T17:28:19Z","provider":"claude"},"next_move":{"owner":"project","reason":"abandoned"},"condition":{"state":"blocked","reason":"Task LOO-154 worktree /Users/jack/src/loopflow.see-and-control-all-current is missing; restore that exact path before `lf task resume LOO-154`; Task identity and PR history are unchanged","observed_at":"2026-09-23T15:06:37.213747Z","evidence_age_secs":5521098,"local_progress":{"state":"missing","unsettled":true,"dirty":null,"authored_commits":null,"recovery_required":true,"reason":"Task LOO-154 worktree /Users/jack/src/loopflow.see-and-control-all-current is missing; restore that exact path before `lf task resume LOO-154`; Task identity and PR history are unchanged"}},"actions":{"recommended":"no_action","reason":"Task is terminal"},"active_pr":null,"section":"later"},{"task":{"id":"0f57c2d5-5967-4db5-86c2-f1fc09aa0ffd","identifier":"LOO-155","name":"Embedded terminal build driver","description":"Closed as superseded. The retired CommandPalette/palette terminal runtime is not the current Mac launch contract. Wave, Project, and Task launch and attach must use the shared Loopflow API; W2-146 owns the current Mac-facing implementation.","rank":16,"completed":true,"assignee":null},"reference":{"issue_url":"https://linear.app/loopflow/issue/LOO-155/embedded-terminal-build-driver","workspace":null},"runtime":null,"next_move":{"owner":"project","reason":"Linear Task is complete"},"condition":{"state":"waiting","reason":"Linear Task is complete","observed_at":"2026-09-23T15:06:37.213951Z","evidence_age_secs":null,"local_progress":{"state":"not_applicable","unsettled":false,"dirty":null,"authored_commits":null,"recovery_required":null,"reason":null}},"actions":{"recommended":null,"reason":"Task is ready to start"},"active_pr":null,"section":"later"},{"task":{"id":"d01abde6-bf28-496d-8753-83f15ebaf00b","identifier":"LOO-156","name":"Reshape the surface, trim the UI","description":"Closed as superseded. The current app exposes WavesView with WaveDetailPane and native Wave Chat; the terminal-only /goal surface and deletion of native chat are no longer the Product direction. Current Now/Roadmap surface work is W2-146.","rank":17,"completed":true,"assignee":null},"reference":{"issue_url":"https://linear.app/loopflow/issue/LOO-156/reshape-the-surface-trim-the-ui","workspace":null},"runtime":null,"next_move":{"owner":"project","reason":"Linear Task is complete"},"condition":{"state":"waiting","reason":"Linear Task is complete","observed_at":"2026-09-23T15:06:37.213953Z","evidence_age_secs":null,"local_progress":{"state":"not_applicable","unsettled":false,"dirty":null,"authored_commits":null,"recovery_required":null,"reason":null}},"actions":{"recommended":null,"reason":"Task is ready to start"},"active_pr":null,"section":"later"},{"task":{"id":"65b606aa-b6a1-4d2d-a91a-255f94b39360","identifier":"LOO-157","name":"UX iteration loop","description":"Closed. A standing UX generator is not a concrete Task; ongoing UX iteration belongs to Mac Surface UX project cadence, with each reproducible gap filed as its own Task.","rank":18,"completed":true,"assignee":null},"reference":{"issue_url":"https://linear.app/loopflow/issue/LOO-157/ux-iteration-loop","workspace":null},"runtime":null,"next_move":{"owner":"project","reason":"Linear Task is complete"},"condition":{"state":"waiting","reason":"Linear Task is complete","observed_at":"2026-09-23T15:06:37.213954Z","evidence_age_secs":null,"local_progress":{"state":"not_applicable","unsettled":false,"dirty":null,"authored_commits":null,"recovery_required":null,"reason":null}},"actions":{"recommended":null,"reason":"Task is ready to start"},"active_pr":null,"section":"later"},{"task":{"id":"5d580b7c-a8ad-4ca0-9249-646ddc75101a","identifier":"LOO-158","name":"wave-surface UX exploration","description":"Closed as superseded by W2-141 and PR #889, which produced the current Now/Available/Roadmap research and W2-146 implementation task. Reopen only as a narrow defect from dogfooding the current surface.","rank":19,"completed":true,"assignee":null},"reference":{"issue_url":"https://linear.app/loopflow/issue/LOO-158/wave-surface-ux-exploration","workspace":null},"runtime":null,"next_move":{"owner":"project","reason":"Linear Task is complete"},"condition":{"state":"waiting","reason":"Linear Task is complete","observed_at":"2026-09-23T15:06:37.213954Z","evidence_age_secs":null,"local_progress":{"state":"not_applicable","unsettled":false,"dirty":null,"authored_commits":null,"recovery_required":null,"reason":null}},"actions":{"recommended":null,"reason":"Task is ready to start"},"active_pr":null,"section":"later"},{"task":{"id":"1e1da818-54b0-4ce5-a4d8-abcf3a9f38a4","identifier":"LOO-159","name":"Make Loopflow Chat follow each Wave's active backing","description":"> “the Loopflow chat should either be a discord client if discord is on or mirror a similar experience for local chat with the waves regardless”\n\nRender one channel-shaped Loopflow Chat surface over the backing-aware API. With no Discord binding, history and compose use durable local Wave chat. With Discord bound, project the live channel without persisting a second transcript and make the backing obvious. Compose must use attributed Discord delivery or an explicit Open in Discord action until that delivery exists—never show a local input that creates a second live conversation. Show backing/epoch boundaries while keeping earlier local history readable.\n\nDemo: chat entirely inside Loopflow in local mode, enable a Discord binding, see the same surface follow that channel, and prove no message can look accepted while absent from the active backing.","rank":20,"completed":true,"assignee":null},"reference":{"issue_url":"https://linear.app/loopflow/issue/LOO-159/make-loopflow-chat-follow-each-waves-active-backing","workspace":null},"runtime":null,"next_move":{"owner":"project","reason":"Linear Task is complete"},"condition":{"state":"waiting","reason":"Linear Task is complete","observed_at":"2026-09-23T15:06:37.213955Z","evidence_age_secs":null,"local_progress":{"state":"not_applicable","unsettled":false,"dirty":null,"authored_commits":null,"recovery_required":null,"reason":null}},"actions":{"recommended":null,"reason":"Task is ready to start"},"active_pr":null,"section":"later"},{"task":{"id":"45a4d4fe-b233-4fc6-94d1-54b7caabf99f","identifier":"LOO-160","name":"Make the Mac app Loopflow's fast control room","description":"## Outcome\n\nThe Mac app becomes the daily front door for the full Loopflow fleet without owning a second runtime or company transcript.\n\n## Contract\n\n* Render the shared fleet snapshot: all repositories and Waves, desired/observed state, active agents, output tok/s, attention, Project/KR proof, Tasks, Runs, recent commits/PRs, activity, and Discord delivery.\n* Selection drills Wave -> Project -> Task -> Run -> raw trace/log/PR.\n* Legal controls come from Rust: start available Task, pause/resume Wave, recover/resume Work, answer a gate, open a PR, and edit planning/KRs through the PM API.\n* Discord is canonical conversation. Open the owning channel; do not mirror the full transcript.\n* Keep missing and stale evidence honest. Do not infer lifecycle, actionability, or health in Swift.\n* Preserve accessibility, stable hierarchy, and narrow-window use from the superseded PRD-1 intent.\n\n## Demo and done when\n\nFrom a cold launch, find an idle Task, start it, watch its Run and PR appear, inspect its trace, edit a KR, pause and resume its Wave, and open the owning Discord channel. Shared fixtures cover local/remote, live/paused/crash-loop, missing evidence, and every legal action.","rank":21,"completed":true,"assignee":null},"reference":{"issue_url":"https://linear.app/loopflow/issue/LOO-160/make-the-mac-app-loopflows-fast-control-room","workspace":null},"runtime":null,"next_move":{"owner":"project","reason":"Linear Task is complete"},"condition":{"state":"waiting","reason":"Linear Task is complete","observed_at":"2026-09-23T15:06:37.213955Z","evidence_age_secs":null,"local_progress":{"state":"not_applicable","unsettled":false,"dirty":null,"authored_commits":null,"recovery_required":null,"reason":null}},"actions":{"recommended":null,"reason":"Task is ready to start"},"active_pr":null,"section":"later"},{"task":{"id":"ed244473-7f2b-47e7-8f8e-61b77f3a81e6","identifier":"LOO-161","name":"Make the real control-room path fast and polished","description":"## Outcome\n\nThe control room feels immediate, calm, and visually finished on the long-lived registry rather than only on fixtures.\n\n## Contract\n\n* Measure cold first paint, refresh, selection, hierarchy expansion, activity paging, and raw-log opening before changing architecture.\n* Remove blocking subprocess/query fan-out and repeated parsing from the real path. Reads remain consistent with the shared DTO.\n* Give current action, next owner, and failure reason the strongest hierarchy; remove internal vocabulary and decorative status noise.\n* Preserve stable selection and scroll position while live data changes.\n* Treat keyboard access, VoiceOver, contrast, reduced motion, narrow windows, loading, partial, and failure states as product behavior.\n* Publish performance budgets from measured dogfood data and keep them in tests where deterministic.\n\n## Demo and done when\n\nRun the app against the month-old shared registry and a mixed local/remote fleet. Repeated cold launch and navigation stay inside published p50/p95 budgets, no interaction blocks on `lfd`, and screenshot/accessibility fixtures cover the complete state matrix.","rank":22,"completed":true,"assignee":null},"reference":{"issue_url":"https://linear.app/loopflow/issue/LOO-161/make-the-real-control-room-path-fast-and-polished","workspace":null},"runtime":null,"next_move":{"owner":"project","reason":"Linear Task is complete"},"condition":{"state":"waiting","reason":"Linear Task is complete","observed_at":"2026-09-23T15:06:37.213956Z","evidence_age_secs":null,"local_progress":{"state":"not_applicable","unsettled":false,"dirty":null,"authored_commits":null,"recovery_required":null,"reason":null}},"actions":{"recommended":null,"reason":"Task is ready to start"},"active_pr":null,"section":"later"},{"task":{"id":"e17ceffb-eb49-42aa-8f73-16d9cc1d7c23","identifier":"W2-86","name":"Conduct a Wave end to end from the Mac","description":"User story\n\nAfter choosing work in Now or Roadmap, a user can shape the Wave’s direction and cadence from the Mac: inspect evidence, approve or revise calibration, record trajectory, arrange the next beats, launch or reattach work, and see the resulting state—without dropping to a terminal or creating Mac-only planning concepts.\n\nScope\n\n* Build on W2-146’s Now/Roadmap/Home launch and attach surface, the shared status/reason contract, and Auditability drill-down.\n* Present proposed calibration changes with their evidence, affected objective/KRs, and an explicit approve/edit/reject action.\n* Let the user record trajectory notes and arrange beat slots against existing Projects and Tasks; Wave owns cadence and Project selection.\n* Show the durable PM/Session mutation and resulting next owner immediately after each action.\n* Reuse shared work, audit, chat, and control DTOs. Do not rebuild a portfolio, runboard, scheduler database, or Swift-owned Session lifecycle.\n\nProof\n\nFor one full dogfood week, the Mac is the only surface needed to review evidence, recalibrate a Wave, choose and schedule its next work, launch/reattach/steer it, and inspect the result. Every terminal fallback is recorded as a failure; every action round-trips to the same state shown by CLI; and no Mac-only domain type becomes a second source of truth.","rank":4294967295,"completed":true,"assignee":null},"reference":{"issue_url":null,"workspace":{"slug":"conduct-wave-from-mac","branch":"jack-heart/conduct-wave-from-mac-revert-wave-trajectory","worktree":"/Users/jack/src/loopflow.conduct-wave-from-mac"}},"runtime":{"work_id":"task_ba2baf1be1a2f90c75d464a2940a6cd4","project_id":"proj_86f8af8b1e71ee288b167663c5f9e41b","routing_project_id":"proj_86f8af8b1e71ee288b167663c5f9e41b","status":"abandoned","reason":"abandoned","updated_at":"2026-07-15T13:19:38Z","provider":"claude"},"next_move":{"owner":"project","reason":"abandoned"},"condition":{"state":"blocked","reason":"Task W2-86 worktree /Users/jack/src/loopflow.conduct-wave-from-mac is missing; restore that exact path before `lf task resume W2-86`; Task identity and PR history are unchanged","observed_at":"2026-09-23T15:06:37.356594Z","evidence_age_secs":6054419,"local_progress":{"state":"missing","unsettled":true,"dirty":null,"authored_commits":null,"recovery_required":true,"reason":"Task W2-86 worktree /Users/jack/src/loopflow.conduct-wave-from-mac is missing; restore that exact path before `lf task resume W2-86`; Task identity and PR history are unchanged"}},"actions":{"recommended":"no_action","reason":"Task is terminal"},"active_pr":null,"section":"later"}]},{"project":{"id":"d19956b2-9955-437d-aea6-d91766231c77","slug":"company-dogfood","name":"Company Dogfood","summary":"Make Loopflow useful for advancing Cube, Etude, Kata, and Hootro: in every chapter week, at least three of these four have durable Work that accurately records the human's current desired next focus and observable material progress on at least one Task pu","definition":"Make Loopflow useful for advancing Cube, Etude, Kata, and Hootro: in every chapter week, at least three of these four have durable Work that accurately records the human's current desired next focus and observable material progress on at least one Task pursuing human-selected work. Humans select priorities; Company Dogfood judges the evidence and exposes missing intent, stalled work, and product friction. Chapter review and reset support that loop. Loopflow self-hosting, runtime settlement, and planning activity do not themselves establish external progress.","flows":{"first":null,"loop":null,"finally":null},"krs":[{"text":"In each of the four seven-day chapter windows, at least three of Cube, Etude, Kata, and Hootro have durable Work accurately stating the human's current desired next focus at the cutoff and dated, verifiable material progress during that window on at least one Task pursuing work selected by that human.","holds":false}]},"runtime":{"work_id":"proj_9f1fc19a84211aed8b8136e55c8ab1f3","status":"ready","reason":"ready","updated_at":"2026-07-19T14:05:39Z","iteration":20,"pending_observations":0,"provider":"codex","last_failure":{"message":"project runner failed: Project plan refresh blocked before the next phase: could not refresh wave/product from Linear: Stored linear token expired and automatic refresh failed: linear OAuth refresh failed: the token endpoint rejected or could not complete the request. Run `lf auth linear` once to reconnect.. Reconnect or run `lf pm sync --wave product`.. Project Work proj_9f1fc19a84211aed8b8136e55c8ab1f3 did not continue on its stale plan; repair Linear planning, then restart it with `lf project run d19956b2-9955-437d-aea6-d91766231c77`","occurred_at":"2026-08-28T22:20:19Z"}},"next_move":{"owner":"project","reason":"ready"},"section":"now","tasks":[{"task":{"id":"eef88fa6-ddcf-4570-a779-8110c7a161c6","identifier":"LOO-278","name":"Add chapter reviews and interactive plan resets","description":"Create a built-in chapter skill family. Autonomous review-chapter evaluates every Project KR across the chapter and writes an evidence-backed chapter report. Interactive start-chapter begins with substantial human direction, decides the Wave portfolio, then launches scoped Wave and Project chapter sessions whose findings can revise parent boundaries. Preserve shipped code and history; expired plans lose planning authority. Prepare a design in the Task worktree, implement the coherent first slice, and stop at a working demo/review for the human.\n\n## Accepted chapter allocation — 2026-09-23\n\nChapter 20260923T000959Z-502f011b; review 2026-10-21T00:09:59.226362+00:00. Disposition: carry. Allocation: opening. Finish existing chapter slice and working human demo/review. Gate 2 accepted 2026-09-23; no external-momentum credit.\n\nOne serial implementation slot per Project; allocation does not launch a controller or interrupt existing work. Preserve stable identity and all prior implementation/PR/Run evidence.","rank":0,"completed":false,"assignee":null},"reference":{"issue_url":"https://linear.app/loopflow/issue/LOO-278/add-chapter-reviews-and-interactive-plan-resets","workspace":{"slug":"chapter-planning","branch":"jack-heart/chapter-planning","worktree":"/Users/jack/src/loopflow.chapter-planning"}},"runtime":{"work_id":"task_ad19281417ca4c1b86d735ac1af6be55","project_id":"proj_9f1fc19a84211aed8b8136e55c8ab1f3","routing_project_id":"proj_9f1fc19a84211aed8b8136e55c8ab1f3","status":"ready","reason":"ready","updated_at":"2026-09-22T01:31:26Z","provider":""},"next_move":{"owner":"project","reason":"ready"},"condition":{"state":"blocked","reason":"Task has uncommitted work","observed_at":"2026-09-23T15:06:37.214Z","evidence_age_secs":135311,"local_progress":{"state":"observed","unsettled":true,"dirty":true,"authored_commits":true,"recovery_required":false,"reason":null}},"actions":{"recommended":"resume","reason":"resume the parked Task"},"active_pr":{"id":"pr_24fe85ffaec24759a65718bd982fbd5a","sequence":1,"slug":"chapter-planning","branch":"jack-heart/chapter-planning","base_commit":"23e81d6e0ef59d371e56e7267e955edb308964cf","phase":"working","empty":null,"publication":null,"merge_commit":null,"abandoned_at":null},"section":"waiting"},{"task":{"id":"2c3d04d1-91b9-45ab-9ee5-2488f97d8aad","identifier":"LOO-185","name":"Provision Discord channels for a human-selected external workflow","description":"When the human selects Discord for Cube, Etude, Kata, or Hootro, idempotently provision or adopt the channels needed for that named workflow, preserve stable bindings through rename and retry, and demonstrate the workflow on its actual repository/Home configuration. Remain parked until that need is evidenced; CLI and native Sessions remain valid operating paths.\n\n## Contract\n\n* Guild and channel IDs are identity; names are presentation and may be renamed.\n* Provision only the category/channels, permissions, and webhook/byline resources the product uses.\n* Reconciliation adopts existing managed resources, repairs safe drift, and refuses ambiguous or foreign resources.\n* Every Wave has a stable visible byline. A Wave ignores its own echo without hiding another Wave's message.\n* Task and incident depth uses Discord threads rather than permanent Task channels.\n* Setup explains required Message Content access and least-privilege bot permissions.\n* Never store the bot token or webhook tokens in git or non-secret configuration.\n\n## Proof\n\nProve the named selected workflow on its actual repository/Home configuration: preserve channel binding/history through rename; reconcile twice without duplicates; cover partial setup and restart, missing permissions, deleted managed channels, duplicate names, and foreign resources. No compulsory two-Home rollout. Secrets resolve through Doppler and never enter git or non-secret configuration.\n\n## Accepted chapter allocation — 2026-09-23\n\nChapter 20260923T000959Z-502f011b; review 2026-10-21T00:09:59.226362+00:00. Disposition: rewrite. Allocation: parked. Select only when the human chooses Discord for a named external workflow and provisioning friction blocks it. Preserve idempotence, identity and secret handling; no compulsory two-Home rollout.\n\nOne serial implementation slot per Project; allocation does not launch a controller or interrupt existing work. Preserve stable identity and all prior implementation/PR/Run evidence.","rank":43,"completed":false,"assignee":null},"reference":{"issue_url":"https://linear.app/loopflow/issue/LOO-185/provision-discord-channels-for-a-human-selected-external-workflow","workspace":null},"runtime":null,"next_move":{"owner":"project","reason":"Task is ready to start"},"condition":{"state":"waiting","reason":"Task is ready to start","observed_at":"2026-09-23T15:06:37.324032Z","evidence_age_secs":null,"local_progress":{"state":"not_applicable","unsettled":false,"dirty":null,"authored_commits":null,"recovery_required":null,"reason":null}},"actions":{"recommended":null,"reason":"Task is ready to start"},"active_pr":null,"section":"available"},{"task":{"id":"9478fcdf-3771-4a39-9aeb-cf9c2f3f97b8","identifier":"LOO-269","name":"Stop durable Turn Basis from gating Task launch","description":"Outcome: Wave → Project → Task remains an intent graph, not a permission chain. A filed Task can gain durable Task Work when launched from an active Wave or Project even if the caller Run has no prior durable Turn Basis. Reproduce with Product/Auditability launching LOO-258: both the Project controller and direct Task route reject the launch with `has no durable Turn Basis for child control`, leaving no Task Work or worktree. Remove that ancestry-health gate while preserving stable Work identity and Run authority. Prove Wave- and Project-initiated launches without prior Turn Basis each create exactly one Task Work and worktree; retries do not duplicate Work; unauthorized external identity still fails for its real authentication reason. Do not repair, recreate, or broaden LOO-258 in this Task.","rank":1,"completed":true,"assignee":null},"reference":{"issue_url":"https://linear.app/loopflow/issue/LOO-269/stop-durable-turn-basis-from-gating-task-launch","workspace":null},"runtime":null,"next_move":{"owner":"project","reason":"Linear Task is complete"},"condition":{"state":"waiting","reason":"Linear Task is complete","observed_at":"2026-09-23T15:06:37.273384Z","evidence_age_secs":null,"local_progress":{"state":"not_applicable","unsettled":false,"dirty":null,"authored_commits":null,"recovery_required":null,"reason":null}},"actions":{"recommended":null,"reason":"Task is ready to start"},"active_pr":null,"section":"later"},{"task":{"id":"c484b752-05d5-4fea-af77-42ef66ce2569","identifier":"LOO-260","name":"Let resident Wave Turns open User Asks from durable invocation identity","description":"## Observed configured failure — 2026-08-21\n\nThe Product resident has a running Wave Run and lf ps shows an exact live provider launch beneath that resident, but the provider Turn environment has no LF_AGENT_INVOCATION_ID. When wave/pursue reached an authorized push boundary and ran lf ask --user, Ask creation failed immediately with: lf ask requires LF_AGENT_INVOCATION_ID from the active agent Turn. No Ask was created, so the headless root Work could neither obtain authority nor durably report the intervention through the required control path.\n\n## Outcome\n\nA provider Turn launched by a resident Wave can open one durable parent or User Ask using its actual durable Invocation identity. The caller never copies an Invocation id from status output and ambient environment never becomes Work authority.\n\n## Proof\n\n* An integration path launches a resident Wave Turn through the configured provider path, invokes lf ask --user, and creates exactly one Ask bound to the current durable Run and Turn.\n* The same proof covers parent routing from Project and Task Turns and User routing from a root Wave Turn.\n* Provider launch either propagates the exact durable Invocation identity or the control command resolves it from an authenticated execution receipt; arbitrary Run ids and unclaimed provider processes are rejected.\n* Missing identity fails at the launch boundary with an actionable settled receipt instead of leaving a working Turn unable to ask.\n* Restart and retry do not duplicate the Ask.\n\n## Boundaries\n\nDo not restore environment variables as the source of Work identity, infer authority from PID or session continuity, special-case Codex, or weaken first-writer-wins Ask settlement.","rank":2,"completed":true,"assignee":null},"reference":{"issue_url":"https://linear.app/loopflow/issue/LOO-260/let-resident-wave-turns-open-user-asks-from-durable-invocation","workspace":null},"runtime":null,"next_move":{"owner":"project","reason":"Linear Task is complete"},"condition":{"state":"waiting","reason":"Linear Task is complete","observed_at":"2026-09-23T15:06:37.273386Z","evidence_age_secs":null,"local_progress":{"state":"not_applicable","unsettled":false,"dirty":null,"authored_commits":null,"recovery_required":null,"reason":null}},"actions":{"recommended":null,"reason":"Task is ready to start"},"active_pr":null,"section":"later"},{"task":{"id":"ca54414e-7181-400c-98b3-89cc1c826805","identifier":"LOO-256","name":"Give resumed Project Runs durable child-control Turn Basis","description":"## Outcome\n\nA Wave Steer that relaunches an existing Project produces a Project Run with durable Turn Basis before that Project controls an immediate child Task. The Project can reserve the Task Run exactly once without weakening Work ancestry.\n\n## Observed configured failure — 2026-08-21\n\nLOO-248 reported the legal next action as resume. Direct Wave-to-Task control correctly refused because a Run may control only immediate child Work. The Wave then issued `lf project steer loopflow-api ...`; the Steer was durably recorded and relaunched Project Run `run_a857b30d87a34bae9ef80de57286287a`. That fresh Project Run failed while reserving the LOO-248 Task Run: `invalid control authority: Run run_a857b30d87a34bae9ef80de57286287a has no durable Turn Basis for child control`. LOO-248 remained ready on existing PR #1231. A prior Project Run failed at the same boundary, so this is convergent evidence rather than a one-off launch race.\n\n## Proof\n\n* An integration path starts or steers a stopped Project from its Wave, durably applies the Steer, and gives the resulting Project Run a valid Basis before immediate-child Task control.\n* The Project reserves or resumes the existing Task Run once; it creates no duplicate Task, worktree, Run, or PR.\n* The exact-authority rule remains: Wave Runs still cannot control Task Work directly, and no ambient environment or provider process becomes authority.\n* If a valid Basis cannot be established, status settles with one actionable non-convergence record rather than advertising resumable churn.\n* The configured Product path can steer Loopflow API to resume LOO-248 without outside terminal intervention.\n\n## Boundaries\n\nDo not restore Session-controller identity, weaken immediate-child ancestry, or special-case LOO-248. Preserve Work → Epoch → Run → Turn authority and fix the generic Project relaunch/control path.","rank":3,"completed":true,"assignee":null},"reference":{"issue_url":"https://linear.app/loopflow/issue/LOO-256/give-resumed-project-runs-durable-child-control-turn-basis","workspace":null},"runtime":null,"next_move":{"owner":"project","reason":"Linear Task is complete"},"condition":{"state":"waiting","reason":"Linear Task is complete","observed_at":"2026-09-23T15:06:37.273388Z","evidence_age_secs":null,"local_progress":{"state":"not_applicable","unsettled":false,"dirty":null,"authored_commits":null,"recovery_required":null,"reason":null}},"actions":{"recommended":null,"reason":"Task is ready to start"},"active_pr":null,"section":"later"},{"task":{"id":"2862d909-fb20-4a15-a7d1-54b5b242ec58","identifier":"LOO-252","name":"Run the skill as a command in human-gate Ask sessions (not an inlined prompt)","description":"Human-gate Ask sessions should run the skill as a COMMAND, not inline its prompt.\n\nPROBLEM: A User-targeted FlowStep Ask (e.g. the review-design human gate) launches an autonomous agent turn whose MAIN PROMPT is the skill's pre-rendered prompt. In rust/loopflow/src/task/runner.rs, `flow_step_ask_prompt` builds it via `prepare_interactive_harness_turn(skill, &seed, ...)` and wraps it with `human_flow_ask_prompt(...)`. The agent therefore just RUNS the skill and self-settles (reviews + approves the design without asking the user). PR #1222 (\"Preserve human reviewer mode\") patched this by injecting \"Reviewer mode: Human reviewer.\" — a band-aid on the wrong structure.\n\nDESIRED: The task agent's session should run the COMMAND `lf review-design` (i.e. invoke the skill through its own harness/flow), NOT receive the skill's rendered prompt as free text. Let the skill's real machinery drive the human gate. The session prompt becomes \"run `lf review-design` for this task step and settle via lf ask resolve/decline/release\", not the skill body inlined.\n\nSCOPE:\n\n* rust/loopflow/src/task/runner.rs: flow_step_ask_prompt / human_flow_ask_prompt — stop inlining prepare_interactive_harness_turn's output; make the session run the `lf <skill>` command.\n* Remove or supersede #1222's \"Human reviewer mode\" injection once the gate no longer runs the skill as an inline prompt.\n* Keep the explicit lf ask resolve/decline/release settlement contract.\n* Free-text (intervention) asks remain an ad-hoc side channel / extra context; they are NOT the pipeline mechanism.\n\nDONE WHEN: starting a real queued human FlowStep Ask launches a session whose recorded prompt invokes the `lf <skill>` command (not the inlined skill body), the design is not auto-approved without the user, and the reviewer-mode band-aid is gone.","rank":4,"completed":true,"assignee":null},"reference":{"issue_url":"https://linear.app/loopflow/issue/LOO-252/run-the-skill-as-a-command-in-human-gate-ask-sessions-not-an-inlined","workspace":{"slug":"run-the-skill-as-a","branch":"jack-heart/run-the-skill-as-a","worktree":"/Users/jack/src/loopflow.run-the-skill-as-a"}},"runtime":{"work_id":"task_4b178d2d59fd421a9f15c07f532f6311","project_id":"proj_9f1fc19a84211aed8b8136e55c8ab1f3","routing_project_id":"proj_9f1fc19a84211aed8b8136e55c8ab1f3","status":"abandoned","reason":"abandoned","updated_at":"2026-08-21T22:33:00Z","provider":"codex"},"next_move":{"owner":"project","reason":"abandoned"},"condition":{"state":"blocked","reason":"Task LOO-252 worktree /Users/jack/src/loopflow.run-the-skill-as-a is missing; restore that exact path before `lf task resume LOO-252`; Task identity and PR history are unchanged","observed_at":"2026-09-23T15:06:37.273492Z","evidence_age_secs":2824417,"local_progress":{"state":"missing","unsettled":true,"dirty":null,"authored_commits":null,"recovery_required":true,"reason":"Task LOO-252 worktree /Users/jack/src/loopflow.run-the-skill-as-a is missing; restore that exact path before `lf task resume LOO-252`; Task identity and PR history are unchanged"}},"actions":{"recommended":"no_action","reason":"Task is terminal"},"active_pr":null,"section":"later"},{"task":{"id":"fdb61a1a-1fe8-49d0-ac7f-27889ae22dda","identifier":"LOO-250","name":"Preserve human reviewer mode in Task Ask sessions","description":"Preserve human reviewer mode in Task Ask sessions\n\n<!-- loopflow-task-start:8c389e14a9126ea37138f1f45fcbb06429954889d2cc43beaafad5224d5c1410 -->","rank":5,"completed":true,"assignee":null},"reference":{"issue_url":"https://linear.app/loopflow/issue/LOO-250/preserve-human-reviewer-mode-in-task-ask-sessions","workspace":{"slug":"preserve-human-reviewer-mode-in","branch":"jack-heart/preserve-human-reviewer-mode-in","worktree":"/Users/jack/src/loopflow.preserve-human-reviewer-mode-in"}},"runtime":{"work_id":"task_692dabda6231427283db5bd73732d1e4","project_id":"proj_9f1fc19a84211aed8b8136e55c8ab1f3","routing_project_id":"proj_9f1fc19a84211aed8b8136e55c8ab1f3","status":"done","reason":"done","updated_at":"2026-08-21T19:01:16Z","provider":"codex"},"next_move":{"owner":"project","reason":"done"},"condition":{"state":"blocked","reason":"Task LOO-250 worktree /Users/jack/src/loopflow.preserve-human-reviewer-mode-in is missing; restore that exact path before `lf task resume LOO-250`; Task identity and PR history are unchanged","observed_at":"2026-09-23T15:06:37.274523Z","evidence_age_secs":2837121,"local_progress":{"state":"missing","unsettled":true,"dirty":null,"authored_commits":null,"recovery_required":true,"reason":"Task LOO-250 worktree /Users/jack/src/loopflow.preserve-human-reviewer-mode-in is missing; restore that exact path before `lf task resume LOO-250`; Task identity and PR history are unchanged"}},"actions":{"recommended":"no_action","reason":"Task is terminal"},"active_pr":null,"section":"later"},{"task":{"id":"477ab9fb-9de9-4604-bda8-5a1aca854bc0","identifier":"LOO-249","name":"Make Task PR copy explain intent and lifecycle","description":"Make Task PR copy explain intent and lifecycle\n\n<!-- loopflow-task-start:630594feb58b58caf4dff4e6ec77b979e4e7cefe7fbca29b1e6773c162ebb8bb -->","rank":6,"completed":true,"assignee":null},"reference":{"issue_url":"https://linear.app/loopflow/issue/LOO-249/make-task-pr-copy-explain-intent-and-lifecycle","workspace":{"slug":"make-task-pr-copy-explain","branch":"jack-heart/make-task-pr-copy-explain","worktree":"/Users/jack/src/loopflow.make-task-pr-copy-explain"}},"runtime":{"work_id":"task_61ac3c1d62e14bc3b5e4d0eed844c6fd","project_id":"proj_9f1fc19a84211aed8b8136e55c8ab1f3","routing_project_id":"proj_9f1fc19a84211aed8b8136e55c8ab1f3","status":"abandoned","reason":"abandoned","updated_at":"2026-08-21T22:32:53Z","provider":"codex"},"next_move":{"owner":"project","reason":"abandoned"},"condition":{"state":"blocked","reason":"Task LOO-249 worktree /Users/jack/src/loopflow.make-task-pr-copy-explain is missing; restore that exact path before `lf task resume LOO-249`; Task identity and PR history are unchanged","observed_at":"2026-09-23T15:06:37.275807Z","evidence_age_secs":2824424,"local_progress":{"state":"missing","unsettled":true,"dirty":null,"authored_commits":null,"recovery_required":true,"reason":"Task LOO-249 worktree /Users/jack/src/loopflow.make-task-pr-copy-explain is missing; restore that exact path before `lf task resume LOO-249`; Task identity and PR history are unchanged"}},"actions":{"recommended":"no_action","reason":"Task is terminal"},"active_pr":null,"section":"later"},{"task":{"id":"1700ca4d-7fbd-4e9f-bb76-895ccd9dcdd6","identifier":"LOO-248","name":"Make PR landing a watched CI-repair loop","description":"Make PR landing a watched CI-repair loop\n\n<!-- loopflow-task-start:6d719ee93e204df98ed8ff9574f03aa6dde6996185638d9f297d145d5ceb5654 -->","rank":7,"completed":true,"assignee":null},"reference":{"issue_url":"https://linear.app/loopflow/issue/LOO-248/make-pr-landing-a-watched-ci-repair-loop","workspace":{"slug":"make-pr-landing-a-watched","branch":"jack-heart/make-pr-landing-a-watched","worktree":"/Users/jack/src/loopflow.make-pr-landing-a-watched"}},"runtime":{"work_id":"task_c203d49b9468408db8998900367506e2","project_id":"proj_9f1fc19a84211aed8b8136e55c8ab1f3","routing_project_id":"proj_9f1fc19a84211aed8b8136e55c8ab1f3","status":"done","reason":"done","updated_at":"2026-08-22T04:59:59Z","provider":"codex"},"next_move":{"owner":"project","reason":"done"},"condition":{"state":"blocked","reason":"Task LOO-248 worktree /Users/jack/src/loopflow.make-pr-landing-a-watched is missing; restore that exact path before `lf task resume LOO-248`; Task identity and PR history are unchanged","observed_at":"2026-09-23T15:06:37.27637Z","evidence_age_secs":2801198,"local_progress":{"state":"missing","unsettled":true,"dirty":null,"authored_commits":null,"recovery_required":true,"reason":"Task LOO-248 worktree /Users/jack/src/loopflow.make-pr-landing-a-watched is missing; restore that exact path before `lf task resume LOO-248`; Task identity and PR history are unchanged"}},"actions":{"recommended":"no_action","reason":"Task is terminal"},"active_pr":null,"section":"later"},{"task":{"id":"3a1d0c34-911a-42e7-8328-9683b62fa357","identifier":"LOO-247","name":"Refuse human-submit inside managed Task worktrees","description":"Recover and finish the committed LOO-162 sequence-2 slice on a lifecycle that can settle. Managed Task worktrees must refuse pr submit before mutation because their finally review is the sole shipping decision; ordinary non-Task submit remains unchanged. Preserve the existing SHA-pinned land path and do not revive the obsolete InteractionReview architecture. Proof: managed refusal and ordinary submit behavior, updated prompt goldens and user docs teaching publish then land, focused Rust tests, and a real CLI refusal before landing. Start this replacement with the fix cycle and stack it on LOO-162 so its committed implementation is preserved; retire LOO-162 only after that binding exists.","rank":8,"completed":true,"assignee":null},"reference":{"issue_url":"https://linear.app/loopflow/issue/LOO-247/refuse-human-submit-inside-managed-task-worktrees","workspace":{"slug":"refuse-human-submit-inside-managed","branch":"jack-heart/refuse-human-submit-inside-managed","worktree":"/Users/jack/src/loopflow.refuse-human-submit-inside-managed"}},"runtime":{"work_id":"task_c15c85ecd2834344bd88f26f78a25e02","project_id":"proj_9f1fc19a84211aed8b8136e55c8ab1f3","routing_project_id":"proj_9f1fc19a84211aed8b8136e55c8ab1f3","status":"abandoned","reason":"abandoned","updated_at":"2026-08-28T23:08:39Z","provider":"codex"},"next_move":{"owner":"project","reason":"abandoned"},"condition":{"state":"blocked","reason":"Task LOO-247 worktree /Users/jack/src/loopflow.refuse-human-submit-inside-managed is missing; restore that exact path on branch \"jack-heart/refuse-human-submit-inside-managed\" before `lf task resume LOO-247`; Task identity and PR history are unchanged","observed_at":"2026-09-23T15:06:37.27735Z","evidence_age_secs":2217478,"local_progress":{"state":"missing","unsettled":true,"dirty":null,"authored_commits":null,"recovery_required":true,"reason":"Task LOO-247 worktree /Users/jack/src/loopflow.refuse-human-submit-inside-managed is missing; restore that exact path on branch \"jack-heart/refuse-human-submit-inside-managed\" before `lf task resume LOO-247`; Task identity and PR history are unchanged"}},"actions":{"recommended":"no_action","reason":"Task is terminal"},"active_pr":{"id":"pr_d45d747cd81644de98a7aee54dfc88e0","sequence":1,"slug":"refuse-human-submit-inside-managed","branch":"jack-heart/refuse-human-submit-inside-managed","base_commit":"696082a9b1817f192aadfe002ef2252fbc437cb6","phase":"working","empty":null,"publication":null,"merge_commit":null,"abandoned_at":null},"section":"later"},{"task":{"id":"8161e183-5109-4a76-b35e-520fa0e2158e","identifier":"LOO-244","name":"Refuse human-submit inside managed Task worktrees","description":"Refuse human-submit inside managed Task worktrees\n\n<!-- loopflow-task-start:a99e8ed180014711e12baee5dad3a6de732a51ed494e7cea251c5fffd77ef7db -->","rank":9,"completed":true,"assignee":null},"reference":{"issue_url":"https://linear.app/loopflow/issue/LOO-244/refuse-human-submit-inside-managed-task-worktrees","workspace":null},"runtime":null,"next_move":{"owner":"project","reason":"Linear Task is complete"},"condition":{"state":"waiting","reason":"Linear Task is complete","observed_at":"2026-09-23T15:06:37.279608Z","evidence_age_secs":null,"local_progress":{"state":"not_applicable","unsettled":false,"dirty":null,"authored_commits":null,"recovery_required":null,"reason":null}},"actions":{"recommended":null,"reason":"Task is ready to start"},"active_pr":null,"section":"later"},{"task":{"id":"692952c0-a99f-4e0e-a7e2-23adf9f962ed","identifier":"LOO-235","name":"Define Project-owned live metrics for KR-driven Wave health","description":"Define Project-owned live metrics for KR-driven Wave health\n\n<!-- loopflow-task-start:02a59cccf082f550c59428601b0cbcfb1e5a7354718e7c9fdeeeceac873b34d1 -->","rank":10,"completed":true,"assignee":null},"reference":{"issue_url":"https://linear.app/loopflow/issue/LOO-235/define-project-owned-live-metrics-for-kr-driven-wave-health","workspace":{"slug":"define-project-owned-live-metrics","branch":"jack-heart/define-project-owned-live-metrics","worktree":"/Users/jack/src/loopflow.define-project-owned-live-metrics"}},"runtime":{"work_id":"task_8840cd0674e240a09ae30991bbf68dfa","project_id":"proj_9f1fc19a84211aed8b8136e55c8ab1f3","routing_project_id":"proj_9f1fc19a84211aed8b8136e55c8ab1f3","status":"done","reason":"done","updated_at":"2026-08-22T00:45:58Z","provider":"codex"},"next_move":{"owner":"project","reason":"done"},"condition":{"state":"blocked","reason":"Task LOO-235 worktree /Users/jack/src/loopflow.define-project-owned-live-metrics is missing; restore that exact path before `lf task resume LOO-235`; Task identity and PR history are unchanged","observed_at":"2026-09-23T15:06:37.279682Z","evidence_age_secs":2816439,"local_progress":{"state":"missing","unsettled":true,"dirty":null,"authored_commits":null,"recovery_required":true,"reason":"Task LOO-235 worktree /Users/jack/src/loopflow.define-project-owned-live-metrics is missing; restore that exact path before `lf task resume LOO-235`; Task identity and PR history are unchanged"}},"actions":{"recommended":"no_action","reason":"Task is terminal"},"active_pr":null,"section":"later"},{"task":{"id":"3f20e6ce-a9a8-4f8f-8b40-6e83a292774b","identifier":"LOO-238","name":"Keep concurrent trace capture from killing Task Runs","description":"Observed 2026-08-20 while LOO-234, LOO-235, and LOO-237 ran concurrently. LOO-237 established a real Task Run and provider invocation, then trace persistence hit `sqlite error: database is locked`. The capture marked itself partial; the next turn failed with `trace capture is already partial`, ending the Task ready/resumable with no process. A fresh Run constructs a fresh capture, but resuming before contention semantics are repaired can repeat the failure.\n\nUser contract:\n\n* Routine concurrent Wave, Project, and Task trace writes do not terminate otherwise healthy Work.\n* Trace persistence acquires write authority with bounded contention behavior across every multi-statement capture path; no deferred read-to-write upgrade bypasses the busy timeout.\n* If capture truly cannot continue, preserve the partial trace and settle the Run once with an actionable reason instead of advertising blind resume churn.\n* The Task, worktree, provider continuity, and PR remain attributable through recovery.\n\nProof:\n\n* A deterministic SQLite contention test drives concurrent multi-turn captures through start, turn transition, receipt updates, and finish without `database is locked`.\n* A persistent-failure test proves one truthful terminal boundary and a preserved partial trace.\n* Replaying the LOO-237-shaped path starts a fresh capture without duplicating Work or losing causal failure history.","rank":11,"completed":true,"assignee":null},"reference":{"issue_url":"https://linear.app/loopflow/issue/LOO-238/keep-concurrent-trace-capture-from-killing-task-runs","workspace":{"slug":"keep-concurrent-trace-capture-from","branch":"jack-heart/keep-concurrent-trace-capture-from","worktree":"/Users/jack/src/loopflow.keep-concurrent-trace-capture-from"}},"runtime":{"work_id":"task_a445483e8b5447318ae91b36e24b4923","project_id":"proj_9f1fc19a84211aed8b8136e55c8ab1f3","routing_project_id":"proj_9f1fc19a84211aed8b8136e55c8ab1f3","status":"done","reason":"done","updated_at":"2026-08-21T22:47:04Z","provider":"codex"},"next_move":{"owner":"project","reason":"done"},"condition":{"state":"blocked","reason":"Task LOO-238 worktree /Users/jack/src/loopflow.keep-concurrent-trace-capture-from is missing; restore that exact path before `lf task resume LOO-238`; Task identity and PR history are unchanged","observed_at":"2026-09-23T15:06:37.280814Z","evidence_age_secs":2823573,"local_progress":{"state":"missing","unsettled":true,"dirty":null,"authored_commits":null,"recovery_required":true,"reason":"Task LOO-238 worktree /Users/jack/src/loopflow.keep-concurrent-trace-capture-from is missing; restore that exact path before `lf task resume LOO-238`; Task identity and PR history are unchanged"}},"actions":{"recommended":"no_action","reason":"Task is terminal"},"active_pr":null,"section":"later"},{"task":{"id":"342cf819-23a9-44e4-939d-cbe8f432d786","identifier":"LOO-236","name":"Present Ask sessions as native Ghostty tabs in one window","description":"Present Ask sessions as native Ghostty tabs in one window\n\n<!-- loopflow-task-start:619bcb11c61f3afe10f8b3b1b6b1f878ec0990e0091bf29a3c0760cb934f374c -->","rank":12,"completed":true,"assignee":null},"reference":{"issue_url":"https://linear.app/loopflow/issue/LOO-236/present-ask-sessions-as-native-ghostty-tabs-in-one-window","workspace":null},"runtime":null,"next_move":{"owner":"project","reason":"Linear Task is complete"},"condition":{"state":"waiting","reason":"Linear Task is complete","observed_at":"2026-09-23T15:06:37.28163Z","evidence_age_secs":null,"local_progress":{"state":"not_applicable","unsettled":false,"dirty":null,"authored_commits":null,"recovery_required":null,"reason":null}},"actions":{"recommended":null,"reason":"Task is ready to start"},"active_pr":null,"section":"later"},{"task":{"id":"dc74191c-4f87-4364-8d79-5fa5227c7cf9","identifier":"LOO-237","name":"Carry Run execution context across User, Wave, and Project runners","description":"Observed across [LOO-226](https://linear.app/loopflow/issue/LOO-226/install-local-builds-without-destroying-live-work), [LOO-229](https://linear.app/loopflow/issue/LOO-229/status-surfaces-must-distinguish-last-recorded-event-from-current), and LOO-240: each Task runner launches a harness, then records a non-resumable failure because trace_capture_context() finds no active RunContext. The CLI establishes journal::RUN_CONTEXT as thread-local state, while WorkRunner uses Runtime::new().block_on(run_work); execution may continue on a Tokio worker thread where the process context is absent. Project runner can drop the same missing capture silently. Outcome: pass one explicit, exact Run execution context through User, Project, and Task Work runners across async thread changes; establish it before provider launch; preserve Run/process identity and authority without inferring from environment or minting a second context; and give Project and Task runners the same fail-closed semantics. Proof: a production-shaped multithreaded __work fixture runs Project and Task bodies with trace capture bound to the supervising Run, records no duplicate Exec/Turn receipts, and demonstrates that genuinely absent or mismatched context fails before harness launch with an actionable error. This Task absorbs [LOO-243](https://linear.app/loopflow/issue/LOO-243/carry-run-execution-context-across-async-work-runners) and preserves the existing [LOO-237](https://linear.app/loopflow/issue/LOO-237/carry-run-execution-context-across-user-wave-and-project-runners) worktree changes. It remains distinct from [LOO-227](https://linear.app/loopflow/issue/LOO-227/let-project-runs-resume-child-tasks-with-durable-control-authority), which owns durable Project-to-child control Basis.","rank":13,"completed":true,"assignee":null},"reference":{"issue_url":"https://linear.app/loopflow/issue/LOO-237/carry-run-execution-context-across-user-wave-and-project-runners","workspace":{"slug":"restore-task-launch-from-user","branch":"jack-heart/restore-task-launch-from-user","worktree":"/Users/jack/src/loopflow.restore-task-launch-from-user"}},"runtime":{"work_id":"task_21b193b0ee3b4c70afd1dcb025dc6589","project_id":"proj_9f1fc19a84211aed8b8136e55c8ab1f3","routing_project_id":"proj_9f1fc19a84211aed8b8136e55c8ab1f3","status":"done","reason":"done","updated_at":"2026-08-21T18:29:24Z","provider":"codex"},"next_move":{"owner":"project","reason":"done"},"condition":{"state":"blocked","reason":"Task LOO-237 worktree /Users/jack/src/loopflow.restore-task-launch-from-user is missing; restore that exact path before `lf task resume LOO-237`; Task identity and PR history are unchanged","observed_at":"2026-09-23T15:06:37.281681Z","evidence_age_secs":2839033,"local_progress":{"state":"missing","unsettled":true,"dirty":null,"authored_commits":null,"recovery_required":true,"reason":"Task LOO-237 worktree /Users/jack/src/loopflow.restore-task-launch-from-user is missing; restore that exact path before `lf task resume LOO-237`; Task identity and PR history are unchanged"}},"actions":{"recommended":"no_action","reason":"Task is terminal"},"active_pr":null,"section":"later"},{"task":{"id":"61abef00-43fc-41bc-a4b3-3e91a7fcbbd3","identifier":"LOO-230","name":"Remove skill capability frontmatter from Task lifecycle validation","description":"Remove skill capability frontmatter from Task lifecycle validation\n\n<!-- loopflow-task-start:d3874c6b4eaa9886ae03555d459228c67314da53174a02559876cc82f3271e9b -->","rank":14,"completed":true,"assignee":null},"reference":{"issue_url":"https://linear.app/loopflow/issue/LOO-230/remove-skill-capability-frontmatter-from-task-lifecycle-validation","workspace":{"slug":"remove-skill-capability-frontmatter-from","branch":"jack-heart/remove-skill-capability-frontmatter-from","worktree":"/Users/jack/src/loopflow.remove-skill-capability-frontmatter-from"}},"runtime":{"work_id":"task_7fdfb94cfe654fafbcf6777a2e162213","project_id":"proj_9f1fc19a84211aed8b8136e55c8ab1f3","routing_project_id":"proj_9f1fc19a84211aed8b8136e55c8ab1f3","status":"abandoned","reason":"abandoned","updated_at":"2026-08-21T17:24:10Z","provider":"codex"},"next_move":{"owner":"project","reason":"abandoned"},"condition":{"state":"blocked","reason":"Task LOO-230 worktree /Users/jack/src/loopflow.remove-skill-capability-frontmatter-from is missing; restore that exact path before `lf task resume LOO-230`; Task identity and PR history are unchanged","observed_at":"2026-09-23T15:06:37.284093Z","evidence_age_secs":2842947,"local_progress":{"state":"missing","unsettled":true,"dirty":null,"authored_commits":null,"recovery_required":true,"reason":"Task LOO-230 worktree /Users/jack/src/loopflow.remove-skill-capability-frontmatter-from is missing; restore that exact path before `lf task resume LOO-230`; Task identity and PR history are unchanged"}},"actions":{"recommended":"no_action","reason":"Task is terminal"},"active_pr":null,"section":"later"},{"task":{"id":"06f8790a-33a1-48d3-8d7e-684693c79b36","identifier":"LOO-223","name":"Headless Chrome capture jobs hijack the user's browser when they outlive their run","description":"Headless Chrome capture jobs hijack the user's browser when they outlive their run\n\nA podium-review screenshot job left `Google Chrome --headless=new --no-startup-window --screenshot=scratch/podium-review/html-mobile.png --user-data-dir=/tmp/loopflow-podium-mobile.D8pMr8` running orphaned (ppid 1) for 5h37m on 2026-08-19. While it lived, the user could not open Chrome at all: LaunchServices routes 'open Chrome' to the existing bundle instance, and the headless instance shows no windows. This also breaks lf auth connect ceremonies, which depend on opening Chrome profiles.\n\nFix direction: whatever spawns headless Chrome for captures must bound its lifetime (timeout + kill on parent exit, same pattern as AuthProcessGroup in provider_auth), and should prefer a capture path that does not claim the user-facing Chrome bundle instance (chrome-headless-shell, or open -na with a throwaway instance). Sweep: find every headless-Chrome spawn site in the repo and apply the same lifetime bound.\n\nDone when: killing the parent mid-capture leaves no Chrome process behind (demo with ps); a capture running concurrently with a user's Chrome session neither blocks opening Chrome nor steals its instance; the spawn-site sweep is enumerated in the PR notes.\n\n<!-- loopflow-task-start:d8998338c0123fbfd77835973503b08514ea7fdc424f829b71e6e54c78fd2085 -->","rank":15,"completed":true,"assignee":null},"reference":{"issue_url":"https://linear.app/loopflow/issue/LOO-223/headless-chrome-capture-jobs-hijack-the-users-browser-when-they","workspace":{"slug":"headless-chrome-capture-jobs-hijack","branch":"jack-heart/headless-chrome-capture-jobs-hijack","worktree":"/Users/jack/src/loopflow.headless-chrome-capture-jobs-hijack"}},"runtime":{"work_id":"task_d0fa47e3ccb24002adf1892dab352a32","project_id":"proj_9f1fc19a84211aed8b8136e55c8ab1f3","routing_project_id":"proj_9f1fc19a84211aed8b8136e55c8ab1f3","status":"abandoned","reason":"abandoned","updated_at":"2026-08-20T04:48:09Z","provider":"codex"},"next_move":{"owner":"project","reason":"refresh reviewer-facing PR copy for the current head before settlement"},"condition":{"state":"blocked","reason":"Task LOO-223 worktree /Users/jack/src/loopflow.headless-chrome-capture-jobs-hijack is missing; restore that exact path on branch \"jack-heart/headless-chrome-capture-jobs-hijack\" before `lf task resume LOO-223`; Task identity and PR history are unchanged","observed_at":"2026-09-23T15:06:37.286367Z","evidence_age_secs":2974708,"local_progress":{"state":"missing","unsettled":true,"dirty":null,"authored_commits":null,"recovery_required":true,"reason":"Task LOO-223 worktree /Users/jack/src/loopflow.headless-chrome-capture-jobs-hijack is missing; restore that exact path on branch \"jack-heart/headless-chrome-capture-jobs-hijack\" before `lf task resume LOO-223`; Task identity and PR history are unchanged"}},"actions":{"recommended":"no_action","reason":"Task is terminal"},"active_pr":{"id":"pr_fa79e991baea4ee0b6320581fc53cfb6","sequence":1,"slug":"headless-chrome-capture-jobs-hijack","branch":"jack-heart/headless-chrome-capture-jobs-hijack","base_commit":"bcea828c8bd29fe40c1365720c0938a7e2459acd","phase":"open","empty":null,"publication":{"requested_at":"2026-08-20T01:04:05Z","presentation":null,"github":{"number":1204,"url":"https://github.com/loopflowstudio/loopflow/pull/1204"},"merge":{"mode":"auto","requested_at":"2026-08-20T08:50:15Z","head_sha":"d6e4de934d9a07157beb0d37a95bdb2e0c4a2d67","after_merge":"continue_task","next_slug":null}},"merge_commit":null,"abandoned_at":null},"section":"later"},{"task":{"id":"90a0f387-7ba4-4b96-a50f-b7724218e170","identifier":"LOO-222","name":"[absorbed] Fix Chrome focus stealing and login-server teardown","description":"Hotfix lf auth connect: stop 1 Hz Chrome focus-stealing and the 180s login-server teardown\n\nTwo defects in the managed login ceremony (`lf auth connect`), observed live on 0.12.8 while reconnecting accounts. Both block account recovery, which blocks wave/project runners fleet-wide.\n\nDefect 1 — focus stealing (claude path):\n`capture_claude_authorization_code_from_chrome` (rust/loopflow/src/provider_auth/mod.rs:1828) polls in a loop until CLAUDE_BROWSER_AUTH_TIMEOUT, executing CLAUDE_VISIBLE_PAGE_SCRIPT ([mod.rs:1864](<http://mod.rs:1864>)) every 1 second. Each iteration unconditionally runs:\n\n* `tell application \"Google Chrome\" to activate` — yanks Chrome to the foreground every second, regardless of whether the auth window exists yet\n* `perform action \"AXRaise\"` + synthesized `keystroke \"a\"/\"c\" using command down` — Cmd+A/Cmd+C land in whatever the user is typing in if focus shifts mid-delay\n* clipboard save/restore each poll — races with any user copy during the ceremony\n\nThe user cannot use their machine while the ceremony runs. Fix direction: never `activate` in the poll loop. Query window existence passively (System Events window enumeration needs no activation); only when the matching \"Authentication code | Claude Platform (<profile>)\" window is present, do one activate+raise+copy pass. Better still, prefer reading the page without synthetic keystrokes if Chrome scripting allows.\n\nDefect 2 — premature login-server teardown (codex path, reproduced today):\n`connect` for authorization flows waits `tokio::time::timeout(AUTH_STATUS_POLL_TIMEOUT, handle.wait())` with AUTH_STATUS_POLL_TIMEOUT = 180s (lf/commands/auth.rs:36,379). On timeout, lf exits; the `.login-` tempdir drops and the AuthProcessGroup Drop (provider_auth/mod.rs:1798) SIGKILLs the codex login process group — including its localhost:1455 OAuth callback listener. A user still completing browser login then gets redirected to [http://localhost:1455/auth/callback?](<http://localhost:1455/auth/callback?>)... and sees ERR_CONNECTION_REFUSED (reproduced 2026-08-19 with [manabot-eng@loopflow.studio](<mailto:manabot-eng@loopflow.studio>); nothing listening on 1455 afterward). The authorization code is orphaned and the account stays credential_state=missing.\n\n180 seconds is far too short for a real login (password manager, 2FA, SSO redirects), and there is no env/config override (`wait_for_active_status` only honors provider expires_in). Fix direction: for interactive browser confirmation, wait the authorization-code flow window (AUTH_CODE_FLOW_TIMEOUT_SECS = 600 exists already at [auth.rs:40](<http://auth.rs:40>)) or until Ctrl-C, and print a clear \"still waiting for browser approval (Ns elapsed)\" heartbeat so the user knows the listener is alive.\n\nDone when:\n\n* During a claude connect ceremony, Chrome is activated at most once before the auth window exists and once to harvest the code; the user can type in another app for the entire poll window without losing focus or keystrokes (manual demo on macOS).\n* A codex connect survives a slow login: with approval deliberately delayed past 3 minutes, the localhost callback still lands, the account flips to connected, and `lf usage` shows it. Reproduce the old behavior's failure in a test at the timeout boundary if feasible without a live provider.\n* `lf auth connect codex manabot-eng@loopflow.studio` completes on this machine (the account invalidated since Aug 14 — the live victim).\n\n<!-- loopflow-task-start:64e413e9cfa527f6343ffd7659325757a2419f5b7bee089b2072418bc5955d3b -->\n\n## Consolidation\n\nAbsorbed into LOO-223. LOO-223 owns both bounded headless-Chrome capture lifetime and the authentication focus/callback acceptance cases from this Task.","rank":16,"completed":true,"assignee":null},"reference":{"issue_url":"https://linear.app/loopflow/issue/LOO-222/absorbed-fix-chrome-focus-stealing-and-login-server-teardown","workspace":{"slug":"hotfix-lf-auth-connect-stop","branch":"jack-heart/hotfix-lf-auth-connect-stop","worktree":"/Users/jack/src/loopflow.hotfix-lf-auth-connect-stop"}},"runtime":{"work_id":"task_13eedfbbb59a489685c5f41737ec6f14","project_id":"proj_9f1fc19a84211aed8b8136e55c8ab1f3","routing_project_id":"proj_9f1fc19a84211aed8b8136e55c8ab1f3","status":"abandoned","reason":"abandoned","updated_at":"2026-08-20T01:14:06Z","provider":"codex"},"next_move":{"owner":"project","reason":"abandoned"},"condition":{"state":"blocked","reason":"Task LOO-222 worktree /Users/jack/src/loopflow.hotfix-lf-auth-connect-stop is missing; restore that exact path before `lf task resume LOO-222`; Task identity and PR history are unchanged","observed_at":"2026-09-23T15:06:37.287143Z","evidence_age_secs":2987551,"local_progress":{"state":"missing","unsettled":true,"dirty":null,"authored_commits":null,"recovery_required":true,"reason":"Task LOO-222 worktree /Users/jack/src/loopflow.hotfix-lf-auth-connect-stop is missing; restore that exact path before `lf task resume LOO-222`; Task identity and PR history are unchanged"}},"actions":{"recommended":"no_action","reason":"Task is terminal"},"active_pr":null,"section":"later"},{"task":{"id":"c2c91762-3d29-4018-b962-e2eb709daeb6","identifier":"LOO-225","name":"Make Task lifecycle selection match the work it must finish","description":"Make Task lifecycle selection match the work it must finish\n\n<!-- loopflow-task-start:e1f89980ba9856e18a41186e7c516e21a5aa9365389e4dd972acaca22bdcd484 -->","rank":17,"completed":true,"assignee":null},"reference":{"issue_url":"https://linear.app/loopflow/issue/LOO-225/make-task-lifecycle-selection-match-the-work-it-must-finish","workspace":{"slug":"lifecycle-capability-contract","branch":"jack-heart/lifecycle-capability-contract","worktree":"/Users/jack/src/loopflow.lifecycle-capability-contract"}},"runtime":{"work_id":"task_b198050f6d7e443c8e02c5e51d0c1c2f","project_id":"proj_9f1fc19a84211aed8b8136e55c8ab1f3","routing_project_id":"proj_9f1fc19a84211aed8b8136e55c8ab1f3","status":"done","reason":"done","updated_at":"2026-08-20T05:58:14Z","provider":"codex"},"next_move":{"owner":"project","reason":"done"},"condition":{"state":"blocked","reason":"Task LOO-225 worktree /Users/jack/src/loopflow.lifecycle-capability-contract is missing; restore that exact path before `lf task resume LOO-225`; Task identity and PR history are unchanged","observed_at":"2026-09-23T15:06:37.288043Z","evidence_age_secs":2970503,"local_progress":{"state":"missing","unsettled":true,"dirty":null,"authored_commits":null,"recovery_required":true,"reason":"Task LOO-225 worktree /Users/jack/src/loopflow.lifecycle-capability-contract is missing; restore that exact path before `lf task resume LOO-225`; Task identity and PR history are unchanged"}},"actions":{"recommended":"no_action","reason":"Task is terminal"},"active_pr":null,"section":"later"},{"task":{"id":"ae8c7122-991a-4c1f-920e-5225b9f03055","identifier":"LOO-220","name":"Make release upgrades converge on an always-on Home","description":"# 5 Whys: An always-on Home cannot install a migration-bearing release\n\n## The Problem\n\nInstalling the latest published release was refused because nine Runs were\nnon-ended, but an always-on Loopflow Home may never naturally reach zero Runs.\n\n## Chain\n\nAlways-on Home cannot update -> every non-ended Run blocks migration -> install\nhas no quiesce/resume protocol -> the safety fix assumed a manual zero-Run\nwindow -> installation is modeled as file replacement rather than Home\nreconciliation.\n\n**Problem**: The machine remained on `lf 0.12.4` while the Product demo needed\nthe `0.12.5` store frontier. Installing the published `v0.12.5` artifact found\nnine active or stopping Runs and changed nothing.\n\n**Why 1**: A migration-bearing promotion rejects every Run whose durable state\nis not `ended`; the check does not mean an old process is currently writing.\n\n**Why 2**: The installer can fence new Run reservations, but it cannot ask\nresident Work to checkpoint, drain its process containment, or resume afterward.\n\n**Why 3**: Promotion was hardened after a branch binary was installed behind an\nincompatible shared-store frontier. The prevention correctly fails closed, but\nits only safe state is a manually drained machine.\n\n**Why 4**: At that point Loopflow did not have sufficiently durable desired\non/off state and restart reconciliation to preserve user intent through a\ncoordinated control-plane restart.\n\n**Why 5 (Root)**: Updating Loopflow is treated as replacing CLI/daemon/app files\nplus migrating SQLite, not as a Home operation that converges enabled Work onto\na new runtime generation.\n\n## Unanswered Whys\n\n| Branch Point | Unexplored Question | Priority |\n| -- | -- | -- |\n| Why 1 | Which non-ended Runs have live old-code containment, and which are only durable pursuit state? | High |\n| Why 2 | What is the safe checkpoint boundary for Wave, Project, and Task Runs? | High |\n| Why 3 | Which release migrations can remain backward-compatible for a rolling upgrade? | Medium |\n| Why 4 | How should remote Homes coordinate a fleet update without a global outage? | Medium |\n\n## Fixes\n\n| Level | Fix | Prevents |\n| -- | -- | -- |\n| Immediate | Make the normal production updater download and promote the latest published artifact, exactly like an external install; keep current-main builds dev-local. | Maintainers accidentally treating unreleased `main` as production. |\n| Structural | Add a migration upgrade operation that fences new Runs, checkpoints and drains live containment, promotes and migrates, then reconciles enabled Work. | Requiring a human to manufacture a zero-Run window. |\n| Systemic | Treat runtime generation and upgrade state as Home reconciliation facts with durable receipts and restart policy. | Always-on operation and safe upgrades remaining contradictory goals. |\n\n## Changes to Implement\n\n- [ ] Replace main-pulling production refresh with latest-published-release\n  resolution and the same signed-artifact promotion path external users take.\n- [ ] Preserve an explicit dev-only source-build command that cannot become the\n  production runtime while migration drafts exist.\n- [ ] Distinguish durable non-ended Work from live old-generation process\n  containment in promotion evidence.\n- [ ] Persist Home upgrade intent and block new Run reservations for the old\n  generation.\n- [ ] Checkpoint and stop live Wave, Project, and Task bodies without changing\n  their enabled flags, definitions, worktrees, or PM state.\n- [ ] Promote CLI, daemon, and app; advance the migration frontier; restart the\n  Home; reconcile every enabled Work item.\n- [ ] Emit a typed receipt for drain, migration, restart, resumed Work, timeout,\n  and rollback/failure state.\n- [ ] Prove a migration-bearing release on an active Wave/Project/Task fixture\n  resumes the same Work without an operator-created zero-Run window.","rank":18,"completed":true,"assignee":null},"reference":{"issue_url":"https://linear.app/loopflow/issue/LOO-220/make-release-upgrades-converge-on-an-always-on-home","workspace":{"slug":"make-release-upgrades-converge-on","branch":"jack-heart/make-release-upgrades-converge-on-2","worktree":"/Users/jack/src/loopflow.make-release-upgrades-converge-on"}},"runtime":{"work_id":"task_b76dc013c62145d785dc6c0366e709f2","project_id":"proj_9f1fc19a84211aed8b8136e55c8ab1f3","routing_project_id":"proj_9f1fc19a84211aed8b8136e55c8ab1f3","status":"abandoned","reason":"abandoned","updated_at":"2026-07-23T04:06:46Z","provider":"codex"},"next_move":{"owner":"project","reason":"abandoned"},"condition":{"state":"blocked","reason":"Task LOO-220 worktree /Users/jack/src/loopflow.make-release-upgrades-converge-on is missing; restore that exact path before `lf task resume LOO-220`; Task identity and PR history are unchanged","observed_at":"2026-09-23T15:06:37.288992Z","evidence_age_secs":5396391,"local_progress":{"state":"missing","unsettled":true,"dirty":null,"authored_commits":null,"recovery_required":true,"reason":"Task LOO-220 worktree /Users/jack/src/loopflow.make-release-upgrades-converge-on is missing; restore that exact path before `lf task resume LOO-220`; Task identity and PR history are unchanged"}},"actions":{"recommended":"no_action","reason":"Task is terminal"},"active_pr":null,"section":"later"},{"task":{"id":"ec89bd9f-aac9-4305-9e9b-a1aec0c0612d","identifier":"LOO-162","name":"Make LLM-session checkpoints authoritative for Task landing","description":"## Problem\n\nManaged Task work currently teaches two incompatible human surfaces. LOOPFLOW.md presents `lf pr submit` plus a GitHub merge click as the human shipping gate, while the Task lifecycle already creates durable interactive reviews inside provider-backed LLM sessions.\n\nThe lifecycle model is broader than one final Gate. Any `interactive: true` step in Kickoff, Iterate, or Gate may use `InteractionPolicy::Require` and block on a human in the existing LLM transcript. `Defer` assigns that same exercise to the owning Project LLM session. Therefore require/require/require, require/defer/require, and defer/defer/defer are all legitimate authored policies; they are not migration states to normalize.\n\nGitHub UI review and a human merge click duplicate this model without its evidence, phase ownership, changes-requested transition, or recovery semantics. Conversely, arming `land` during Iterate can let merge outrun later required LLM-session checkpoints.\n\n## User-visible outcome\n\nA human conducts every required Task checkpoint by conversing in an LLM session, whether the checkpoint appears during Kickoff, Iterate, or Gate. The Task remains parked at that exact lifecycle step until the durable InteractionReview disposition resolves it. Project-deferred checkpoints happen through the Project LLM session using the same review protocol.\n\nManaged Tasks never require the GitHub UI for review or merge. Agents publish PRs as evidence while work is in flight. Once the Task lifecycle has cleared every applicable required interaction, its approved settlement intent still matches current Task and PR evidence, and repository checks permit merging, Loopflow lands the PR mechanically. `changes-requested` resumes the correct owning phase without merge.\n\n`submit` and `pr open` remain available only outside managed Tasks or when a human explicitly asks to inspect GitHub; neither is part of the managed Task lifecycle.\n\n## End-to-end proof\n\nExercise managed Tasks against a real test repository and shared store:\n\n1. A required Kickoff interaction parks in the Task provider transcript. Human follow-ups stay FIFO in that transcript; approval advances and changes-requested does not silently skip the Kickoff checkpoint.\n2. A Task whose Iterate plan is `Require` parks on an interactive inner-flow step and cannot publish settlement or arm merge until that review resolves. A `Defer` Iterate routes the same exercise to the Project provider transcript.\n3. Required Gate interactions run in the Task provider transcript. Changes-requested returns the same Session to Iterate; approval permits settlement only when the reviewed fingerprint remains current.\n4. No managed path opens GitHub or waits for a human merge click. Iterate may call `lf pr publish`; `lf pr submit` and premature `lf pr land` are refused or excluded from Task prompts before lifecycle approval.\n5. After all required lifecycle reviews clear, one replay-safe landing uses the recorded `-c` or `--next <slug>` disposition. CI failure keeps the PR open and invokes the existing repair lifecycle; green CI lets the merge queue settle it.\n6. Restart during an LLM review or between final approval and land preserves the transcript, phase, disposition, and exactly-once landing action.\n\nProve this with focused Task runner/store/PR-operation tests and a CLI-level lifecycle exercise spanning required Kickoff, required Iterate, required Gate, changes-requested, restart, approval, and merge.\n\n## Source of truth\n\nThe authoritative state is TaskLifecyclePlan and its per-phase InteractionPolicy, the phase cursor, durable InteractionReview conversation/disposition/evidence, TaskGateProposal settlement intent, and TaskPr publication/after-merge disposition. LLM prompts, CLI/Mac status, and recommended actions are derived views. GitHub review state is repository evidence, not human lifecycle authority.\n\n## Affected surfaces and consumers\n\n* Task runner transitions and review resumption in Kickoff, Iterate, and Gate\n* Human and Project reviewer protocols in the existing provider-backed transcripts\n* TaskGateProposal and TaskPr settlement intent, including replay-safe complete-versus-next landing\n* Task-worktree authority for `lf pr publish`, `submit`, `open`, and `land`\n* LOOPFLOW.md; task_clarify, task_pursue, task_mutate, review-design, demo, code-review, gate, land, and submit skills\n* `lf task attach`, review message/reply/complete commands, Mac handoff presentation, status, and recommended actions\n* CLI help, README, operations documentation, builtin prompt assertions, and lifecycle tests\n\n## Absent and error states\n\nNo live provider body, missing reviewer, unresolved required review, changes-requested, stale evidence fingerprint, changed PR head, no PR, missing settlement disposition, CI failure, GitHub outage, failed land request, restart, and missing registry authority must each produce an actionable durable state. None may silently advance a phase, self-approve, open GitHub as a fallback, merge early, duplicate land, or wait on an unexplained merge click.\n\n## Operational boundary\n\nReview conversations and dispositions survive body replacement. Approval-to-land is replay safe across process death and network failure. The system never arms merge while any required lifecycle review is unresolved or while reviewed Task/PR evidence is stale.\n\n## Exclusions\n\nDo not remove GitHub PRs, weaken branch protection, eliminate `submit` for ordinary non-Task PRs, require one fixed interaction policy across all phases, add policy-selection UI, or redesign the generic provider terminal transport.\n\n## Project KR\n\nDirectly advances: every dispatched task loop either lands its PR unattended after its LLM-session checkpoints clear or stops with an actionable non-convergence record, with zero silent stalls and zero human rescues through GitHub.","rank":19,"completed":true,"assignee":null},"reference":{"issue_url":"https://linear.app/loopflow/issue/LOO-162/make-llm-session-checkpoints-authoritative-for-task-landing","workspace":{"slug":"make-task-gate-approval-the","branch":"jack-heart/make-task-gate-approval-the-2","worktree":"/Users/jack/src/loopflow.make-task-gate-approval-the"}},"runtime":{"work_id":"task_f0f81a9582fe12bce91ceba5f0f15c57","project_id":"proj_9f1fc19a84211aed8b8136e55c8ab1f3","routing_project_id":"proj_9f1fc19a84211aed8b8136e55c8ab1f3","status":"abandoned","reason":"abandoned","updated_at":"2026-08-22T04:59:58Z","provider":"claude"},"next_move":{"owner":"project","reason":"abandoned"},"condition":{"state":"blocked","reason":"Task LOO-162 worktree /Users/jack/src/loopflow.make-task-gate-approval-the is missing; restore that exact path before `lf task resume LOO-162`; Task identity and PR history are unchanged","observed_at":"2026-09-23T15:06:37.290794Z","evidence_age_secs":2801199,"local_progress":{"state":"missing","unsettled":true,"dirty":null,"authored_commits":null,"recovery_required":true,"reason":"Task LOO-162 worktree /Users/jack/src/loopflow.make-task-gate-approval-the is missing; restore that exact path before `lf task resume LOO-162`; Task identity and PR history are unchanged"}},"actions":{"recommended":"no_action","reason":"Task is terminal"},"active_pr":null,"section":"later"},{"task":{"id":"e59a1581-699c-4d55-a1bd-6fe5d6ca5372","identifier":"LOO-163","name":"[retired] Make OpenCode GLM SSE disconnects observable and recoverable","description":"User-visible outcome\\n\\nProduct Wave work can use GLM through OpenCode without producing a hollow body. If OpenCode's SSE stream disconnects before useful work or mid-turn, Loopflow records the exact failure, preserves the durable Session/directive/worktree, and either retries only at a proven-safe boundary or hands the next body to the configured backup provider. No body that emitted no usable work remains reported as healthy or complete.\\n\\nIncident evidence\\n\\nDuring the current Product pursuit, several GLM/OpenCode bodies were hollow after an SSE disconnect. The work had to be handed manually to Claude Opus. Preserve the affected run/process/Task receipts as the reproduction corpus; do not infer the cause from the provider name alone.\\n\\nInvestigation and contract\\n\\n* Identify where the SSE stream ended: OpenCode/provider transport, Loopflow harness decoding, timeout/cancellation, or account/model routing. Record model, provider, endpoint class, timing, last valid event, and terminal error without logging credentials or raw auth.\\n* Define an observable hollow-body boundary: no incorporated directive, durable mutation, useful assistant output, or explicit terminal disposition.\\n* Make pre-first-content and mid-stream disconnects produce durable failed/stalled body evidence with an actionable reason. Never turn EOF into success.\\n* Preserve Task/Project Session identity, provider history, worktree, commands, and generation fencing across recovery.\\n* Retry only when replay safety is proven. Otherwise route the next generation through the configured backup provider and retain the failed OpenCode generation as audit evidence.\\n* Keep the behavior in the shared OpenCode/harness and child-supervision contract, not Product-specific prompts or a GLM-name special case.\\n\\nProof\\n\\n* A deterministic fake SSE server covers disconnect before headers/content, after metadata but before useful output, mid-tool call, and after a durable completion event.\\n* Tests prove exact body outcome, no false completion, one writer, no duplicate external side effect, and correct safe retry or backup-provider handoff.\\n* Replay the affected Product receipts and explain the root cause from evidence.\\n* Run at least ten GLM/OpenCode Product bodies with zero hollow successes; every forced disconnect is visible with reason and recovery owner.","rank":20,"completed":true,"assignee":null},"reference":{"issue_url":"https://linear.app/loopflow/issue/LOO-163/retired-make-opencode-glm-sse-disconnects-observable-and-recoverable","workspace":{"slug":"make-opencode-glm-sse-disconnects","branch":"jack-heart/make-opencode-glm-sse-disconnects-3","worktree":"/Users/jack/src/loopflow.make-opencode-glm-sse-disconnects"}},"runtime":{"work_id":"task_e5fe011eaf216a3a3960a6380699a9e7","project_id":"proj_9f1fc19a84211aed8b8136e55c8ab1f3","routing_project_id":"proj_9f1fc19a84211aed8b8136e55c8ab1f3","status":"abandoned","reason":"abandoned","updated_at":"2026-07-21T17:28:19Z","provider":"opencode"},"next_move":{"owner":"project","reason":"abandoned"},"condition":{"state":"blocked","reason":"Task LOO-163 worktree /Users/jack/src/loopflow.make-opencode-glm-sse-disconnects is missing; restore that exact path on branch \"jack-heart/make-opencode-glm-sse-disconnects-3\" before `lf task resume LOO-163`; Task identity and PR history are unchanged","observed_at":"2026-09-23T15:06:37.29156Z","evidence_age_secs":5521098,"local_progress":{"state":"missing","unsettled":true,"dirty":null,"authored_commits":null,"recovery_required":true,"reason":"Task LOO-163 worktree /Users/jack/src/loopflow.make-opencode-glm-sse-disconnects is missing; restore that exact path on branch \"jack-heart/make-opencode-glm-sse-disconnects-3\" before `lf task resume LOO-163`; Task identity and PR history are unchanged"}},"actions":{"recommended":"no_action","reason":"Task is terminal"},"active_pr":{"id":"pr_d68377ecc722441f9534f5318e016c47","sequence":3,"slug":"3","branch":"jack-heart/make-opencode-glm-sse-disconnects-3","base_commit":"b8369f51e44ec82cec0cb42a1b4cac77f97e8ce8","phase":"working","empty":null,"publication":null,"merge_commit":null,"abandoned_at":null},"section":"later"},{"task":{"id":"5e6a2e23-fb95-43fb-9b9e-7ef964f3684d","identifier":"LOO-207","name":"Make managed Tasks survive missing lifecycle flows","description":"## Observed failure\n\nOn 2026-07-21, LOO-193 advertised resume as its recommended legal action, but the recorded loop flow is task and the latest resume failed with flow not found: task. The current repository no longer exposes that flow. LOO-150 and LOO-152 carry the same stale lifecycle plan, and LOO-178 cannot even reconcile because its worktree is missing.\n\n## Outcome\n\nA managed Task never recommends or attempts a lifecycle phase whose flow cannot be resolved. Existing durable Tasks with a removed flow converge through one explicit, safe migration or actionable recovery path that preserves Task identity, worktree, dirty changes, provider history, and PR sequence. New Tasks cannot persist a lifecycle plan that names an unavailable flow.\n\n## Proof\n\nReproduce the exact LOO-193 snapshot: parked loop phase, no live body, dirty uncommitted work, recorded missing flow, recommended resume. Before the fix, resume fails. After the fix, status and the legal command agree and the same Task resumes through a valid flow without losing local work. Cover an open merged-PR successor, a missing worktree, and a newly created Task. Do not add a compatibility flow alias that hides invalid durable state; keep lifecycle validation and migration explicit.","rank":21,"completed":true,"assignee":null},"reference":{"issue_url":"https://linear.app/loopflow/issue/LOO-207/make-managed-tasks-survive-missing-lifecycle-flows","workspace":{"slug":"make-managed-tasks-survive-missing","branch":"jack-heart/make-managed-tasks-survive-missing-2","worktree":"/Users/jack/src/loopflow.make-managed-tasks-survive-missing"}},"runtime":{"work_id":"task_f607ae8aec8d45bcb634e58b81ae5a34","project_id":"proj_9f1fc19a84211aed8b8136e55c8ab1f3","routing_project_id":"proj_9f1fc19a84211aed8b8136e55c8ab1f3","status":"abandoned","reason":"abandoned","updated_at":"2026-08-28T22:07:47Z","provider":"codex"},"next_move":{"owner":"project","reason":"PR is published but settlement is not armed with `lf pr land -c`"},"condition":{"state":"blocked","reason":"Task LOO-207 worktree /Users/jack/src/loopflow.make-managed-tasks-survive-missing is missing; restore that exact path on branch \"jack-heart/make-managed-tasks-survive-missing-2\" before `lf task resume LOO-207`; Task identity and PR history are unchanged","observed_at":"2026-09-23T15:06:37.296644Z","evidence_age_secs":2221130,"local_progress":{"state":"missing","unsettled":true,"dirty":null,"authored_commits":null,"recovery_required":true,"reason":"Task LOO-207 worktree /Users/jack/src/loopflow.make-managed-tasks-survive-missing is missing; restore that exact path on branch \"jack-heart/make-managed-tasks-survive-missing-2\" before `lf task resume LOO-207`; Task identity and PR history are unchanged"}},"actions":{"recommended":"no_action","reason":"Task is terminal"},"active_pr":{"id":"pr_d5cb91f6ea9047bd926bfe4e89f97f38","sequence":2,"slug":"2","branch":"jack-heart/make-managed-tasks-survive-missing-2","base_commit":"ebe2fb596babd13343e38b20089eb98a40cd1985","phase":"open","empty":null,"publication":{"requested_at":"2026-08-28T18:04:26Z","presentation":{"title":"LOO-207: Make managed Tasks survive missing lifecycle flows","body":"<!-- loopflow:task-pr-context:start -->\n> [!NOTE]\n> **Task:** [LOO-207 — Make managed Tasks survive missing lifecycle flows](https://linear.app/loopflow/issue/LOO-207/make-managed-tasks-survive-missing-lifecycle-flows)\n> **Task cycle:** feature\n> **PR lifecycle:** PR 2 is published for review; no Task settlement is requested.\n<!-- loopflow:task-pr-context:end -->\n\n## Evaluate\n\n```bash\ncargo test -p loopflow --test task_initialization_tests new_task_launch_rejects_an_unavailable_flow_before_persistence\n```\n\nThe test passes after an unavailable loop flow produces a `flow not found` error naming the requested flow. It also proves that the rejected launch leaves both `tasks` and `task_prs` empty.\n\n## Why it matters\n\nA removed or renamed lifecycle flow must stop Task launch before durable state is created. Otherwise a configuration error can leave behind a managed Task or PR record for work that never started, complicating status and recovery.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Added an integration fixture with a registered Wave and PM snapshot that exercises a genuinely new Task through `task_run`\n- Asserted unavailable lifecycle validation happens before Task and PR persistence\n- Materialized the draft status-truth schema explicitly in Task initialization and recovery fixtures so they test against the schema expected by this checkout\n\n## Risks / Not included\n\n- No production behavior or migration logic changed; this PR adds regression proof and aligns test fixtures with the current draft schema","head_sha":"2e1eacdd97dc085b46facc74e72b1b9554f0aee4"},"github":{"number":1246,"url":"https://github.com/loopflowstudio/loopflow/pull/1246"},"merge":null},"merge_commit":null,"abandoned_at":null},"section":"later"},{"task":{"id":"69d0fc85-a698-4d8d-a9c8-12c540dc5a71","identifier":"LOO-164","name":"Let an agent hand interactive work to a human and resume","description":"## User-visible outcome\n\nAn agent can deliberately open an interactive Codex, Claude Code, or other vendor session in the correct Home and worktree, block behind that exact session, and resume after the human completes or hands the work back. The same durable handoff can be opened from embedded Ghostty or a supported external presentation without creating a second agent or lifecycle.\n\n## Contract\n\n* Add one durable interactive child Session under the owning Wave, Project, or Task Session. Record parent, Home, worktree, provider, provider session id when available, body generation, reason human input is needed, and terminal outcome.\n* W2-135 body leases and recovery remain authoritative. Build on its active PR rather than adding a parallel process owner.\n* Launching the handoff atomically marks the parent as waiting for a human and blocks its flow at a replay-safe boundary.\n* Expose a small attach descriptor with stable Session id, status, cwd, host, required environment, and terminal attach command or argv. Terminal bytes stay outside the API.\n* Completion or explicit hand-back records durable evidence, terminates or adopts the child safely, and wakes the same blocked parent exactly once.\n* Body death, app restart, host restart, repeated attach, and stale completion remain idempotent and do not orphan or duplicate the handoff.\n* Keep non-interactive Wave, Project, Task, and direct execution bodies distinct. This primitive grants controls only to deliberate interactive handoffs.\n\n## Historical implementation evidence\n\nRehome the lifecycle proven by commits c1d4adae8, f0eafbb18, 1267bf494, fbcf9f3af, c358e9cf4, 710bcd60c, and f0292d588 under the current store and Wave/Project/Task ontology. Do not restore lfd or the deleted parallel Session catalog from 309575f8e.\n\n## Proof\n\nDeterministic tests cover local handoff, repeated attach, parent process replacement, app restart, child body death, explicit hand-back, completion, and concurrent completion. Ten real handoffs open the exact same Session, preserve provider history and worktree, and resume the parent once. Shared DTO fixture tests pin the attach descriptor for Rust and Swift consumers.\n\n## Delivery\n\nStart this Task stacked on W2-135. The first PR owns the shared store and CLI contract plus tests. Mac Active Sessions and presentation adapters follow as separate Tasks.","rank":22,"completed":true,"assignee":null},"reference":{"issue_url":"https://linear.app/loopflow/issue/LOO-164/let-an-agent-hand-interactive-work-to-a-human-and-resume","workspace":{"slug":"let-an-agent-hand-interactive","branch":"jack-heart/let-an-agent-hand-interactive-interactive-parent-resume","worktree":"/Users/jack/src/loopflow.let-an-agent-hand-interactive"}},"runtime":{"work_id":"task_bd7f8b96641e71b53cbac3915805134b","project_id":"proj_9f1fc19a84211aed8b8136e55c8ab1f3","routing_project_id":"proj_9f1fc19a84211aed8b8136e55c8ab1f3","status":"abandoned","reason":"abandoned","updated_at":"2026-07-21T17:28:19Z","provider":"claude"},"next_move":{"owner":"project","reason":"abandoned"},"condition":{"state":"blocked","reason":"Task LOO-164 worktree /Users/jack/src/loopflow.let-an-agent-hand-interactive is missing; restore that exact path before `lf task resume LOO-164`; Task identity and PR history are unchanged","observed_at":"2026-09-23T15:06:37.299062Z","evidence_age_secs":5521098,"local_progress":{"state":"missing","unsettled":true,"dirty":null,"authored_commits":null,"recovery_required":true,"reason":"Task LOO-164 worktree /Users/jack/src/loopflow.let-an-agent-hand-interactive is missing; restore that exact path before `lf task resume LOO-164`; Task identity and PR history are unchanged"}},"actions":{"recommended":"no_action","reason":"Task is terminal"},"active_pr":null,"section":"later"},{"task":{"id":"abde656d-06c9-4572-a2df-499c009c8749","identifier":"LOO-165","name":"Make Wave control-plane reconciliation self-healing","description":"## User-visible outcome\n\nA running Wave continuously converges durable Project and Task intent with live process bodies, provider work, pull-request truth, and repository state. Users no longer see dead Projects counted as active, merged PRs described as open, or read-only commands rewriting their canonical checkout. After a laptop restart or body death, Loopflow either safely recovers the same work or names the exact boundary requiring intervention.\n\n## Evidence to investigate\n\n1. A live Product or Infrastructure Wave resident did not recover dead Project bodies.\n2. Product reported five active Projects while every Project process was dead.\n3. W2-135 continued to report PR #903 as open after GitHub had merged it.\n4. Read-only Project turns refused to run when canonical main was dirty.\n5. lf wt list invoked sync_main, auto-stashed existing edits, updated canonical main, and still returned a listing; additional edits then made main dirty again.\n\nPreserve these as five deterministic reproductions. Do not collapse them into one generic stale-status bug before the ownership and event paths are mapped.\n\n## Research questions\n\n* Which durable record expresses desired Wave, Project, and Task intent, and which supervisor owns convergence for each level?\n* What does active mean for intent, Session, body, provider turn, and child work? Which counts and labels should each product surface expose?\n* Which event or observation reconciles GitHub PR state, and how fresh must it be before status may claim open, merged, failed, or review-required?\n* Why do read-only Project turns depend on a clean mutable canonical checkout? Can they run against an immutable recorded base or repository snapshot while Task writers retain isolated worktrees?\n* Which commands currently call sync_main or other mutating Git operations transitively? What public API makes read-only versus synchronizing behavior mechanically explicit?\n* Which failures belong to automatic recovery, safe adoption, retry, NeedsInput, or terminal state under the W2-135 lease model?\n\n## Source of truth\n\nDurable Wave, Project, Task, directive, PR-sequence, and body-generation records in the Loopflow store own intent and identity. Process probes, GitHub, Git, and provider sessions are timestamped observations, not alternate identity. One reconciliation projection derives status, active counts, attention, next owner, and legal controls for CLI, roadmap, chat, and Swift.\n\n## Product and API contract\n\n* A live Wave supervisor periodically and eventfully reconciles every selected Project Session. It adopts a valid body, starts a safe missing body, preserves terminal intent, or records why recovery is unsafe.\n* Desired active intent and observed live bodies are distinct typed fields. Counts must state which they count; a dead body can never make a live-process count positive.\n* PR observations reconcile by stable PR identity and current head. A merge transitions the PR sequence exactly once and wakes the owning Project or Task decision path without waiting for a manual status probe.\n* Read-only Project turns and inspection commands never require, clean, sync, reset, stash, fetch into, or rewrite canonical main. If fresh upstream state is required, the command names and owns that mutation explicitly.\n* lf wt list and every other list, status, roadmap, doctor, diff, and file inspection surface are side-effect free. Add a mechanical command classification or boundary test so future transitive sync calls fail review and CI.\n* Reconciliation is idempotent and restart-safe. Concurrent Wave, Project, Task, status, and external-observer events converge without duplicate bodies, lost edits, repeated PR transitions, or parallel intent.\n* Every automatic action and refusal emits durable evidence with reason, freshness, next owner, and legal controls, feeding W2-123 rather than inventing a second presentation model.\n\n## Affected surfaces and consumers\n\nWave and Project supervisors; Task/PR lifecycle; store schema and events; GitHub observation; Git/worktree operations; lf status, lf roadmap, lf project/task status, lf wt list, lf doctor; Wave Chat; Mac and iOS shared DTOs; builtin Wave/Project/Task skills; release and dogfood automation.\n\n## Absent and error states\n\nMissing execution context, unavailable GitHub, unreachable Home, ambiguous process ownership, dirty canonical checkout, stale observations, uncertain external side effects, and conflicting generations must remain explicit evidence. Never guess, report an empty healthy state, mutate main during inspection, or replay a control-uncertain action.\n\n## Operational boundary\n\nReconciliation must remain bounded with no provider body required for mechanical adoption, liveness, GitHub refresh, or status projection. Read-only local commands should return promptly from persisted evidence and bounded probes. GitHub failure preserves the last observation with its age. A restart must converge without a human discovering the stall first.\n\n## End-to-end proof\n\nRun Product and Infrastructure with at least two selected Projects each. Kill every Project body, merge one waiting Task PR externally, leave canonical main dirty with named uncommitted edits, and invoke wt list, status, roadmap, and Project reconciliation concurrently. Prove:\n\n* the Wave residents recover every replay-safe Project body exactly once;\n* live-body and durable-intent counts remain distinct and correct;\n* the merged PR advances once and reaches its owning decision path;\n* all inspection commands leave HEAD, index, worktree, refs, and stash byte-for-byte unchanged;\n* unsafe recovery becomes NeedsInput with exact evidence;\n* CLI and Swift fixtures render the same state, reason, freshness, owner, and controls.\n\nRepeat the scenario across process and laptop restart. Re-running reconciliation is a no-op.\n\n## Delivery shape\n\nOne stable Task worktree and ordered serial PRs. Begin with a cross-layer design and deterministic reproductions. Expected slices are: reconciliation/source-of-truth model; Project-body recovery and active-count semantics; PR observation convergence; side-effect-free inspection and explicit sync APIs; shared status consumers and real two-Wave dogfood. Adjust boundaries when the code proves a simpler sequence.\n\n## Relationship to existing work\n\nBuild on W2-135 body generations and write leases, W2-140 Project Session succession, W2-156 CI observation, and W2-123 visible-state semantics. Do not duplicate their models. If a required primitive is missing, extend its owning shared API in this Task's serial PR sequence and record the dependency.\n\n## Exclusions\n\nDo not pop or delete existing stashes, discard dirty work, create a second supervisor/store, or redesign GitHub review policy. Do not make canonical main writable by Project turns merely to bypass the read-only boundary.","rank":23,"completed":true,"assignee":null},"reference":{"issue_url":"https://linear.app/loopflow/issue/LOO-165/make-wave-control-plane-reconciliation-self-healing","workspace":{"slug":"make-wave-control-plane-reconciliation","branch":"jack-heart/make-wave-control-plane-reconciliation-project-body-recovery","worktree":"/Users/jack/src/loopflow.make-wave-control-plane-reconciliation"}},"runtime":{"work_id":"task_8eb408976ab97e15c11eda2d42add0f7","project_id":"proj_9f1fc19a84211aed8b8136e55c8ab1f3","routing_project_id":"proj_9f1fc19a84211aed8b8136e55c8ab1f3","status":"abandoned","reason":"abandoned","updated_at":"2026-07-21T17:28:19Z","provider":"claude"},"next_move":{"owner":"project","reason":"abandoned"},"condition":{"state":"blocked","reason":"Task LOO-165 worktree /Users/jack/src/loopflow.make-wave-control-plane-reconciliation is missing; restore that exact path before `lf task resume LOO-165`; Task identity and PR history are unchanged","observed_at":"2026-09-23T15:06:37.300039Z","evidence_age_secs":5521098,"local_progress":{"state":"missing","unsettled":true,"dirty":null,"authored_commits":null,"recovery_required":true,"reason":"Task LOO-165 worktree /Users/jack/src/loopflow.make-wave-control-plane-reconciliation is missing; restore that exact path before `lf task resume LOO-165`; Task identity and PR history are unchanged"}},"actions":{"recommended":"no_action","reason":"Task is terminal"},"active_pr":null,"section":"later"},{"task":{"id":"4194aa8d-29f7-43dd-85f4-62c2e7ce0753","identifier":"LOO-166","name":"[retired] Resolve Cadenza Linear team ownership","description":"## User-visible outcome\n\nA Loopflow user opening Linear sees Cadenza work owned by the intended Cadenza team structure. Projects, Tasks, identifiers, and links agree with the repository and Wave that own the work; creating work through Loopflow cannot silently attach it to the legacy W2 team.\n\n## Investigation\n\n* Reproduce why Cadenza's Unified Practice Targets Project and W2-157 are associated with the legacy shared team even though the Cadenza Waves declare Linear team bindings.\n* Establish whether Linear team ownership belongs to a repository, to each Wave, or to an explicit Wave-to-team mapping that supports both. Reconcile that decision with W2-155's one-team-per-Wave contract and the desired Cadenza experience.\n* Audit the authoritative binding path from wave GOAL.md through the registry/database, PM sync, projectCreate(teamIds), task creation, doctor, roadmap, and Swift consumers.\n* Determine whether the defect is stale configuration, incomplete rollout, unsupported cross-repository discovery, or a product-model mismatch.\n* Inventory every affected Cadenza Initiative, Project, open Task, completed Task, and active Session before proposing mutation.\n* Design an idempotent migration that repairs Linear Project team associations as well as Task teams, preserves stable provider UUIDs and live Session/PR ownership, and reports identifier changes.\n* Identify why the shipped reteam path and lf pm doctor did not prevent or repair this state.\n\n## Source of truth\n\nThe result must name one authoritative persisted mapping among repository, Wave, Linear Initiative, Linear team, and Linear Project. Linear display names, team keys, and issue identifiers remain presentation; stable IDs own identity. Every CLI and Swift view derives from the same mapping.\n\n## End-to-end proof\n\nFrom a clean Cadenza checkout, create or adopt one Wave, create a Project, and create a Task through Loopflow. The Linear Project appears under the decided Cadenza team, the Task receives the expected team prefix, lf pm sync/show/doctor agree, and roadmap/status links resolve to the same stable objects. Repeat against the current Unified Practice Targets data and prove the migration plan is a no-op on its second run.\n\n## Absent and error states\n\nMissing repository ownership, conflicting Wave bindings, inaccessible Linear teams, Projects attached to multiple or legacy teams, and active Tasks unsafe to move must stop with an exact diagnosis. No command may guess a team or partially move a hierarchy.\n\n## Operational boundary\n\nDiscovery and dry-run are read-only. Any follow-on apply path must be restart-safe, preserve active Task Sessions and PR sequences, and expose every planned mutation before Linear side effects.\n\n## Exclusions\n\nDo not silently move existing Cadenza work during this investigation. Do not redesign Linear's workspace hierarchy, rename unrelated teams, or migrate completed history until the ownership policy and migration contract are explicit.","rank":24,"completed":true,"assignee":null},"reference":{"issue_url":"https://linear.app/loopflow/issue/LOO-166/retired-resolve-cadenza-linear-team-ownership","workspace":{"slug":"resolve-cadenza-linear-team-ownership","branch":"jack-heart/resolve-cadenza-linear-team-ownership-3","worktree":"/Users/jack/src/loopflow.resolve-cadenza-linear-team-ownership"}},"runtime":{"work_id":"task_94182c109eee3665545112c2f984a4be","project_id":"proj_9f1fc19a84211aed8b8136e55c8ab1f3","routing_project_id":"proj_9f1fc19a84211aed8b8136e55c8ab1f3","status":"abandoned","reason":"abandoned","updated_at":"2026-07-21T17:28:19Z","provider":"opencode"},"next_move":{"owner":"project","reason":"abandoned"},"condition":{"state":"blocked","reason":"Task LOO-166 worktree /Users/jack/src/loopflow.resolve-cadenza-linear-team-ownership is missing; restore that exact path before `lf task resume LOO-166`; Task identity and PR history are unchanged","observed_at":"2026-09-23T15:06:37.300494Z","evidence_age_secs":5521098,"local_progress":{"state":"missing","unsettled":true,"dirty":null,"authored_commits":null,"recovery_required":true,"reason":"Task LOO-166 worktree /Users/jack/src/loopflow.resolve-cadenza-linear-team-ownership is missing; restore that exact path before `lf task resume LOO-166`; Task identity and PR history are unchanged"}},"actions":{"recommended":"no_action","reason":"Task is terminal"},"active_pr":null,"section":"later"},{"task":{"id":"cd90421b-c587-4492-b55f-8e6a90ae111c","identifier":"LOO-167","name":"[retired] Wake a waiting Task into ci-fix when its PR fails","description":"User story\n\nAfter a Task opens a PR, it sleeps without consuming a provider body while required checks are pending. If a required check fails on the current PR head, Loopflow wakes that same durable Task into a bounded `ci-fix` turn, repairs the existing branch, and updates the same PR. The user does not discover CI failures manually or rescue the worker from its worktree.\n\nLifecycle contract\n\n* Pending checks are healthy waiting: persist the PR, head SHA, check state, and freshness, but run no provider body.\n* A required check transitioning to failed on the current head enqueues one audited `ci-fix` turn for the same Task Session, worktree, provider history, and active PR sequence. Include PR number/URL, branch, head SHA, failing check names, and log URLs so the skill resolves the exact failure.\n* Coalesce simultaneous failures and deduplicate wakeups by PR head plus observed failure set. A repeated poll or webhook delivery must not create two bodies or two fixes.\n* The `ci-fix` turn follows the builtin skill: reproduce the latest failure, make the smallest correct fix, run targeted then proportional checks, and report an infrastructure or credential blocker rather than weakening tests.\n* After a push changes the head SHA, return to sleep and watch the new checks. Green checks remain waiting for the configured review/merge action; a new failure may wake one new `ci-fix` turn.\n* Manual `lf task resume ISSUE MESSAGE` remains a supported override for rebase or review feedback and must be consumed before the default open-PR waiting transition.\n* Preserve the exactly-one-body/write-lease rules and expose pending, fixing, blocked, and green-with-next-owner truthfully through `lf status`.\n\nOperational boundary\n\nUse the existing Task event/command path and builtin `ci-fix` skill. Do not add a second CI worker identity, duplicate Task, new worktree, provider transcript, or CI-specific monitor store. GitHub check evidence is authoritative only for the PR current head; stale failures never wake work.\n\nProof\n\nA deterministic integration harness opens a PR and proves: pending checks consume no body; one required failure starts exactly one `ci-fix` turn with canonical metadata; duplicate and multi-check deliveries coalesce; the fix pushes the same branch/PR and rearms observation for the new SHA; green CI does not wake a body; and an infrastructure failure produces an actionable blocker without code churn. Reproduce W2-144 generation 7 to prove a queued manual repair is incorporated once instead of being discarded because the PR is open.\n\n## Infrastructure dependencies\n\nThe full done-whens remain open until these substrate tasks merge and their evidence is incorporated:\n\n* W2-229 — deterministic failed-PR ci-fix lifecycle proof\n* W2-230 — durable audited ci-fix command ledger\n* W2-231 — actionable Blocked semantics for infrastructure failures\n* W2-232 — bounded ci-fix settlement without generic gate re-entry\n\nPR #967 may ship as an incremental Product slice; it is not task-completion evidence by itself.","rank":25,"completed":true,"assignee":null},"reference":{"issue_url":"https://linear.app/loopflow/issue/LOO-167/retired-wake-a-waiting-task-into-ci-fix-when-its-pr-fails","workspace":{"slug":"wake-a-waiting-task-into","branch":"jack-heart/wake-a-waiting-task-into-ci-fix-lifecycle-proof","worktree":"/Users/jack/src/loopflow.wake-a-waiting-task-into"}},"runtime":{"work_id":"task_113a3a20a1168da783afc89467c367c8","project_id":"proj_9f1fc19a84211aed8b8136e55c8ab1f3","routing_project_id":"proj_9f1fc19a84211aed8b8136e55c8ab1f3","status":"abandoned","reason":"abandoned","updated_at":"2026-07-21T17:28:19Z","provider":"opencode"},"next_move":{"owner":"project","reason":"abandoned"},"condition":{"state":"blocked","reason":"Task LOO-167 worktree /Users/jack/src/loopflow.wake-a-waiting-task-into is missing; restore that exact path on branch \"jack-heart/wake-a-waiting-task-into-ci-fix-lifecycle-proof\" before `lf task resume LOO-167`; Task identity and PR history are unchanged","observed_at":"2026-09-23T15:06:37.301271Z","evidence_age_secs":5521098,"local_progress":{"state":"missing","unsettled":true,"dirty":null,"authored_commits":null,"recovery_required":true,"reason":"Task LOO-167 worktree /Users/jack/src/loopflow.wake-a-waiting-task-into is missing; restore that exact path on branch \"jack-heart/wake-a-waiting-task-into-ci-fix-lifecycle-proof\" before `lf task resume LOO-167`; Task identity and PR history are unchanged"}},"actions":{"recommended":"no_action","reason":"Task is terminal"},"active_pr":{"id":"pr_c662e2c9ef2a4fe78ac347e509332871","sequence":3,"slug":"ci-fix-lifecycle-proof","branch":"jack-heart/wake-a-waiting-task-into-ci-fix-lifecycle-proof","base_commit":"7efe30fb24d9befa874b1f754d825a024acc2607","phase":"working","empty":null,"publication":null,"merge_commit":null,"abandoned_at":null},"section":"later"},{"task":{"id":"fa4b5b80-49b7-48af-ae40-e253c5a75fef","identifier":"LOO-168","name":"Give every Wave its own Linear team and Task prefix","description":"## User story\n\nAs a Loopflow user browsing Linear, I can identify the owning Wave from a Task identifier alone: PRD-* for Product, INF-* for Infrastructure, and INT-* for Intelligence. Creating, moving, and running work through Loopflow preserves the Wave → Project → Task hierarchy without funneling every Task into one shared W2 team.\n\n## End-to-end contract\n\n* Persist an explicit Linear team binding per Wave alongside its Initiative binding. Stable provider IDs own identity; team display names and keys remain mutable presentation.\n* Make `lf pm init` create or adopt the intended Wave team and requested key, diagnosing conflicts instead of guessing.\n* Associate Linear Projects with the owning Wave team and create every new Task in that team.\n* Provide an idempotent, restart-safe migration for current W2 Tasks. Preserve issue UUIDs, descriptions, comments, relationships, PR links, ordering, completion, and Loopflow Task and Project Session ownership while updating visible identifiers wherever they are cached or displayed.\n* Protect live and in-review Tasks during migration. Prove that a Linear team move is safe for an active Session or defer it explicitly; never strand a worktree, PR sequence, provider history, or durable Session because W2-123 becomes PRD-123.\n* Make and document one deliberate policy for completed W2 history: preserve it as historical or migrate it with traceable identity.\n* Keep Linear team keys and prefixed Project display names separate from Loopflow Wave and Project identity. Repo slugs, cache keys, and command inputs must not derive from provider presentation.\n* Keep CLI, status, chat and roadmap links, Swift DTOs, docs, and `lf pm doctor` consistent with the same mapping.\n\n## Proof\n\n* Product, Infrastructure, and Intelligence each create a real Task through Loopflow and receive PRD-, INF-, and INT- identifiers respectively.\n* A dry run names every issue that will move, every identifier that will change, and every protected Task it will defer.\n* Migration preserves open and completed work, active Session lookup by stable issue ID, PR associations, Project membership, and task ordering.\n* Re-running setup and migration performs no duplicate team, Project, Task, or move.\n* A cross-Wave move either completes safely with a traceable identifier change or refuses with an exact recovery action.\n* PM sync and doctor finish cleanly, and the Linear workspace is visibly grouped by Wave without changing Loopflow repo names.","rank":26,"completed":true,"assignee":null},"reference":{"issue_url":"https://linear.app/loopflow/issue/LOO-168/give-every-wave-its-own-linear-team-and-task-prefix","workspace":{"slug":"give-every-wave-its-own","branch":"jack-heart/give-every-wave-its-own-reteam-existing-work","worktree":"/Users/jack/src/loopflow.give-every-wave-its-own"}},"runtime":{"work_id":"task_1a33fa263171ae88436b4b86bb5c6098","project_id":"proj_9f1fc19a84211aed8b8136e55c8ab1f3","routing_project_id":"proj_9f1fc19a84211aed8b8136e55c8ab1f3","status":"abandoned","reason":"abandoned","updated_at":"2026-07-21T17:28:19Z","provider":"claude"},"next_move":{"owner":"project","reason":"abandoned"},"condition":{"state":"blocked","reason":"Task LOO-168 worktree /Users/jack/src/loopflow.give-every-wave-its-own is missing; restore that exact path before `lf task resume LOO-168`; Task identity and PR history are unchanged","observed_at":"2026-09-23T15:06:37.309922Z","evidence_age_secs":5521098,"local_progress":{"state":"missing","unsettled":true,"dirty":null,"authored_commits":null,"recovery_required":true,"reason":"Task LOO-168 worktree /Users/jack/src/loopflow.give-every-wave-its-own is missing; restore that exact path before `lf task resume LOO-168`; Task identity and PR history are unchanged"}},"actions":{"recommended":"no_action","reason":"Task is terminal"},"active_pr":null,"section":"later"},{"task":{"id":"ee037012-eaf5-4c1e-8663-4ac89c498f8c","identifier":"LOO-169","name":"[absorbed] Preserve actionable Project blockers","description":"Absorbed into “Make every visible state explain what happened and who acts next.” The Mac Surface UX reproduction remains an explicit acceptance case: pursuit-authored Task/PR dependencies must survive mutation into durable Project status and next_move; generic no-mutation language is only for a true planning dead end.","rank":27,"completed":true,"assignee":null},"reference":{"issue_url":"https://linear.app/loopflow/issue/LOO-169/absorbed-preserve-actionable-project-blockers","workspace":null},"runtime":null,"next_move":{"owner":"project","reason":"Linear Task is complete"},"condition":{"state":"waiting","reason":"Linear Task is complete","observed_at":"2026-09-23T15:06:37.311679Z","evidence_age_secs":null,"local_progress":{"state":"not_applicable","unsettled":false,"dirty":null,"authored_commits":null,"recovery_required":null,"reason":null}},"actions":{"recommended":null,"reason":"Task is ready to start"},"active_pr":null,"section":"later"},{"task":{"id":"83fcc4fc-428e-4942-8290-f0129d85621a","identifier":"LOO-170","name":"Make every CLI command resolve managed Wave context consistently","description":"User story\n\nInside a Wave, Project, or Task process, every `lf` command should act on the current durable Wave without requiring `--wave`, confusing a UUID for a name, or failing differently by subsystem. Explicit targeting must remain predictable for scripts and humans outside managed context.\n\nContract\n\n* Establish one resolver for `LF_WAVE_ID`: durable registry UUID first, hand-set Wave name as an intentional fallback, explicit `--wave` always wins.\n* Apply it to PM reads and mutations, status, chat, Project/Task launch helpers, trace attribution, and other ambient Wave consumers instead of fixing commands independently.\n* Preserve cache-only behavior: `lf pm show --no-sync --json` inside managed Wave and child processes never requires Linear or a guessed cwd.\n* Distinguish missing context, stale registry identity, and unknown explicit Wave with actionable errors.\n* Keep the environment as process context, never as the source of Wave identity or process role.\n\nProof\n\nA command matrix runs the relevant read and mutation parsers from Wave, Project, Task, hand-set-name, explicit-override, stale-ID, and no-context environments. Every command resolves the same Wave or returns the same classified error; the original `lf pm show` UUID reproduction passes from both resident Product and its Mac Project Session. This replaces the stale launcher diagnosis that treated exporting a UUID as the bug; inconsistent consumers were the bug.","rank":28,"completed":true,"assignee":null},"reference":{"issue_url":"https://linear.app/loopflow/issue/LOO-170/make-every-cli-command-resolve-managed-wave-context-consistently","workspace":{"slug":"make-every-cli-command-resolve","branch":"jack-heart/make-every-cli-command-resolve-chat-radio-memory","worktree":"/Users/jack/src/loopflow.make-every-cli-command-resolve"}},"runtime":{"work_id":"task_55eafafe0b5d7803336a02602c15b7af","project_id":"proj_9f1fc19a84211aed8b8136e55c8ab1f3","routing_project_id":"proj_9f1fc19a84211aed8b8136e55c8ab1f3","status":"abandoned","reason":"abandoned","updated_at":"2026-07-21T17:28:19Z","provider":"claude"},"next_move":{"owner":"project","reason":"abandoned"},"condition":{"state":"blocked","reason":"Task LOO-170 worktree /Users/jack/src/loopflow.make-every-cli-command-resolve is missing; restore that exact path before `lf task resume LOO-170`; Task identity and PR history are unchanged","observed_at":"2026-09-23T15:06:37.311732Z","evidence_age_secs":5521098,"local_progress":{"state":"missing","unsettled":true,"dirty":null,"authored_commits":null,"recovery_required":true,"reason":"Task LOO-170 worktree /Users/jack/src/loopflow.make-every-cli-command-resolve is missing; restore that exact path before `lf task resume LOO-170`; Task identity and PR history are unchanged"}},"actions":{"recommended":"no_action","reason":"Task is terminal"},"active_pr":null,"section":"later"},{"task":{"id":"69a78b36-9d2c-4b72-96ad-8b09985e0b58","identifier":"LOO-171","name":"Recover an abandoned Task without losing its work or PR history","description":"User story\n\nWhen a Task attempt is abandoned because its provider, process, or execution context is unsafe, the user can deliberately recover that same durable Task without losing its worktree, serial PR history, directives, or audit trail—and without Loopflow silently restarting terminal work.\n\nCurrent product model\n\nA Linear Task may ship through multiple serial PRs. The Task is durable intent; Task Session attempts and process bodies are execution history. Completed Tasks and merged completion PRs never relaunch. Failed or interrupted work resumes the same safe Session. Abandonment requires an explicit recovery decision.\n\nContract\n\n* Offer one explicit recover action for an abandoned Task. It creates a linked successor attempt only when the stable worktree and next serial PR can be adopted safely; otherwise it requires a new Task and explains why.\n* Preserve predecessor/successor history, Task directives, existing PR sequence, branch/base evidence, and pinned execution context. Never create parallel active attempts or parallel active PRs.\n* Converge concurrent recovery requests on exactly one non-terminal attempt.\n* Integrate with the leased-body supervision model: automatic process recovery may replace a body, but terminal abandonment is never crossed automatically.\n* Expose actionability in CLI and shared Now/Roadmap DTOs: recover, resume, start next PR, complete, or no legal action, with reason and owner.\n\nProof\n\nEnd-to-end tests cover interrupted resume, safe abandoned successor, unsafe legacy context, concurrent recover, submitted Task, multi-PR Task between PRs, and completed Task. One dogfood Task is abandoned and deliberately recovered through its next PR with one worktree, one active writer, complete history, and no manual database or Git repair. Depends on the shared supervision contract in W2-135.","rank":29,"completed":true,"assignee":null},"reference":{"issue_url":"https://linear.app/loopflow/issue/LOO-171/recover-an-abandoned-task-without-losing-its-work-or-pr-history","workspace":{"slug":"recover-abandoned-task","branch":"jack-heart/recover-abandoned-task-2","worktree":"/Users/jack/src/loopflow.recover-abandoned-task"}},"runtime":{"work_id":"task_bd9342391df884d82d63dbc4f5f5f69d","project_id":"proj_9f1fc19a84211aed8b8136e55c8ab1f3","routing_project_id":"proj_9f1fc19a84211aed8b8136e55c8ab1f3","status":"abandoned","reason":"abandoned","updated_at":"2026-07-21T17:28:19Z","provider":"opencode"},"next_move":{"owner":"project","reason":"abandoned"},"condition":{"state":"blocked","reason":"Task LOO-171 worktree /Users/jack/src/loopflow.recover-abandoned-task is missing; restore that exact path before `lf task resume LOO-171`; Task identity and PR history are unchanged","observed_at":"2026-09-23T15:06:37.313777Z","evidence_age_secs":5521098,"local_progress":{"state":"missing","unsettled":true,"dirty":null,"authored_commits":null,"recovery_required":true,"reason":"Task LOO-171 worktree /Users/jack/src/loopflow.recover-abandoned-task is missing; restore that exact path before `lf task resume LOO-171`; Task identity and PR history are unchanged"}},"actions":{"recommended":"no_action","reason":"Task is terminal"},"active_pr":null,"section":"later"},{"task":{"id":"d2ae21dc-3394-48df-8762-276431dc8c20","identifier":"LOO-172","name":"Make lf roadmap the machine-wide view of planned work","description":"## User story\n\nAs the person conducting Loopflow, I can run one fast command and understand every durable piece of planned work across every Wave: what exists, what is underway, what is blocked, and what could be started next. I should not have to open Linear, query each Wave, or interpret process internals to understand the roadmap.\n\n## Product vocabulary\n\n* `lf status` is exclusively the live execution view: Wave residents, Project and Task bodies, runs, current commands, progress age, stalls, review waits, recovery, and attention. It answers what is happening now and whether it is healthy.\n* `lf roadmap` is the durable intent view backed by the local on-disk PM snapshot: Waves, Projects, KRs, and every open Task. It answers what exists and what could be worked on. Live execution state may be overlaid on a roadmap item, but the roadmap never becomes the owner of that state.\n* `lf pm` remains the Linear planning mutation and synchronization surface.\n* Do not add `lf work` or `lf status --all` as competing roadmap vocabulary. Tighten existing `lf status` output when necessary so the boundary remains true.\n\n## End-to-end experience\n\n`lf roadmap` is global by default and accepts an optional Wave scope. Its human output groups Tasks by Wave and Project, then presents concise sections for Now, Needs attention, Available, and Later. Every Task row carries its identifier, title, plan rank, concise reason, next owner, and active PR. When a durable Task has a live Session, the row overlays the shared execution category and progress age from `lf status`. Unavailable evidence says unavailable; an unstarted Task is never confused with a dead process.\n\n`lf roadmap --json` emits one machine-wide shared DTO for CLI, Mac, iOS, and Wave Chat. Consumers derive Now, Available, and roadmap lenses from the same snapshot rather than spawning one subprocess per Wave or rebuilding status rules independently.\n\n## Implementation bounds\n\n* Read the existing SQLite registry and PM snapshots locally. The command is deterministic and fast: no Linear sync, network request, or agent turn.\n* Reuse existing per-Wave Project and Task snapshots where their contract is correct. Add one envelope rather than a parallel planning model or database.\n* Batch process and tmux evidence once per query; do not perform one subprocess or liveness probe per Task.\n* Consume shared supervision categories and progress evidence from [W2-135](https://linear.app/loopflow/issue/W2-135/make-session-bodies-leased-progress-aware-and-recoverable). If that contract has not landed, keep the first slice additive and integrate after rebase rather than inventing another status taxonomy.\n* Treat [W2-141](https://linear.app/loopflow/issue/W2-141/research-unified-now-available-work-views) as product research input and provide the data contract consumed by [W2-131](https://linear.app/loopflow/issue/W2-131/show-the-all-wave-roadmap-and-launch-or-attach-work-from-chat) and the Mac roadmap surface.\n\n## Proof\n\n* On the real accumulated workspace, one `lf roadmap` invocation lists all open Tasks in Product, Infrastructure, and Intelligence with no per-Wave commands.\n* A running Task, review-waiting Task, stalled or failed Task, dependency-blocked Task, ready unstarted Task, and evidence-unavailable Task each render distinctly with the correct next owner.\n* `lf roadmap --wave product` is a scoped projection of the same global result.\n* `lf roadmap --json` round-trips through Rust and Swift fixtures without defaults or silent fallbacks.\n* `lf status` contains live execution and attention rather than the complete inactive roadmap; `lf roadmap` contains durable planned work and only overlays live evidence.\n* Mac and CLI consume one roadmap snapshot and agree on classification for the same fixture.\n* A measured real-workspace read has a named latency budget and avoids N-Wave and N-Task subprocess fan-out.\n* Rust, Swift, migration, and smoke gates pass, and user docs teach `lf status`, `lf roadmap`, and `lf pm` by example without overlapping promises.","rank":30,"completed":true,"assignee":null},"reference":{"issue_url":"https://linear.app/loopflow/issue/LOO-172/make-lf-roadmap-the-machine-wide-view-of-planned-work","workspace":{"slug":"make-lf-work-the-machine","branch":"jack-heart/make-lf-work-the-machine","worktree":"/Users/jack/src/loopflow.make-lf-work-the-machine"}},"runtime":{"work_id":"task_50195641afaaedc123327ee74171e1e3","project_id":"proj_9f1fc19a84211aed8b8136e55c8ab1f3","routing_project_id":"proj_9f1fc19a84211aed8b8136e55c8ab1f3","status":"abandoned","reason":"abandoned","updated_at":"2026-07-21T17:28:19Z","provider":"codex"},"next_move":{"owner":"project","reason":"abandoned"},"condition":{"state":"blocked","reason":"Task LOO-172 worktree /Users/jack/src/loopflow.make-lf-work-the-machine is missing; restore that exact path before `lf task resume LOO-172`; Task identity and PR history are unchanged","observed_at":"2026-09-23T15:06:37.314438Z","evidence_age_secs":5521098,"local_progress":{"state":"missing","unsettled":true,"dirty":null,"authored_commits":null,"recovery_required":true,"reason":"Task LOO-172 worktree /Users/jack/src/loopflow.make-lf-work-the-machine is missing; restore that exact path before `lf task resume LOO-172`; Task identity and PR history are unchanged"}},"actions":{"recommended":"no_action","reason":"Task is terminal"},"active_pr":null,"section":"later"},{"task":{"id":"be89f28d-a6be-4431-99c6-d8e61de25f26","identifier":"LOO-173","name":"Project pursuit creates a successor after terminal Session","description":"Dogfood on 2026-07-14 proved the documented recovery path is impossible. The legacy loopflow-api Project Session ps_033fb81ca1504126860f82dced780e26 was explicitly abandoned because it predates pinned execution context. `lf project run d19956b2-9955-437d-aea6-d91766231c77` and `lf task run W2-139` must then create or ensure a current-context successor, but both rediscover the terminal row keyed to the Linear Project and reject it.\n\nMake Project pursuit history append-only while allowing exactly one current non-terminal Session per Linear Project:\n\n* `lf project run <project>` creates a successor when the latest Session is terminal (abandoned or completed), preserving the terminal Session and its events.\n* Task reservation ensures or adopts that same successor; concurrent project and task launches converge on one new Session rather than creating parallels.\n* Failed or stopped but resumable Sessions retain identity and are resumed; only terminal intent opens a successor.\n* Surface predecessor and successor identity in status or audit so history remains traceable.\n* Add end-to-end tests for abandon then project run and abandon then task run, including a concurrency case.\n\nThis is the blocker for filed task W2-139; do not bypass the registry or relabel W2-139 under another Project.","rank":31,"completed":true,"assignee":null},"reference":{"issue_url":"https://linear.app/loopflow/issue/LOO-173/project-pursuit-creates-a-successor-after-terminal-session","workspace":null},"runtime":null,"next_move":{"owner":"project","reason":"Linear Task is complete"},"condition":{"state":"waiting","reason":"Linear Task is complete","observed_at":"2026-09-23T15:06:37.314851Z","evidence_age_secs":null,"local_progress":{"state":"not_applicable","unsettled":false,"dirty":null,"authored_commits":null,"recovery_required":null,"reason":null}},"actions":{"recommended":null,"reason":"Task is ready to start"},"active_pr":null,"section":"later"},{"task":{"id":"7cd11fa8-a825-4b6f-a68c-448c00bdea29","identifier":"LOO-174","name":"[absorbed] Session liveness and execution context","description":"W2-135 now owns the unified product contract and implementation for durable Session identity, disposable body generations, truthful liveness, meaningful progress, write leases, safe recovery, pinned execution context, and cross-surface status. This Task was correctly scoped when process liveness was the immediate gap, but 2026-07-14 dogfood proved that liveness without progress and lease ownership still permits multi-hour silent stalls and duplicate writers. Keep one implementation and one worker: all remaining W2-139 acceptance criteria move to W2-135. W2-144 now depends on W2-135.","rank":32,"completed":true,"assignee":null},"reference":{"issue_url":"https://linear.app/loopflow/issue/LOO-174/absorbed-session-liveness-and-execution-context","workspace":null},"runtime":null,"next_move":{"owner":"project","reason":"Linear Task is complete"},"condition":{"state":"waiting","reason":"Linear Task is complete","observed_at":"2026-09-23T15:06:37.314852Z","evidence_age_secs":null,"local_progress":{"state":"not_applicable","unsettled":false,"dirty":null,"authored_commits":null,"recovery_required":null,"reason":null}},"actions":{"recommended":null,"reason":"Task is ready to start"},"active_pr":null,"section":"later"},{"task":{"id":"6f362006-6b35-4bbf-abee-7cc868490161","identifier":"LOO-175","name":"Guarantee every Task PR contains only that Task’s work","description":"User story\n\nWhen Loopflow launches and submits a Task, the resulting PR contains exactly the work authored for that Task—never an unpushed canonical-main commit, a sibling Task’s change, or hidden ancestry from a stale stack. A human can trust the PR range before review without reconstructing Git history.\n\nContract\n\n* Place new Task worktrees from a fetched `origin/<default>` commit when a remote exists; record that exact base as durable Task/PR evidence. A repository with no remote falls back explicitly to local main.\n* Treat canonical main ahead of its upstream as a control-plane violation and stop new placement before contamination spreads.\n* Before publication, prove the recorded base is compatible with current `origin/main`, the branch contains Task-authored changes, and the proposed PR range matches `lf task changes`.\n* Refuse a contaminated or ambiguous range before GitHub side effects, naming the foreign commits/files and the safe rebase or recovery action.\n* Keep readable branch names as hints. Placement metadata, commit ancestry, and Task PR sequence are authoritative.\n* Work with multi-PR Tasks: after each serial merge, the next PR starts from current origin/main while the stable Task worktree and history continue.\n\nProof\n\nIntegration tests reproduce an ahead-of-origin canonical main, a stale recorded base, a squash-merged parent, a no-remote repository, and a multi-PR continuation. Every safe case opens the intended minimal range; every unsafe case stops before push. In ten dogfood Task PRs, GitHub’s range, `lf task changes`, and the Task’s recorded base agree with zero manual commit dropping.\n\nOriginal evidence retained: W2-132/#877 and W2-130/#882 both inherited a foreign canonical-main commit and required manual repair. The old W2-141 scratch-file claim is not an acceptance criterion: submit intentionally clears scratch, so range correctness must be proven from durable Task and Git evidence instead.","rank":33,"completed":true,"assignee":null},"reference":{"issue_url":"https://linear.app/loopflow/issue/LOO-175/guarantee-every-task-pr-contains-only-that-tasks-work","workspace":{"slug":"prove-task-pr-range","branch":"jack-heart/prove-task-pr-range-2","worktree":"/Users/jack/src/loopflow.prove-task-pr-range"}},"runtime":{"work_id":"task_73c78de1ba8914670c438aa8ac5203d1","project_id":"proj_9f1fc19a84211aed8b8136e55c8ab1f3","routing_project_id":"proj_9f1fc19a84211aed8b8136e55c8ab1f3","status":"abandoned","reason":"abandoned","updated_at":"2026-07-21T17:28:19Z","provider":"claude"},"next_move":{"owner":"project","reason":"abandoned"},"condition":{"state":"blocked","reason":"Task LOO-175 worktree /Users/jack/src/loopflow.prove-task-pr-range is missing; restore that exact path before `lf task resume LOO-175`; Task identity and PR history are unchanged","observed_at":"2026-09-23T15:06:37.3149Z","evidence_age_secs":5521098,"local_progress":{"state":"missing","unsettled":true,"dirty":null,"authored_commits":null,"recovery_required":true,"reason":"Task LOO-175 worktree /Users/jack/src/loopflow.prove-task-pr-range is missing; restore that exact path before `lf task resume LOO-175`; Task identity and PR history are unchanged"}},"actions":{"recommended":"no_action","reason":"Task is terminal"},"active_pr":null,"section":"later"},{"task":{"id":"d4a4eb7c-bfd1-4bd5-a124-d64e92661bec","identifier":"LOO-176","name":"[absorbed] Converge partial Task creation safely","description":"Absorbed into active W2-135, “Make Session bodies leased, progress-aware, and recoverable.” Its real-concurrency acceptance cases remain required there: distinguish SQLITE_BUSY from UNIQUE, converge a reserved-but-unplaced Task, preserve terminal intent, and never turn run into an implicit restart of a body that already executed.","rank":34,"completed":true,"assignee":null},"reference":{"issue_url":"https://linear.app/loopflow/issue/LOO-176/absorbed-converge-partial-task-creation-safely","workspace":null},"runtime":null,"next_move":{"owner":"project","reason":"Linear Task is complete"},"condition":{"state":"waiting","reason":"Linear Task is complete","observed_at":"2026-09-23T15:06:37.317769Z","evidence_age_secs":null,"local_progress":{"state":"not_applicable","unsettled":false,"dirty":null,"authored_commits":null,"recovery_required":null,"reason":null}},"actions":{"recommended":null,"reason":"Task is ready to start"},"active_pr":null,"section":"later"},{"task":{"id":"ffeac343-6815-4ae9-9ae9-ff44d88ea59f","identifier":"LOO-177","name":"lf task run finishes partial creation; split BUSY from UNIQUE","description":"Closed as an exact duplicate of W2-137. W2-137 owns bounded SQLITE_BUSY retry, UNIQUE collision adoption, and convergence of partially created Task Sessions.","rank":35,"completed":true,"assignee":null},"reference":{"issue_url":"https://linear.app/loopflow/issue/LOO-177/lf-task-run-finishes-partial-creation-split-busy-from-unique","workspace":null},"runtime":null,"next_move":{"owner":"project","reason":"Linear Task is complete"},"condition":{"state":"waiting","reason":"Linear Task is complete","observed_at":"2026-09-23T15:06:37.31777Z","evidence_age_secs":null,"local_progress":{"state":"not_applicable","unsettled":false,"dirty":null,"authored_commits":null,"recovery_required":null,"reason":null}},"actions":{"recommended":null,"reason":"Task is ready to start"},"active_pr":null,"section":"later"},{"task":{"id":"295a9330-558c-49f6-8402-4de577551097","identifier":"LOO-178","name":"[retired] Make Session bodies leased, progress-aware, and recoverable","description":"Product thesis\n\nA Wave, Project, or Task is durable intent. A runner, provider turn, tmux session, PID, and process group are disposable bodies that temporarily act for that intent. Users should never have to manage those bodies, but they must always be able to see whether durable work is advancing, why it is not, and what Loopflow will do next. Wave, Project, and Task Sessions must share one coherent supervision model across CLI, Mac, iOS, chat, prompts, and worker processes.\n\nEvidence that this Task must absorb\n\n* On 2026-07-14 three Claude bodies slept for more than four hours while their Tasks still reported running because a PID and tmux session existed.\n* W2-132 previously produced two live Claude processes using one provider history and worktree. A status column was treated as a write lock.\n* Project processes died while child Tasks continued, leaving the durable hierarchy and the process hierarchy in disagreement.\n* Legacy Sessions without pinned execution context could not be relaunched safely. PR #882 correctly refused to guess.\n* Terminal Project pursuit could not create a successor until PR #894 separated terminal history from current work.\n* An unbounded SSH command held a turn indefinitely until PR #893.\n* PR #889 found two liveness paths in one snapshot disagreeing about whether tmux existed.\n* Partial Task creation, process restart, host restart, interrupt, abandonment, and external side effects all create boundaries where blind replay is unsafe.\n\nProduct contract\n\n1. Durable Session identity owns intent, directives, history, budget, relationships, worktree, PR sequence, terminal intent, and pinned execution context. It never derives identity from a process body.\n2. Every body generation has an explicit write lease: generation and lease token, process group, PID or tmux identity, provider session, pinned lf binary and store, start time, heartbeat, activity time, meaningful progress time, deadline, and terminal outcome.\n3. Exactly one generation may write, spawn, advance the flow, or report completion for a Session. Launch adopts a healthy body. Supersession atomically revokes the old lease, reaps its entire process group, and only then starts the successor. Stale generations become read-only and exit.\n4. Liveness and progress are different evidence. Persist the current flow step and command, last provider event, last durable mutation, activity age, progress age, and relevant deadline. A long command may be alive without producing output, but it must be named, bounded or explicitly extended, and interruptible.\n5. Desired intent and observed body state stay separate. The shared state model must express Working, Stalled, Recovering, NeedsInput, Stopped, Failed, Terminal, and Unobservable without collapsing them into one status string. Every state names the evidence, next owner, and legal controls.\n6. Recovery is automatic only at a proven replay-safe boundary. A body lost during an external side effect becomes control-uncertain or NeedsInput with the command and evidence preserved; Loopflow must not blindly repeat it. Terminal intent always wins and is never restarted.\n7. Supervisors recover the same durable Session and provider history. They never create parallel intent as a recovery mechanism. Host and process restarts must converge through the same state machine.\n8. The shared wire contract feeds CLI, Mac, iOS, chat, and the Now/Roadmap work views. Human surfaces show occasional clear updates and actionable state; detailed heartbeats and command evidence remain in audit. Use the existing database and append-only events, not a second monitor store.\n\nDelivery shape\n\nThis is one multi-PR Task with one stable worktree and provider history. Begin with an ambitious scratch design that audits W2-135, W2-139, PRs #882, #889, #893, #894, and the current supervisor and harness implementations. Write a one-screen user model, shared data types, a state-transition table, recovery policy, and serial PR boundaries before production changes. Keep one implementation across Wave, Project, and Task Sessions; do not add a Task-only watchdog beside existing supervision.\n\nExpected serial slices are: shared supervision and wire model; atomic generation/write lease and process-group ownership; progress lease plus safe recovery; cross-surface status and controls; deterministic end-to-end dogfood. Adjust the boundaries when the code proves a simpler sequence, but preserve the single product model.\n\nProof\n\n* A fake provider that stays alive but makes no meaningful progress becomes Stalled under a deterministic test clock, with current step or command and progress age visible.\n* Safe recovery reaps the entire old process group and resumes the same Session, worktree, provider history, and pinned context at generation plus one. Sampling proves live writers never exceed one.\n* A process or host restart adopts a valid body or recovers the same Session without duplicating work.\n* A lost body during an uncertain external side effect becomes NeedsInput and is not replayed.\n* Abandoned, completed, submitted, and otherwise terminal intent never restarts.\n* CLI and Swift DTO fixtures expose the same evidence, category, reason, next owner, and controls.\n* One intentional real dogfood stall is detected and recovered without a human discovering it from elapsed wall time.\n* Full Rust, Swift, migration, and smoke gates pass for each relevant slice.\n\nThis Task absorbs W2-139. W2-144 and its Now, Available, and Roadmap consumers should depend on this unified contract rather than inventing another liveness model.","rank":36,"completed":true,"assignee":null},"reference":{"issue_url":"https://linear.app/loopflow/issue/LOO-178/retired-make-session-bodies-leased-progress-aware-and-recoverable","workspace":{"slug":"make-session-bodies-leased-progress","branch":"jack-heart/make-session-bodies-leased-progress-stall-recovery-dogfood","worktree":"/Users/jack/src/loopflow.make-session-bodies-leased-progress"}},"runtime":{"work_id":"task_4069580b6426fe8ef6f8ce90d0670e55","project_id":"proj_9f1fc19a84211aed8b8136e55c8ab1f3","routing_project_id":"proj_9f1fc19a84211aed8b8136e55c8ab1f3","status":"abandoned","reason":"abandoned","updated_at":"2026-07-21T17:28:19Z","provider":"opencode"},"next_move":{"owner":"project","reason":"refresh reviewer-facing PR copy for the current head before settlement"},"condition":{"state":"blocked","reason":"Task LOO-178 worktree /Users/jack/src/loopflow.make-session-bodies-leased-progress is missing; restore that exact path on branch \"jack-heart/make-session-bodies-leased-progress-stall-recovery-dogfood\" before `lf task resume LOO-178`; Task identity and PR history are unchanged","observed_at":"2026-09-23T15:06:37.31806Z","evidence_age_secs":5521098,"local_progress":{"state":"missing","unsettled":true,"dirty":null,"authored_commits":null,"recovery_required":true,"reason":"Task LOO-178 worktree /Users/jack/src/loopflow.make-session-bodies-leased-progress is missing; restore that exact path on branch \"jack-heart/make-session-bodies-leased-progress-stall-recovery-dogfood\" before `lf task resume LOO-178`; Task identity and PR history are unchanged"}},"actions":{"recommended":"no_action","reason":"Task is terminal"},"active_pr":{"id":"pr_d22a986eee7348359aba09b2259ffa46","sequence":5,"slug":"stall-recovery-dogfood","branch":"jack-heart/make-session-bodies-leased-progress-stall-recovery-dogfood","base_commit":"d6910e607261d91798b1a941f771e8f26c55f778","phase":"open","empty":null,"publication":{"requested_at":"2026-07-16T13:13:48Z","presentation":null,"github":{"number":996,"url":"https://github.com/loopflowstudio/loopflow/pull/996"},"merge":null},"merge_commit":null,"abandoned_at":null},"section":"later"},{"task":{"id":"243bfd4a-7c60-40fe-8e72-ab57dd66d18b","identifier":"LOO-179","name":"Make Project and Task Session supervision recover safely","description":"Reproduce the W2-127 failures: stale tmux environment, branch-built lf opening the live registry, interrupt relaunching with the wrong executable, Project supervision restarting an unsafe Task, and abandoned or stopped sessions showing false state. Pin executable and LF_DB_PATH context, make interrupt and abandon terminal and observable, prevent supervisor restart after terminal intent, preserve worktrees and branches, and add end-to-end recovery tests.","rank":37,"completed":true,"assignee":null},"reference":{"issue_url":"https://linear.app/loopflow/issue/LOO-179/make-project-and-task-session-supervision-recover-safely","workspace":{"slug":"w2-130","branch":"jack-heart/w2-130","worktree":"/Users/jack/src/loopflow.w2-130"}},"runtime":{"work_id":"task_2851571016b4d8fb88d289f8e6fde0f3","project_id":"proj_9f1fc19a84211aed8b8136e55c8ab1f3","routing_project_id":"proj_9f1fc19a84211aed8b8136e55c8ab1f3","status":"done","reason":"done","updated_at":"2026-07-21T17:28:19Z","provider":"claude"},"next_move":{"owner":"project","reason":"done"},"condition":{"state":"blocked","reason":"Task LOO-179 worktree /Users/jack/src/loopflow.w2-130 is missing; restore that exact path before `lf task resume LOO-179`; Task identity and PR history are unchanged","observed_at":"2026-09-23T15:06:37.32044Z","evidence_age_secs":5521098,"local_progress":{"state":"missing","unsettled":true,"dirty":null,"authored_commits":null,"recovery_required":true,"reason":"Task LOO-179 worktree /Users/jack/src/loopflow.w2-130 is missing; restore that exact path before `lf task resume LOO-179`; Task identity and PR history are unchanged"}},"actions":{"recommended":"no_action","reason":"Task is terminal"},"active_pr":null,"section":"later"},{"task":{"id":"8e77a60f-71e7-4e73-8471-2a1d9c2deb58","identifier":"LOO-180","name":"lf pm show --json emits no projects/synced_at; Swift plan decode breaks","description":"This branch added Swift RegistryQuery.plan()/PmShowSnapshot expecting lf pm show --json to carry a 'projects' array (slug/name/summary/definition/krs) plus 'synced_at'. The CLI actually emits {initiative, items, project, provider, wave} only — item-level fields (description, rank, project, assignee) match, but the project-level plan does not. As non-optional Codable fields the decode throws, so the Mac wave plan renders objective-only with zero projects.\n\nAlso: lf pm sync still writes wave/<wave>/projects/*.md markdown cache, which the Linear-owned PM design (scratch/pm-linear-source.md, now folded to MEMORY) says should not exist. Decide the wire contract: either lf pm show --json emits projects+synced_at from the SQLite snapshot (and sync populates it) and drops markdown rendering, or the Swift model reverts to reading files. Pick one source.","rank":38,"completed":true,"assignee":null},"reference":{"issue_url":"https://linear.app/loopflow/issue/LOO-180/lf-pm-show-json-emits-no-projectssynced-at-swift-plan-decode-breaks","workspace":null},"runtime":null,"next_move":{"owner":"project","reason":"Linear Task is complete"},"condition":{"state":"waiting","reason":"Linear Task is complete","observed_at":"2026-09-23T15:06:37.321829Z","evidence_age_secs":null,"local_progress":{"state":"not_applicable","unsettled":false,"dirty":null,"authored_commits":null,"recovery_required":null,"reason":null}},"actions":{"recommended":null,"reason":"Task is ready to start"},"active_pr":null,"section":"later"},{"task":{"id":"5bb2acde-4682-48d6-a868-ce85bf3c847b","identifier":"LOO-181","name":"[obsolete] lfd-owned Wave identity","description":"Closed as obsolete. lfd is no longer the product owner of execution or Wave identity, repository GOAL/MEMORY remain the current authored Wave context, and W2-88 now owns the explicit user-owned Home contract (jack@local or SSH address) inherited through Project and Task work. Reviving an lfd master-copy/export/pull system would restore a second source of truth and conflict with the current architecture.","rank":39,"completed":true,"assignee":null},"reference":{"issue_url":"https://linear.app/loopflow/issue/LOO-181/obsolete-lfd-owned-wave-identity","workspace":null},"runtime":null,"next_move":{"owner":"project","reason":"Linear Task is complete"},"condition":{"state":"waiting","reason":"Linear Task is complete","observed_at":"2026-09-23T15:06:37.32183Z","evidence_age_secs":null,"local_progress":{"state":"not_applicable","unsettled":false,"dirty":null,"authored_commits":null,"recovery_required":null,"reason":null}},"actions":{"recommended":null,"reason":"Task is ready to start"},"active_pr":null,"section":"later"},{"task":{"id":"b1ef4c76-8bbf-4a11-b210-d89132be8564","identifier":"LOO-182","name":"PM API: wave/project/task pass (superseded by infrastructure task; CLI shipped)","description":"Load-bearing against amnesia: scratch/ is cleared on land, so the design doc survives only at commit 2f27ffcb. Summary: wave=local dir, project=wave/<w>/projects/<p>.md, task=Linear issue labeled project:<slug>; PM space = Linear container (stop calling it a project). Commands: pm status/doctor/sync --plan/sync, show/update --wave --project, space rename, task move/import. Sync applies only low-risk changes; ambiguous moves stay in the plan. Fix the GraphQL String!-vs-ID mismatch while in the layer. STRANDED CONTAINERS holding live receipts: fbdd6124 (ex goals/datamodel — flowloop chain: steward brief 606d59b7, v1b 33a98266, v1c ac851c0b, project-tier bf2d8709, bare-fallback a9dc614d, recreated architecture items 9b295516/a99948c1/187e8e1a, Swift cleanup 99bc76fc, skills-own-projects e8bc7f23 which is DONE via PR #852 and needs closing after import), 8c4ba3f9 (ex architecture), 6cf881ef (ex memory). Migrate: mac->product 9ee88f2a stays, quality->intelligence 0e2c75ee stays, systems->infrastructure 7cf1518e stays.","rank":40,"completed":true,"assignee":null},"reference":{"issue_url":"https://linear.app/loopflow/issue/LOO-182/pm-api-waveprojecttask-pass-superseded-by-infrastructure-task-cli","workspace":null},"runtime":null,"next_move":{"owner":"project","reason":"Linear Task is complete"},"condition":{"state":"waiting","reason":"Linear Task is complete","observed_at":"2026-09-23T15:06:37.32183Z","evidence_age_secs":null,"local_progress":{"state":"not_applicable","unsettled":false,"dirty":null,"authored_commits":null,"recovery_required":null,"reason":null}},"actions":{"recommended":null,"reason":"Task is ready to start"},"active_pr":null,"section":"later"},{"task":{"id":"cc84a449-3b12-486c-bf6d-ab9ccde93230","identifier":"LOO-183","name":"Long tail: crons UI, remote compute, mobile","description":"Closed. A parking lot is not a concrete Task. File a narrow Task under the owning Project only when crons UI, a second remote host, or a mobile product decision produces executable work.","rank":41,"completed":true,"assignee":null},"reference":{"issue_url":"https://linear.app/loopflow/issue/LOO-183/long-tail-crons-ui-remote-compute-mobile","workspace":null},"runtime":null,"next_move":{"owner":"project","reason":"Linear Task is complete"},"condition":{"state":"waiting","reason":"Linear Task is complete","observed_at":"2026-09-23T15:06:37.321831Z","evidence_age_secs":null,"local_progress":{"state":"not_applicable","unsettled":false,"dirty":null,"authored_commits":null,"recovery_required":null,"reason":null}},"actions":{"recommended":null,"reason":"Task is ready to start"},"active_pr":null,"section":"later"},{"task":{"id":"e229f364-09a6-4a16-a241-7f901cfca14f","identifier":"LOO-184","name":"Converse with one Wave through one Discord channel","description":"## Outcome\n\nA human and one real running Wave converse in one existing company Discord channel. A human message becomes durable Wave input, the Wave response appears in Discord, and a listener restart loses or duplicates neither side.\n\n> \"the wave is basically the stand in for the human, offering judgment and direction.\"\n\n## Contract\n\n* Discord is the canonical shared chat; Loopflow retains the external reference and exact Run input/output for evidence, not a second company transcript.\n* Bind one explicitly configured existing guild channel to one Wave. Do not provision categories, shared rooms, threads, or wave-specific identities yet.\n* The Wave listener owns polling, cursor, journal-first idempotent delivery, resident wake, and outbound receipt. The resident owns judgment.\n* Initial binding starts at the current channel head. Thereafter restart catches up after the last committed message.\n* Deduplicate inbound messages by provider/channel/message identity. Record outbound intent before send and reconcile the provider message ID after send.\n* Read the Discord token only from Doppler/env. Never print it or pass it into provider children.\n* Use only permissions exercised here: view channel, read history, read message content, and send messages.\n* Do not restore the deleted generic bus or add Gateway machinery before polling load proves it necessary.\n\n## Demo and done when\n\nPost \"summarize your current objective\" in the bound channel and watch the real Wave answer. Restart its listener, post a second message, and receive one response. The trace shows exactly two source-linked human inputs and their assistant outputs. Tests cover first attach at head, ordered catch-up, duplicate fetch, crash between journal and cursor, outbound send reconciliation, self-echo rejection, missing permissions, and secret scrubbing.","rank":42,"completed":true,"assignee":null},"reference":{"issue_url":"https://linear.app/loopflow/issue/LOO-184/converse-with-one-wave-through-one-discord-channel","workspace":{"slug":"converse-with-one-wave-through","branch":"jack-heart/converse-with-one-wave-through","worktree":"/Users/jack/src/loopflow.converse-with-one-wave-through"}},"runtime":{"work_id":"task_123381b4bc954de9a3e0c0d4ed32fa01","project_id":"proj_9f1fc19a84211aed8b8136e55c8ab1f3","routing_project_id":"proj_9f1fc19a84211aed8b8136e55c8ab1f3","status":"done","reason":"done","updated_at":"2026-07-21T17:28:19Z","provider":"codex"},"next_move":{"owner":"project","reason":"done"},"condition":{"state":"blocked","reason":"Task LOO-184 worktree /Users/jack/src/loopflow.converse-with-one-wave-through is missing; restore that exact path before `lf task resume LOO-184`; Task identity and PR history are unchanged","observed_at":"2026-09-23T15:06:37.321993Z","evidence_age_secs":5521098,"local_progress":{"state":"missing","unsettled":true,"dirty":null,"authored_commits":null,"recovery_required":true,"reason":"Task LOO-184 worktree /Users/jack/src/loopflow.converse-with-one-wave-through is missing; restore that exact path before `lf task resume LOO-184`; Task identity and PR history are unchanged"}},"actions":{"recommended":"no_action","reason":"Task is terminal"},"active_pr":null,"section":"later"},{"task":{"id":"923cdfdb-aecd-4752-98bc-77091455f880","identifier":"LOO-186","name":"Let relevant Waves share one Discord room without a roll call","description":"## Outcome\n\nEvery running Wave listens to the company Loopflow channel. Most human messages receive one relevant Wave response; other Waves remain silent unless they have distinct context or need a question answered.\n\n> \"People should assume that most things need response from exactly one person, but they also shouldnt be afraid to share if tehy have additional relevant perspective, or ask questions if needed.\"\n\n## Contract\n\n* A message in a Wave channel addresses that Wave. An unaddressed shared-channel message reaches every running Wave.\n* Exactly-one is a social and prompt contract, not distributed consensus. Do not add a coordinator or arbiter before measured duplicate responses justify it.\n* Silence is valid: a Wave can absorb company direction and later steer its children without acknowledging every message.\n* Preserve shared-channel messages across downtime as ordered pending input. Consume large backlogs in bounded batches without silent truncation.\n* Record response count, irrelevant responses, context tokens, pending age, and which later child Steers cite a shared message.\n* Stable Loopflow authorship prevents self-loops while allowing Waves to hear one another.\n\n## Demo and done when\n\nPost one Wave-specific request, one cross-Wave priority update, and one unplaced idea. The relevant Wave answers the first, affected Waves absorb the second, and the idea ends with a clear owner without a roll call. A restart during backlog processing preserves every unconsumed message. One week of samples reports response-count and context-cost evidence rather than claiming routing quality from a synthetic test alone.","rank":44,"completed":true,"assignee":null},"reference":{"issue_url":"https://linear.app/loopflow/issue/LOO-186/let-relevant-waves-share-one-discord-room-without-a-roll-call","workspace":null},"runtime":null,"next_move":{"owner":"project","reason":"Linear Task is complete"},"condition":{"state":"waiting","reason":"Linear Task is complete","observed_at":"2026-09-23T15:06:37.324033Z","evidence_age_secs":null,"local_progress":{"state":"not_applicable","unsettled":false,"dirty":null,"authored_commits":null,"recovery_required":null,"reason":null}},"actions":{"recommended":null,"reason":"Task is ready to start"},"active_pr":null,"section":"later"},{"task":{"id":"63b06501-60e3-45ec-b594-1586a9f5c1de","identifier":"LOO-187","name":"Enforce Wave fleet capacity and explain idle work","description":"## Outcome\n\nLong-running Waves cannot create runaway agent or token churn, and the system can explain why ready Work is or is not running.\n\n## Contract\n\n* Enforce explicit concurrency and token budgets through Run reservation across Wave -> Project -> Task, not prompts alone.\n* A child cannot escape its ancestor cap. Replacement bodies do not double-count capacity.\n* Expose open-agent count, five-minute completed output tok/s, cumulative usage, cap, remaining capacity, and exhaustion reason by Wave and fleet.\n* Distinguish healthy idle, gated, capacity-blocked, credential-blocked, paused, stalled, and unexplained idle.\n* Do not collapse orthogonal facts into a synthetic health score.\n* Build on `lf ps`/`lf top`, Work placement, Run leases, and shared status projections.\n\n## Demo and done when\n\nSet a small fleet cap, let several Waves compete for Work, and prove reservations never exceed it. Completing or pausing Work releases capacity and the next eligible Work advances. Every non-running ready Task names its owner and blocking fact. Deterministic tests cover nested caps, retry/replacement, stale processes, and concurrent reservation.","rank":45,"completed":true,"assignee":null},"reference":{"issue_url":"https://linear.app/loopflow/issue/LOO-187/enforce-wave-fleet-capacity-and-explain-idle-work","workspace":null},"runtime":null,"next_move":{"owner":"project","reason":"Linear Task is complete"},"condition":{"state":"waiting","reason":"Linear Task is complete","observed_at":"2026-09-23T15:06:37.324034Z","evidence_age_secs":null,"local_progress":{"state":"not_applicable","unsettled":false,"dirty":null,"authored_commits":null,"recovery_required":null,"reason":null}},"actions":{"recommended":null,"reason":"Task is ready to start"},"active_pr":null,"section":"later"},{"task":{"id":"48c08025-959d-4983-898b-a402888611d4","identifier":"LOO-188","name":"Prove Loopflow Live for one uninterrupted week","description":"## Outcome\n\nLoopflow demonstrates that long-running Wave operation is trustworthy under real work, not merely in a restart test.\n\n## Preconditions\n\nBegin after Discord shared chat, durable residency, fleet capacity, activity/composite updates, fleet snapshot, and the control-room path are usable. SCI-1 and PRD-11 provide complete evidence and claim provenance.\n\n## Proof window\n\nRun at least five desired-running Waves across Loopflow and Cadenza for seven uninterrupted days, on at least two Homes, in one company Discord. Record every pause, listener/resident restart, Discord gap, duplicate or irrelevant response, unexplained idle period, manual rescue, budget escape, raw-log fallback, and UI evidence mismatch.\n\n## Closure criteria\n\n* Desired-running Waves recover; durable pauses stay paused.\n* Tested Discord delivery has zero silent loss and zero unexplained duplicates.\n* The spawn chain never exceeds its caps.\n* Every non-running ready Task has an actionable reason.\n* Every child Steer and composite claim resolves to evidence.\n* The app answers current work, change, attention, and proof without a terminal.\n* Blocking counterexamples are fixed through their owning project. They are not waived or rewritten as success.\n\nThe Task closes on the seven-day evidence record and linked fixes, not on starting the soak.","rank":46,"completed":true,"assignee":null},"reference":{"issue_url":"https://linear.app/loopflow/issue/LOO-188/prove-loopflow-live-for-one-uninterrupted-week","workspace":null},"runtime":null,"next_move":{"owner":"project","reason":"Linear Task is complete"},"condition":{"state":"waiting","reason":"Linear Task is complete","observed_at":"2026-09-23T15:06:37.324034Z","evidence_age_secs":null,"local_progress":{"state":"not_applicable","unsettled":false,"dirty":null,"authored_commits":null,"recovery_required":null,"reason":null}},"actions":{"recommended":null,"reason":"Task is ready to start"},"active_pr":null,"section":"later"},{"task":{"id":"f31fbcb6-2e4f-47a0-a093-9887b12efc10","identifier":"LOO-189","name":"Persist and reconcile Wave running versus paused intent","description":"## Outcome\n\nA user can keep Waves alive for weeks or pause one deliberately without process killing, surprise restart, or interference with manual work.\n\n## Contract\n\n* Persist desired Wave residency as `running` or `paused`; keep it distinct from listener, resident, provider-body, and Work state.\n* `lf start` records running intent. `lf stop` records paused intent. A pause survives `lfd`, listener, and machine restart.\n* `lfd` remains the one keeper per Home and reconciles locally placed running Waves. It never chooses product work.\n* Apply bounded restart backoff and surface crash loops with reason, attempt count, and next retry.\n* Reuse the shared disposable-body supervision contract in PRD-10; do not create a second Task-only or Wave-only liveness vocabulary.\n* Preserve ENG-120 as a concrete first-start/no-endpoint acceptance case.\n\n## Demo and done when\n\nRun several Waves, kill one listener and one resident, pause another, then restart `lfd`. Desired-running Waves recover on their placed Home; the paused Wave stays off. First-start partial failure is retry-safe and actionable. CLI and Swift fixtures show desired intent and each observed layer independently.","rank":47,"completed":true,"assignee":null},"reference":{"issue_url":"https://linear.app/loopflow/issue/LOO-189/persist-and-reconcile-wave-running-versus-paused-intent","workspace":null},"runtime":null,"next_move":{"owner":"project","reason":"Linear Task is complete"},"condition":{"state":"waiting","reason":"Linear Task is complete","observed_at":"2026-09-23T15:06:37.324035Z","evidence_age_secs":null,"local_progress":{"state":"not_applicable","unsettled":false,"dirty":null,"authored_commits":null,"recovery_required":null,"reason":null}},"actions":{"recommended":null,"reason":"Task is ready to start"},"active_pr":null,"section":"later"},{"task":{"id":"3c42d477-ac56-4f6e-8aa3-953766566b8b","identifier":"LOO-190","name":"Expose one active Wave chat backing without split-brain delivery","description":"> “the non-discord chat maybe is still something we should offer if discord integration isnt turn on”\n\nMake local Wave chat the default active backing and Discord an optional replacement for future messages. Expose a closed local-or-Discord backing and conversation epoch through the product API. When Discord is active, a Loopflow-authored message must route honestly to Discord or be rejected with an Open-in-Discord action; it must never disappear into a parallel local conversation. Project Discord history on demand without storing a duplicate transcript. Preserve prior local history as a readable earlier epoch.\n\nDone when the same Wave can operate fully in local mode, switch to a Discord binding without dual-write or split-brain compose, and every rendered message names its durable local or Discord source.","rank":48,"completed":true,"assignee":null},"reference":{"issue_url":"https://linear.app/loopflow/issue/LOO-190/expose-one-active-wave-chat-backing-without-split-brain-delivery","workspace":{"slug":"expose-one-active-wave-chat","branch":"jack-heart/expose-one-active-wave-chat","worktree":"/Users/jack/src/loopflow.expose-one-active-wave-chat"}},"runtime":{"work_id":"task_9ef67f38cebc44bebc98b75204c179cd","project_id":"proj_9f1fc19a84211aed8b8136e55c8ab1f3","routing_project_id":"proj_9f1fc19a84211aed8b8136e55c8ab1f3","status":"abandoned","reason":"abandoned","updated_at":"2026-07-21T17:28:19Z","provider":"codex"},"next_move":{"owner":"project","reason":"abandoned"},"condition":{"state":"blocked","reason":"Task LOO-190 worktree /Users/jack/src/loopflow.expose-one-active-wave-chat is missing; restore that exact path before `lf task resume LOO-190`; Task identity and PR history are unchanged","observed_at":"2026-09-23T15:06:37.324117Z","evidence_age_secs":5521098,"local_progress":{"state":"missing","unsettled":true,"dirty":null,"authored_commits":null,"recovery_required":true,"reason":"Task LOO-190 worktree /Users/jack/src/loopflow.expose-one-active-wave-chat is missing; restore that exact path before `lf task resume LOO-190`; Task identity and PR history are unchanged"}},"actions":{"recommended":"no_action","reason":"Task is terminal"},"active_pr":null,"section":"later"},{"task":{"id":"9ca0428d-bb19-446f-b7ef-ff3f7d7c5336","identifier":"LOO-191","name":"Loopflow work moves to LOO without losing Task continuity","description":"Intent\n\nAfter repository-scoped Linear Teams ship, migrate the Loopflow repository's Waves from their current per-Wave Teams onto one Loopflow Team with key LOO.\n\nThis is a separate consequential migration, not part of proving the new data model. Existing Task UUIDs, Projects, Initiatives, durable Work, PR links, branch history, and active or recoverable Sessions must remain attributable after human-readable issue identifiers change.\n\nScope\n\n* Create or adopt the LOO Team as Loopflow's sole repository Team.\n* Move Loopflow Projects and unsettled Tasks from legacy Wave Teams to LOO through supported Loopflow operations.\n* Preserve each Project's exactly-one Wave association and apply canonical Wave-qualified Project titles.\n* Verify settled historical Tasks remain inspectable even if they are not physically migrated.\n* Do not archive or delete legacy Teams until all open work and recovery references are proven safe and a human explicitly chooses cleanup.\n\nDone when\n\n* Every open Loopflow Task is on LOO and resolves to the same Wave and Project as before migration.\n* Active, waiting, review, merged, abandoned, and recoverable Task states retain their legal actions.\n* Existing PR attachments, UUID-based references, roadmap entries, and worktree/task status remain coherent.\n* No current Project or Task is stranded on a legacy Team.\n* A before/after inventory records changed human issue keys and stable UUIDs.\n* Loopflow's real Waves can run, sync, create a Task, publish a PR attachment, and recover a Task after migration.\n* Legacy Team cleanup is presented separately and is not performed implicitly.","rank":49,"completed":true,"assignee":null},"reference":{"issue_url":"https://linear.app/loopflow/issue/LOO-191/loopflow-work-moves-to-loo-without-losing-task-continuity","workspace":null},"runtime":null,"next_move":{"owner":"project","reason":"Linear Task is complete"},"condition":{"state":"waiting","reason":"Linear Task is complete","observed_at":"2026-09-23T15:06:37.326442Z","evidence_age_secs":null,"local_progress":{"state":"not_applicable","unsettled":false,"dirty":null,"authored_commits":null,"recovery_required":null,"reason":null}},"actions":{"recommended":null,"reason":"Task is ready to start"},"active_pr":null,"section":"later"},{"task":{"id":"c2295698-9083-4b92-8f93-5a7b9c7fe612","identifier":"LOO-192","name":"One repository owns one Linear team across all of its Waves","description":"Intent\n\n“Specifically, I want to make it so that each repo gets one team, so we'll have LOO for Loopflow. And then just put the wave name in each project so that it's obvious what the project is part of. This also makes sense for potentially larger nesting of waves because if you want to have a large nesting I don't think you want a lot of teams.”\n\nChange the Linear sizing invariant from one Team per Wave to one Team per repository.\n\nTarget model\n\n* Repository: one stable Linear Team and issue-key namespace.\n* Wave: one Linear Initiative and durable operating context; Waves may be nested without creating Teams.\n* Project: exactly one Wave-owned measured bet. Its visible Linear title includes the canonical Wave path.\n* Task: one Linear issue on the repository Team, resolved to its Wave through its exactly-one Project relationship rather than through Team ownership.\n\nExamples\n\n* Loopflow repository Team: LOO.\n* Hootro repository Team: HOO.\n* Project title: Survival — A real task reaches done.\n* Nested project title: Survival / Infrastructure — Gmail.\n\nThe title path is redundant human orientation, not the source of truth. Stable IDs and Initiative/Project associations remain authoritative. Use the canonical Wave ancestry so equal leaf names in different branches remain legible.\n\nConstraints\n\n* A repository may bind only one Linear Team. All of its Waves reuse that binding.\n* Two different repositories must not silently claim the same Team.\n* A Project still belongs to exactly one Wave even though its Team no longer identifies the Wave.\n* Task and Project resolution must remain deterministic from UUIDs and Project membership.\n* Existing Wave nesting, status, roadmap, task execution, PR lifecycle, and worktree ownership must not depend on unique Team prefixes.\n* Repo-scoped PM authority should have one durable configuration owner rather than duplicated per-Wave values that can drift.\n* Partial rollout must fail closed; do not leave some commands resolving Wave by Team while others resolve by Project.\n\nDemo\n\nIn one fixture repository, initialize two sibling or parent/child Waves against one Team key. Create one Project under each, see Wave-qualified titles, create Tasks that share the same issue prefix, and resolve each Task back to the correct Wave through status, roadmap, task run, and project controls. A second repository attempting to claim the same Team is refused actionably.\n\nDone when\n\n* The repository-to-Team invariant is represented durably and validated by pm init, sync, project/task creation, resolution, and doctor surfaces.\n* Multiple Waves in one repository share one Team without ambiguity.\n* Project titles include canonical Wave paths, including nesting.\n* Task-to-Wave resolution uses exactly-one Project ownership, not exclusive Team ownership.\n* The full Wave-resolution and PM lifecycle test matrix covers same-repo sharing, nested Waves, cross-repo collision, duplicate Project association, restart, and migration compatibility.\n* Documentation and recovery errors describe repository-scoped Teams consistently.\n\nThis is one architectural change: internal implementation may proceed in slices, but it should ship only when all planning and task consumers agree on the new invariant.","rank":50,"completed":true,"assignee":null},"reference":{"issue_url":"https://linear.app/loopflow/issue/LOO-192/one-repository-owns-one-linear-team-across-all-of-its-waves","workspace":{"slug":"one-repository-owns-one-linear","branch":"jack-heart/one-repository-owns-one-linear","worktree":"/Users/jack/src/loopflow.one-repository-owns-one-linear"}},"runtime":{"work_id":"task_8ad790387a4049c088754e0bd49c25d0","project_id":"proj_9f1fc19a84211aed8b8136e55c8ab1f3","routing_project_id":"proj_9f1fc19a84211aed8b8136e55c8ab1f3","status":"abandoned","reason":"abandoned","updated_at":"2026-07-21T17:28:19Z","provider":"codex"},"next_move":{"owner":"project","reason":"abandoned"},"condition":{"state":"blocked","reason":"Task LOO-192 worktree /Users/jack/src/loopflow.one-repository-owns-one-linear is missing; restore that exact path before `lf task resume LOO-192`; Task identity and PR history are unchanged","observed_at":"2026-09-23T15:06:37.326764Z","evidence_age_secs":5521098,"local_progress":{"state":"missing","unsettled":true,"dirty":null,"authored_commits":null,"recovery_required":true,"reason":"Task LOO-192 worktree /Users/jack/src/loopflow.one-repository-owns-one-linear is missing; restore that exact path before `lf task resume LOO-192`; Task identity and PR history are unchanged"}},"actions":{"recommended":"no_action","reason":"Task is terminal"},"active_pr":null,"section":"later"},{"task":{"id":"0cc9440c-5d15-4d10-8ec1-f9b3577248b1","identifier":"LOO-193","name":"[retired] Make Task recommended actions agree with legal lifecycle commands","description":"## Problem\n\nA durable Task can advertise a supervisor action that its command boundary refuses. On 2026-07-18, PRD-20 reported status=waiting, actions.recommended=resume, and resume available because requested changes should be addressed. Both lf task resume PRD-20 --model codex and lf task follow-up PRD-20 then refused: PR #1052 is submitted and in review, so only the reviewer may advance it.\n\nThis makes shared status and next-action evidence untrustworthy and strands a headless Project pursuit at an action Loopflow itself says is legal.\n\n## Contract\n\nDerive recommended actions and command authorization from one lifecycle decision. A submitted Task in review must either expose the actual review action and Human/Project owner, or accept the advertised supervisor action when the review disposition makes that legal. Never recommend an action the corresponding command will reject for the same unchanged snapshot.\n\nKeep required InteractionReview authority intact. Do not self-approve, bypass review, or make an open PR permission to restart work.\n\n## Proof\n\nAdd a lifecycle regression covering the exact PRD-20 shape: submitted open PR, required review, requested changes or unresolved disposition, no live body. Assert task status, roadmap/next owner, and each legal CLI action agree before and after review disposition and restart. CLI and shared DTO consumers must render the same owner and next action.\n\n## KR\n\nAdvances the Task-loop trust streak: every stopped Task must expose an actionable non-convergence record with a legal next action, never a silent stall or false repair instruction.","rank":51,"completed":true,"assignee":null},"reference":{"issue_url":"https://linear.app/loopflow/issue/LOO-193/retired-make-task-recommended-actions-agree-with-legal-lifecycle","workspace":{"slug":"make-task-recommended-actions-agree","branch":"jack-heart/make-task-recommended-actions-agree","worktree":"/Users/jack/src/loopflow.make-task-recommended-actions-agree"}},"runtime":{"work_id":"task_c1a44ebdda399351bb625d127dcaed3a","project_id":"proj_9f1fc19a84211aed8b8136e55c8ab1f3","routing_project_id":"proj_9f1fc19a84211aed8b8136e55c8ab1f3","status":"abandoned","reason":"abandoned","updated_at":"2026-07-21T17:28:19Z","provider":"codex"},"next_move":{"owner":"project","reason":"abandoned"},"condition":{"state":"blocked","reason":"Task LOO-193 worktree /Users/jack/src/loopflow.make-task-recommended-actions-agree is missing; restore that exact path on branch \"jack-heart/make-task-recommended-actions-agree\" before `lf task resume LOO-193`; Task identity and PR history are unchanged","observed_at":"2026-09-23T15:06:37.329045Z","evidence_age_secs":5521098,"local_progress":{"state":"missing","unsettled":true,"dirty":null,"authored_commits":null,"recovery_required":true,"reason":"Task LOO-193 worktree /Users/jack/src/loopflow.make-task-recommended-actions-agree is missing; restore that exact path on branch \"jack-heart/make-task-recommended-actions-agree\" before `lf task resume LOO-193`; Task identity and PR history are unchanged"}},"actions":{"recommended":"no_action","reason":"Task is terminal"},"active_pr":{"id":"pr_eef9be5b9f0d48c6a3e1e11afe0f8abc","sequence":1,"slug":"make-task-recommended-actions-agree","branch":"jack-heart/make-task-recommended-actions-agree","base_commit":"7db6ddf045e48afcf88c3aeafa639e114b9a3e40","phase":"working","empty":null,"publication":null,"merge_commit":null,"abandoned_at":null},"section":"later"},{"task":{"id":"921fafdf-25a2-433f-adc0-9b1ca3aaa9ff","identifier":"LOO-194","name":"Recover a Run across accounts and providers","description":"<!-- loopflow-task-start:8bd290370bc1f6d9d944478b4b3edd6f2794637996a759632dfd8f2a6436b566 -->","rank":52,"completed":true,"assignee":null},"reference":{"issue_url":"https://linear.app/loopflow/issue/LOO-194/recover-a-run-across-accounts-and-providers","workspace":{"slug":"recover-run-routing","branch":"jack-heart/recover-run-routing-2","worktree":"/Users/jack/src/loopflow.recover-run-routing"}},"runtime":{"work_id":"task_8e08e49c2f013a4fa0f686362c859836","project_id":"proj_9f1fc19a84211aed8b8136e55c8ab1f3","routing_project_id":"proj_9f1fc19a84211aed8b8136e55c8ab1f3","status":"abandoned","reason":"abandoned","updated_at":"2026-07-21T17:28:19Z","provider":"codex"},"next_move":{"owner":"project","reason":"abandoned"},"condition":{"state":"blocked","reason":"Task LOO-194 worktree /Users/jack/src/loopflow.recover-run-routing is missing; restore that exact path before `lf task resume LOO-194`; Task identity and PR history are unchanged","observed_at":"2026-09-23T15:06:37.335925Z","evidence_age_secs":5521098,"local_progress":{"state":"missing","unsettled":true,"dirty":null,"authored_commits":null,"recovery_required":true,"reason":"Task LOO-194 worktree /Users/jack/src/loopflow.recover-run-routing is missing; restore that exact path before `lf task resume LOO-194`; Task identity and PR history are unchanged"}},"actions":{"recommended":"no_action","reason":"Task is terminal"},"active_pr":null,"section":"later"},{"task":{"id":"caa6efc5-d7ca-4912-9e67-89918f4e82fe","identifier":"LOO-195","name":"[retired] Make review supervisors observable and patient","description":"Problem\n\nReview supervisors currently infer body health from indirect signals: whether the worktree changed and the last line visible in the tmux control pane. This can turn patient agent work into a restart loop.\n\nIncident evidence: PRD-39 review ir_84622b87f9b047cb8a1261d74733eb56 on 2026-07-18.\n\n* The control pane remained on `preparing launch prompt`, an info line emitted before prompt assembly at rust/loopflow/src/lf/commands/run.rs:169. Provider progress is not rendered there, so the line was stale presentation rather than current state.\n* Codex generation 1 actively processed the review for 4m23s: it read review-design, the 394-line design, questions, and surrounding account code, and described the planned rewrite. The Project interrupted it before its first edit.\n* Generation 2 actively processed for 2m32s, including context compaction and further source inspection, then was interrupted.\n* Generation 3 actively processed for 2m16s, then was interrupted.\n* All three provider rollouts ended with `turn_aborted: interrupted`; none emitted a provider failure.\n* The Project nevertheless recorded `Codex launch prompt remained stuck` and handed the Task to OpenCode.\n* OpenCode produced the rewrite after roughly six uninterrupted minutes. The difference was patience, not provider health.\n\nScope\n\nAudit the complete reviewer decision surface: APIs, status projections, command receipts, event streams, attach/control output, and provider-neutral activity evidence. Determine whether Project and Wave reviewers receive enough timely information to distinguish queued input, prompt assembly, a working Turn, a quiet Turn, provider failure, and dead containment. Make supervision consume that truthful evidence.\n\nDo not redesign the authored Review API or interaction protocol in this task. Treat that as a separate product effort; this task owns the evidence and liveness surface reviewers use when deciding whether to wait, message, interrupt, or hand off.\n\nDone when\n\n1. The design inventories every input currently available to a reviewer and records what each proves and cannot prove, including `lf task status`, Review messages and receipts, Run/Launch/Turn events, provider streams, and tmux control output.\n2. A provider-neutral reviewer projection or stream distinguishes prompt assembly, an active provider Turn, a quiet but live Turn, queued/delivered input, a typed provider failure, and proven-missing containment. Codex, Claude, and OpenCode yield the same decision semantics even when their native streams differ.\n3. Reviewer-facing output exposes the current transition, latest trustworthy activity, and command delivery state without requiring raw provider transcripts or private reasoning.\n4. No supervisor interrupt, retry, or provider handoff is legal solely because no diff, receipt, or visible provider output appeared within an ad hoc wall-clock interval. Quiet live agents remain live.\n5. Automatic interrupt or handoff requires one of: an explicit User instruction, a typed provider failure whose recovery policy permits replacement, or proven-missing exact containment. The durable event records the triggering evidence.\n6. A regression fixture holds a review Turn open longer than the former observation window while it emits provider activity but no file edit; the supervisor receives useful liveness updates and neither interrupts nor changes provider.\n7. A second fixture emits a typed provider failure and proves the supervisor performs exactly one legal recovery action.\n8. The PRD-39 incident can be replayed without generating multiple Codex bodies or an unsupported OpenCode handoff, and the reviewer output makes the correct wait decision obvious.","rank":53,"completed":true,"assignee":null},"reference":{"issue_url":"https://linear.app/loopflow/issue/LOO-195/retired-make-review-supervisors-observable-and-patient","workspace":{"slug":"make-review-supervisors-observable-and","branch":"jack-heart/make-review-supervisors-observable-and","worktree":"/Users/jack/src/loopflow.make-review-supervisors-observable-and"}},"runtime":{"work_id":"task_4774e5ff5a824fb2438ca5b5b16df593","project_id":"proj_9f1fc19a84211aed8b8136e55c8ab1f3","routing_project_id":"proj_9f1fc19a84211aed8b8136e55c8ab1f3","status":"abandoned","reason":"abandoned","updated_at":"2026-07-21T17:28:19Z","provider":"codex"},"next_move":{"owner":"project","reason":"abandoned"},"condition":{"state":"blocked","reason":"Task LOO-195 worktree /Users/jack/src/loopflow.make-review-supervisors-observable-and is missing; restore that exact path on branch \"jack-heart/make-review-supervisors-observable-and\" before `lf task resume LOO-195`; Task identity and PR history are unchanged","observed_at":"2026-09-23T15:06:37.338845Z","evidence_age_secs":5521098,"local_progress":{"state":"missing","unsettled":true,"dirty":null,"authored_commits":null,"recovery_required":true,"reason":"Task LOO-195 worktree /Users/jack/src/loopflow.make-review-supervisors-observable-and is missing; restore that exact path on branch \"jack-heart/make-review-supervisors-observable-and\" before `lf task resume LOO-195`; Task identity and PR history are unchanged"}},"actions":{"recommended":"no_action","reason":"Task is terminal"},"active_pr":{"id":"pr_0cb77ba475334fe38d98adaa4ea31fef","sequence":1,"slug":"make-review-supervisors-observable-and","branch":"jack-heart/make-review-supervisors-observable-and","base_commit":"a7044e2b5bf64b195551c2d9398b434087e8fc72","phase":"working","empty":null,"publication":null,"merge_commit":null,"abandoned_at":null},"section":"later"},{"task":{"id":"22d37a5a-5900-4a14-b520-68b909e2d6ab","identifier":"LOO-196","name":"Delete Session and make Run the sole executor","description":"## Outcome\n\nFinish the one-way cut begun by PR #1073. Wave, Project, and Task execution all use the shared Work -> Epoch -> Run -> Launch contract. ProjectSession and TaskSession stop being controller identities; Run is the only execution authority and Launch is the only provider/process lifetime. Provider conversation continuity remains a Launch resume token, not a Loopflow Session aggregate.\n\n## Starting point\n\nBase the work on merged main at PR #1073 (`ae1344a57`). `docs/architecture.md` is the design ledger. Update its moment-of-transparency first so shipped child-priority behavior and this remaining bridge are stated exactly. Make ambitious cross-cutting passes; do not preserve two controller stacks as a compatibility layer.\n\n## Required cut\n\n* Route Project and Task reserve, advance, wait, stop, interrupt, recovery, reaping, and completion fencing through one shared Run execution path keyed by `WorkRef`. Domain flows and closure checks remain explicit typed dispatch, not factories or generic registries.\n* Keep stable Work and Epoch history across executor replacement. Run owns the exact opaque write lease. Launch owns PID/process group/tmux/provider route, containment, and optional resume token. Turn remains optional for opaque TUIs.\n* Delete `ProjectSessionStatus`, `TaskSessionStatus`, `ChildWriteLease`, body generations, legacy Session authority environment variables, Session successor/controller identity, mirrored Run transitions, duplicate Project/Task runners and stores, and their DTO/CLI/Swift/schema surfaces. Do not delete provider resume continuity or terminal attach presentation merely because a vendor calls it a session.\n* Make keeper recovery adopt or replace through Run/Launch evidence. Missing, stale, revoked, stopped, or foreign credentials fail closed; no ambient environment inference may become User authority. Interrupt targets the exact active Run/Launch and never falls back to Session lookup.\n* Derive Work status, waits, review attention, controls, liveness, usage, and monitoring from Work/Epoch/Run/Launch/Turn plus domain truth. Preserve Project and Wave child-first lanes: direct User input first, then oldest child Review, then background cadence without losing the playhead.\n* Preserve historical audit data only where it remains meaningful. Author the final one-way schema deletion as a draft migration under the release canonicalization contract; do not add a second registry or backwards-compatibility model.\n* Update docs, builtins, fixtures, and tests in the same pass. Remove stale Session language from public product concepts while retaining explicit provider terminology where it describes reality.\n\n## Behavior changes to prove\n\n* Starting, waking, steering, interrupting, stopping, recovering, and completing Project and Task Work touch one authoritative Run state machine. Races with new Steer input cannot lose work or commit stale completion.\n* A confirmed live Send records how delivery occurred but does not consume its Steer; a later Run/Turn Basis proves durable incorporation identically across Codex, Claude, OpenCode, and opaque tmux TUIs.\n* A dead or unreachable process cannot remain a writer. Reaping requires positive containment evidence; unknown side effects remain explicit and are never blindly retried.\n* A User-facing interactive review remains a live Launch even when the app is closed. Parent-agent reviews route through child attention and do not become a separate decision aggregate.\n* Recovery after process or host restart preserves Work, Epoch, provider continuity when available, worktree, PR, outstanding Steers, and exactly-once child attention without reconstructing controller identity from Handles.\n\n## Done when\n\n1. Production code has zero Project/Task Session-controller types, tables, leases, generations, runners, or authority env vars; focused searches document any surviving vendor/UI use of the word session.\n2. There is one Run reserve/advance/stop/recover path for Wave, Project, and Task, with typed Work dispatch only at domain behavior boundaries.\n3. Behavioral tests cover exact authority, stale completion, input-vs-stop races, seed-only/live steering portability, keeper adoption/reaping, opaque TUI execution, restart, and child-first responsiveness.\n4. Rust, migration, Python, Swift, UI compile, and E2E proofs pass; DTO fixtures remain lockstep with no defaults.\n5. `docs/architecture.md` describes current reality without a temporary Session bridge.\n6. Total repository source is at or below the documented 121,819-line ceiling, with deletion—not compatibility shims—accounting for the reduction.\n7. The PR receives exact-head architectural review, lands from current main, and the live Product Wave can launch, steer, interrupt, recover, and finish a real Task through Run with no Session-controller record.","rank":54,"completed":true,"assignee":null},"reference":{"issue_url":"https://linear.app/loopflow/issue/LOO-196/delete-session-and-make-run-the-sole-executor","workspace":{"slug":"delete-session-and-make-run","branch":"jack-heart/delete-session-and-make-run","worktree":"/Users/jack/src/loopflow.delete-session-and-make-run"}},"runtime":{"work_id":"task_9903f3b326db0b04cf40c024bceefd19","project_id":"proj_9f1fc19a84211aed8b8136e55c8ab1f3","routing_project_id":"proj_9f1fc19a84211aed8b8136e55c8ab1f3","status":"abandoned","reason":"abandoned","updated_at":"2026-07-21T17:28:19Z","provider":"claude"},"next_move":{"owner":"project","reason":"abandoned"},"condition":{"state":"blocked","reason":"Task LOO-196 worktree /Users/jack/src/loopflow.delete-session-and-make-run is missing; restore that exact path before `lf task resume LOO-196`; Task identity and PR history are unchanged","observed_at":"2026-09-23T15:06:37.345604Z","evidence_age_secs":5521098,"local_progress":{"state":"missing","unsettled":true,"dirty":null,"authored_commits":null,"recovery_required":true,"reason":"Task LOO-196 worktree /Users/jack/src/loopflow.delete-session-and-make-run is missing; restore that exact path before `lf task resume LOO-196`; Task identity and PR history are unchanged"}},"actions":{"recommended":"no_action","reason":"Task is terminal"},"active_pr":null,"section":"later"}]}],"truncated":false},"unavailable_projects":[]}]}
